hadiths[1002]{hadithnumber,text}:
"37075","(37075) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim Abi Al-Nadr: A man asked Muhammad bin Sirin: What do you say in your gatherings? These are the storytellers. He said: I do not command you to do it, nor forbid you from it. Storytelling is something newly invented. This creation is more recent than the Kharijites."
"37076","(37076) Mu’tamir told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, that when God created Adam, He created his eyes before the rest of his body, and he said: O Lord, complete the rest of my creation before the setting of the sun, so God revealed: {And man is hasty}"
"37077","(37077) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abu Malik, who said: The first verse to be revealed from Bara’iyya {Go forth in lightness. And heavy}"
"37078","(37078) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b, who said: God created souls before He created them. bodies, so He took their covenant."
"37079","(37079) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, he said: The first thing that begins with before Ablution is washing the hands."
"37080","(37080) Al-Fadl narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr said: The first thing that is rewarded for Islam as a vessel is rewarded is what people say about fate."
"37081","(37081) Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The people of prayer and the Hisba are among the muezzins, the first to He will be clothed on the Day of Resurrection."
"37082","(37082) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymiy, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, which mosque was placed first on earth? He said: The Sacred Mosque. I said: Then what? He said: Al-Aqsa Mosque. It means the Holy House."
"37083","(37083) Yazid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Abu Amr, on the authority of Ubaid bin Al-Khashshash, on the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: I entered upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was in the mosque. I said: Which of the prophets came first? He said: Adam. He said: I said: Bye. Was he a prophet? He said: Yes, a prophet who speaks."
"37084","(37084) Qubaisa narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hammam, who said: The first mux that existed on earth An old woman went out with some flour for her in a bag, and a strong wind came and scattered it. So Solomon said: Look who rode the sea. With this smell, they fined him."
"37085","(37085) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Malik bin Ayman, he said: The first to grow old. Abraham, peace and blessings be upon him, said: What is this? He said: Honor and forbearance."
"37086","(37086) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr ibn Qays, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, he said: Ibrahim was the first to be clothed with two cloaks, then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was clothed with a robe while he was on the verge of The right hand of the throne.\n(Ahmad 101, Abu Ali 562)"
"37087","(37087) Qubaysah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Mughiriya bin Al-Nu’man, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The first of the creatures to be clothed at that time was Abraham."
"37088","(37088) Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Waqid narrated to us, Zuhair narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, he said: It was said to Qutham: How did Ali inherit the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, instead of you? He said: By God, he was the first of us to catch up with him and the strongest of us with him. Sticky"
"37089","(37089) Muhammad bin Bishr Al-Abdi narrated to us, Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he said in his hadith: But go to Noah, for he was the first messenger sent to the earth."
"37090","(37090) Ibn Bishr narrated to us, Abu Hayyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Zur’i, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Peace be upon him, in a hadith he mentioned, he said: Then they would come to Adam, and he would say: Go to Noah, and they would say: O Noah, you are the first of the messengers. To the people of the earth."
"37091","(37091) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, who said: The first man to draw a sword in God’s name Al-Zubayr"
"37092","(37092) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Mas`ar, on the authority of Simak al-Hanafi, who said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: When the beginning of al-Muzzammil was revealed They were standing in a manner similar to how they stand during the month of Ramadan, and there was a year between the beginning and the end of it. (Ibn Jarir 29)"
"37093","(37093) Affan narrated to us, Ali bin Masadhi narrated to us, Ibrahim bin Al-Ala’ al-Ghanawi narrated to us, he said: We have been informed that Ka'b used to say: The first of the cities was devastation on its wings. We said: What are its wings, O Ka'b? He said: Basra and Egypt."
"37094","(37094) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Yusuf bin Mihran, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The first to deny Adam."
"37095","(37095) Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The first to be appointed successor in the matter of division was Omar ibn al-Khattab."
"37096","(37096) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Ubaid and Muhammad bin Qays, on the authority of Ali bin Rabi’a, he said, the first to Qarza bin Kaab wailed for him in Kufa."
"37097","(37097) Zaid told us, Ibn Abi Khalid told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Rashid, on the authority of a woman from the Ansar who was called Asma bint Yazeed bin Al-Sakan, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Umm Saad: Don’t your tears stop and go away Your sadness, for your son was the first at whom God laughed and for whom the throne shook."
"37098","(37098) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Mugheerah bin Al-Nu’man, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose among us and said: The first of creation will be clothed by Abraham. (Ibn Abi Asim 11)"
"37099","(37099) Ali bin Ubaid told us, he said: Ibn Abi Khaled told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, he said: The people will be gathered Barefoot and naked, the first to be met with the garment of Abraham, peace be upon him."
"37100","(37100) Waki’ and Abu Usama narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Khalid, who said: I heard Abu Amr Al-Shaybani say: It was Maran is the beginning of the year and Qadisiyah is the end of the year."
"37101","(37101) Shababah told us, on the authority of Warqa’, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, {As We initiated the first creation, We will return it} He said: barefoot naked"
"37102","(37102) And with its chain of transmission, on the authority of Mujahid {in the first pages}, he said: The Torah and the Gospel."
"37103","(37103) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Yazid Al-Farisi, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Uthman: The Anfals were among The first of what was revealed in Medina, and it was innocent of the last of what was revealed of the Qur’an."
"37104","(37104) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, Qais narrated to us, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Abu Sadiq, on the authority of Alim, On the authority of Salman, he said: The first of this nation to welcome its Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, the first of it to Islam was Ali bin Ubayy. Student"
"37105","(37105) Waki` narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, that Abu Bakr sought help from someone suffering from distress. So he encouraged him and said: I have never sought the advice of anyone before you in Islam."
"37106","(37106) Shababi told us, on the authority of Warqa’, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid {in the first pages} who said: The Torah and the Gospel."
"37107","(37107) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, he heard Abu Salamah say regarding expiation for swearing an oath: extend with the first mudd."
"37108","(37108) Qutayba narrated to us, Laith narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Salam, that he said in a hadith mentioned by him: Then Adam denied, so his descendants denied, and that was the first day on which he was commanded to be martyrs."
"37109","(37109) Surayj bin Al-Nu’man narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz bin Abi Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Salih bin Kaysan, he said: He informed us Al-Raqashī, on the authority of Anas, said: The angels met Adam as he was circumambulating the Kaaba, and said: O Adam, you have performed Hajj, and he said: Yes, They said: We performed Hajj two thousand years before you."
"37110","(37110) Zaid told us, Qais told us, he said: I saw Shimr bin Atiyya borrowed a turban and brought him his own. Sabriyah returned it and said: I saw that the first time people saw Sabriyah they rose up to him and burned him."
"37111","(37111) Yazeed told us, Yahya bin Al-Mutawakkil Abu Aqeel told us, he said: Ismail bin Rafi’ told us, on the authority of Ibn By Abu Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, that she said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: If it was for one of the first that God forbade him And He made a covenant with me after worshiping idols and drinking wine: and the companions of men."
"37112","(37112) Husayn narrated to us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Ibrahim: The first to pronounce (In the Name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful) The Bedouins"
"37113","(37113) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: The most recent people among the people are standing in Ramadan and praying the noon prayer. And Qunoot at dawn and Qasas."
"37114","(37114) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: People do not have an Eid except at the beginning of the day."
"37115","(37115) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abbas bin Abdul Rahman Al-Hashimi, who said: The first time mosques were created was that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw dirt on the forehead and rubbed it, then he ordered the creation to be smeared with it on its place. So people created mosques."
"37116","(37116) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Hafsa, on the authority of Abu Jamra, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The first plural. It was gathered together in Medina, then it was gathered in Bahrain. (Bukhari 892)"
"37117","(37117) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Ziyad bin Alaqi, on the authority of Saad, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He handed over the authority of Abdullah bin Jahsh, and he was the first prince to be given authority in Islam. (Bazzar 1757)"
"37118","(37118) Zaid told us, Sufyan bin Hussein told us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Anas bin Hakim Al-Dhabi, he said: Abu Hurairah said to me: When you go to the people of Egypt, tell them that you heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He says: The first thing a servant will be held accountable for on the Day of Resurrection is the obligatory prayer. (Ibn Majah 1425. Ahmed 290)"
"37119","(37119) Yazeed told us, Al-Dastawwi told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Amir Al-Uqaili, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The first three of your nation were presented to me. They will enter Paradise, and the first three to enter Hell. As for the first three to enter Paradise, the witness and Abd A slave who was not distracted by the slavery of this world from obeying his Lord, and a poor and chaste person with dependents. As for the first of the three to enter Hell, So he is an authoritative prince, someone who has a wealth of money that does not fulfill God’s rights regarding his wealth, and a poor and proud person."
"37120","(37120) Ibn Bishr narrated to us, Abu Hayyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Zur’a, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: I have memorized from The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a hadith that I have not yet forgotten. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: The first of the verses Coming out: The rising of the sun from the west, or the emergence of an animal upon the people in the morning, then whatever it was before its companion, then upon the latter. He affected her soon. (Muslim 2260, Ahmad 164)"
"37121","(37121) Hatem narrated to us, Ja’far bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The first usury to be lost is the interest of Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Muttalib."
"37122","(37122) Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Sadiqah bin Yasar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, praised God and praised him for what he deserved, then he said: O people, all the blood was in The Jahiliyya is a wasteland, and the first of your blood was the blood of Iyas bin Rabi’ah bin Al-Harith, who was a breastfeeding woman in Banu Layth. So Hudhail killed him, and the first usurer in pre-Islamic times was Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib, and he was the first usurer to give up. {Yours is yours. You shall not wrong or be wronged.} (Abdullah bin Hamid 858, Bazar 1141)"
"37123","(37123) Yazeed told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, that Ali said: The beginning of ablution is rinsing the mouth and nose."
"37124","(37124) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: I think that selling should be abandoned at the first call to prayer. Narrated by Othman, may God be pleased with him."
"37125","(37125) Waki’ narrated to us, Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: God Almighty began by creating the heavens. On Sunday, then Sunday, Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, and Friday, and He made each day a thousand years."
"37126","(37126) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murra, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: No soul is killed unjustly except that the first son of Adam owes a measure of its blood, because he was the first to The age of killing"
"37127","(37127) Many narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far, on the authority of Maymun, when these verses were revealed: {And those who slander chaste women and then do not “Bring four witnesses, so flog them with eighty lashes, and never accept any witness from them.” A man said: If a man sees His family did not like it, so he went and collected four. The man had finished his need, and if he mentioned that, he would be flogged, and it would not be accepted for him. Shahadah, and he was one of the transgressors, so the verses of curses were revealed, and that man was the first to be tested. He said what he said. With this, the cursed verses were revealed."
"37128","(37128) Sahl narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The first to die was Adam."
"37129","(37129) Wakī’ narrated to us, Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was Al-Abtah descends first."
"37130","(37130) Ibn Mushir narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of Fatima, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He said to her: You are the first of my family to join me. She laughed at that."
"37131","(37131) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah did not recite Qunoot at dawn, and the first Whoever recites it is against Ali, and they think that he only did that because he was a warrior."
"37132","(37132) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Fazari, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, who said: The Iqama is the beginning of the prayer."
"37133","(37133) A sheikh of ours narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: The first person to give a handful of wheat in the zakat of the fitr was fair. A saa of dates from Othman bin Affan."
"37134","(37134) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I am the master of the children of Adam. And the first for whom the earth will open, and the first to intercede."
"37135","(37135) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: I was informed that the first kid was fed with her son. Father's mother"
"37136","(37136) Al-Samimi narrated to us, Humaid narrated to us, he said: I asked Al-Hasan: Who was the first to deliver the sermon before the prayer, and he said: Othman bin Affan led the people in prayer, then he addressed them, and he saw many people who did not understand the prayer, so they did so."
"37137","(37137) Zaid and Al-Samimi told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: The first The signs of the Hour are a fire that will gather people from the east to the west, and as for the first food that the people of Paradise will eat, it will increase. Whale liver."
"37138","(37138) Ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr narrated to us, Abd al-Jalil bin Atiyya narrated to us, he raised it, he said the first thing The servant is asked about him, about his prayer."
"37139","(37139) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: Qunut in the month of Ramadan. He said: Omar is the first to You said: I said: The other half altogether. He said: Yes."
"37140","(37140) Ibn Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Iyad ibn Dinar, the client of Laith, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, I heard him say: He said: Abu Al-Qasim, may God bless him and grant him peace: The first of my group to enter Paradise from my nation will be in the form of the moon on the night of the full moon, then the next. Follow her on the brightest star in the sky. (Ahmed 257)"
"37141","(37141) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of Fatima, that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said to her: You are the first of my family to join me, and what an excellent predecessor I am to you. (Muslim 1905. Ibn Majah 1621)"
"37142","(37142) Muhammad bin Musab narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Aisha, she said: God’s obligation The first obligatory prayer was two rak'ahs, then he completed them for the present one, and the traveling prayer was approved as the first obligatory rak'ah."
"37143","(37143) Ibn Mus’ab narrated to us, he said: Al-Awza’i narrated to me, he said: I asked Al-Zuhri about the witnesses of the young men, and he said: It was Marwan bin Al-Hakam was the first to rule that."
"37144","(37144) Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: It has informed me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The feast on the first day is true, the second is good, and the third is hypocrisy."
"37145","(37145) Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: He was the first to introduce the call to prayer for breaking the fast. And Al-Adha are Banu Marwan."
"37146","(37146) I found in my book, on the authority of Suwayd bin Amr, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Qays bin Saad, on the authority of Tawus, he said: The first to dress at dawn was Bilal at the time of Abu Bakr. Whenever he said: Hail Ali al-Falah, he would say: Prayer is better than sleep. Twice"
"37147","(37147) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Amara bin Al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah;"
"37148","(37148) And Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And peace be upon him. He said: The first group of my nation to enter Paradise will be on the shape of the moon on the night of the full moon, then those who will be colored on the brightest. A shining star in the sky."
"37149","(37149) Al-Fadl narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Ja’far narrated to us, on the authority of his father, that he used to like to recite The two rak'ahs are first introduced: {Say, O disbelievers} and {Say: He is God, One} in tawaf."
"37150","(37150) Aswad narrated to us, Ja’far bin Ziyad narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Hassan, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: The first to ask about The clear evidence is clear. They said: O Abu Umayyah, she narrated it. He said: You narrated it, so I narrated it."
"37151","(37151) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The first to God’s friend Abraham, peace and blessings be upon him, is clothed."
"37152","(37152) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Muti’, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, who said: Omar said: May God curse so-and-so, for he was the first to Permission to sell alcohol."
"37153","(37153) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Abu Al-Za’ra’, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: Then God permits intercession, so the first intercessor on the Day of Resurrection will be the Holy Spirit Gabriel, then Abraham, the Most Merciful’s friend. Then Moses, peace be upon them both, then your Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, will rise. Fourthly, no one will intercede after him for what he intercedes for. And it is the praised place. (Taalisi 389)"
"37154","(37154) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The first to circumambulate the Kaaba The angels"
"37155","(37155) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The first thing that God created was Something is the pen, then He created the Nun, and pressed the earth on the back of the Nun."
"37156","(37156) Ubaidah narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The first time prayer was made obligatory, it was made obligatory. Two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs. When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Medina, he added two rak'ahs for every two rak'ahs except Morocco"
"37157","(37157) Al-Fadl narrated to us, Hashraj bin Nabatiyah narrated to us, he said: Sa’id bin Jumhan narrated to me, I said to Saffina, that his son The Umayyads claim that the dispute is among them. He said: The Banu al-Zarqa’i lied. Rather, they were kings who were among the strongest of kings, and the first of the kings. Muawiyah (Tirmidhi 2226)"
"37158","(37158) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Omar bargained with a man for a horse, so he rode it and it became damaged. So he said to the man: Take your horse. The man said: No. Omar said: Make an arbitrator between you and me. The man said: Shurayh, so they disputed. To him, and Shurayh said: O Commander of the Faithful, take what you bought, or return as you took. Omar said: And the judgment is only upon So he took him to Kufa and sent him as a judge, for it was the first day he knew him."
"37159","(37159) Abu Asama told us, Sufyan told us, he said: Wasil Al-Ahdab told me, he said: Aidhidha told me, a woman. From Banu Asad, and he praised her well. She said: I heard Abdullah bin Masoud having intercourse with men and women, meaning O people, whoever overtakes you, whether a woman or a man, then the first zenith, the first zenith, for today we are On the Fitrah."
"37160","(37160) Affan told us, Hammad told us, he said: Al-Azraq bin Qays told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Yamar, on the authority of a man from Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The first thing a servant will be held accountable for on the Day of When he performed his prayer, if he had completed it, it would be recorded as complete, and if it was not complete, he said: Look, will you find it? My servant has some voluntary acts, so complete him with what he neglected of his obligatory prayers, then zakat, then the deeds will be taken according to that. (Ahmed 65)"
"37161","(37161) Abd al-Rahim and Issa told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Anas, who said: The first plunder of a fifth in Islam. The robbery of Al-Bara' bin Malik."
"37162","(37162) Affan told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Abu Tufayl, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: The first to The people of Mecca emerge from Mecca: the monkey."
"37163","(37163) Wakī’ narrated to us, Ubayd Allah bin Abi Ziyad narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Tufayl Aamir bin Watheli: I asked Ibn Abbas, about the journey between Safa and Marwa, and he said: The first one to do it was Abraham, peace be upon him."
"37164","(37164) Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, Issa bin Al-Mukhtar narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Layla, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, that he said: The first group to enter Paradise are those who praise God in good and bad times.\n(Hakim 502. Tabarani 288)"
"37165","(37165) Aswad narrated to us, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Abu Hurr Al-Raqqashi, on the authority of his uncle, who said: I was taking the reins of the camel of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the middle of the days of the East, defending the people from her. He said: O people, all wealth and influences of the pre-Islamic era were under the feet of these people until the Day of Resurrection. The first interest to be paid is the blood of Rabi’ah bin Al-Harith bin Abdul Muttalib, and God has decreed that the first usury to be paid is the usury of Al-Abbas. Ibn Abd al-Muttalib {You shall have your capital. You shall not wrong or be wronged}"
"37166","(37166) Abu Asama narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd, on the authority of Abu Nadrah, he said: He addressed us. Ibn Abbas in Basra, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I am the first one from whom the earth will open, and he is not proud.\n(Ahmad 281, Abu Ali 2322)"
"37167","(37167) Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Omar was the first person to fall on his knees to the ground."
"37168","(37168) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr: {Man was created from a calf} He said: Adam, peace and blessings be upon him, was created, then the spirit was breathed into him, and the first thing that was blown into was his knees, so he went and got up, and said: {Man was created from Hurry}"
"37169","(37169) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, Zuhair narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Ibn Masoud: The first surah The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited it to the people: (and the star)"
"37170","(37170) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid: It was said: Patience at the first shock."
"37171","(37171) Zaid told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The first person to know about insight was Ibn Abbas."
"37172","(37172) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hunaidah ibn Khalid Al-Khuza’i, who said: The first head was given as a sacrifice in Islam is the head of Amr bin Al-Hamq, given to Muawiyah."
"37173","(37173) Al-Fadl narrated to us, Abu Isra’il narrated to us, he said: Some of our companions told me that Talhahi was the first to pledge allegiance. Ali, and a Bedouin saw him and said: A matter that cannot be completed, so I said to Abu Israel: From what, he said: From the command of his hand."
"37174","(37174) Ishaq ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, he said: A sheikh narrated to me, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, he said: The first to The police were set by Amr ibn Al-Aas, and when he fell ill during which he died, he sent for his police and said: Take your weapons and your armor. And come to me. When he came to him, he said, “I was only preparing for you a day like this. Will you be able to turn away from me?” Something of what I am in. They said: Glory be to God. You say this, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was seeking your advice. And he will command you in charge of the armies, and he said: How would you know that perhaps the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was getting acquainted with me? With that"
"37175","(37175) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Talha ibn Amr, who said: I heard Ata’ saying: When the prohibition of alcohol was first revealed: {They ask you about wine and gambling. Say, “In them is a great sin, but there are benefits for the people.”}"
"37176","(37176) Khalid bin Mukhlid told us, he said: Muhammad Musa told me, he said: Muhammad bin Amr bin Ali told me, on the authority of Ali bin Abu Talib, he said: The first to be buried in Al-Baqi’ was Othman bin Mazun, then he was followed by Ibrahim bin Muhammad, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he greeted you."
"37177","(37177) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, who said: Abdullah said: If you see the event So you should do the first thing."
"37178","(37178) Malik told us, he said: Sa’l bin Shuaib told me, he said: Firas bin Yahya told me, he said: You are correct in Al-Hajjaj imprisoned a piece of paper dotted with grammar, and it was the first dot I saw, so I brought it to Al-Sha’abi and showed it to him, and he said: Read it to him, and do not punctuate it with your hand."
"37179","(37179) Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, Muhammad bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, and Ibn Abi Najih They said: The first to enact the prayer upon killing was Khubayb bin Adiyy."
"37180","(37180) Zaid narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: The first person to declare Islam was his brother, So he left her, so she went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she informed him, so he sent for him and the Qur’an was revealed: {God has certainly heard the saying of The one who argues with you about her husband."
"37181","(37181) Zaid Abu Shayba told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: The first person to know about Kufa was Ibn Al-Zubayr."
"37182","(37182) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Shabib, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that Omar wrote a servant to him. He was called Abu Umayyah, and he was surprised by his star when he arrived. Ikrimah said: He was the first star to perform in Islam."
"37183","(37183) Zaid told us, Abu Al-Fadl Khalid bin Rabah told us, Abu Sawwar Al-Adawi told us, on the authority of Jundub bin Abd. God said: The first thing that stinks from the son of Adam is his stomach. When he dies, do not put anything in it except perfume."
"37184","(37184) Zaid told us, Ibn Ishaq told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Marthad bin Abdullah. Al-Yazani was the first of the people of Egypt to go to the mosque, and he would not bring anything without giving it in charity."
"37185","(37185) Abu Al-Qasim Muslimah bin Al-Qasim narrated to us, Abu Al-Hasan Yaqoub bin Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Zaid narrated to us. Ibn Hajar al-Qurashi al-Asqalani in Ashkelon, he said: Abu al-Fadl Salih ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he narrated to us Ibrahim bin Mahdi Al-Masaysi, Abu Hafs Omar bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Abar told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Azdi, on the authority of Abu Burda ibn Abi Musa, on the authority of Abu Musa, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The first to He entered the bathroom and the light was made for him, Suleiman bin Dawud, peace be upon him. When he entered it and found that he was hot and faint, he said: He has taken refuge from God's punishment is a punishment for him before there is no punishment for him. (Tabarani 464)"
"37186","(37186) Muslim narrated to us, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Jahm narrated to us in Baghdad, Abdullah bin Ahmad narrated to us. Ibn Muhammad Ibn Hanbal, he said: My father told me, Hajjaj told us, he said: I heard Abu Israel, he said: The first day I knew about it. Al-Hakam on the day Al-Sha’abi perished. He said: A person came to ask about a matter, and they said: You should go to Al-Hakam bin Utaiba."
"37187","(37187) My father told us, Sufyan told us, Ayoub said: The first time we sat with him, meaning Ikrimah, Hassan said. Your good deeds are like this."
"37188","(37188) My father told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, he said: The first woman The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, married her to Khadija bint Khuwalid, then he married Soudah bint Zam’iya, then he married Aisha bint Abi Bakr in Mecca, and he consummated his marriage with her in Medina, then he married Zainab bint Khuzaymah in Medina. Al-Hilaliyah, then he married Umm Salamah bint Abi Umayyah, then he married Juwayriyah bint Al-Harith from Banu Al-Mustaliq. And she was among those whom God had bestowed upon him. Then he married Maimunah bint Al-Harith, who gave herself to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him. Then he had sex with Safiyya bint Huyya, and that was among the things that God had bestowed upon her on the Day of Khaybar. Then he had sex with Zainab bint Jahsh, and his wife was Zayd bin Harithah. Zainab bint Khuzaymah died before the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He married Hafsa bint Umar, Umm Habibah bint Abi Sufyan, Al-Kindiyya, and a woman from Kalb, and they were all Whoever marries fourteen women."
"37189","(37189) Muslimah, Yaqoub bin Ishaq bin Hujr told us, Abu Musa told us, Damrah told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Yazeed, on the authority of a man whom he named, who said: The first one to make the allegiance was Ibrahim Khalil al-Rahman, peace be upon him. He was informed that a people They raided Lot and took him captive, so he gathered a group and marched towards them with his servants and masters until he overtook them and rescued him. And his family."
"37190","(37190) Muslimah: Abu Ja`far Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Ma’afiri narrated to us. Al-Masri, known as Ibn Hamawiyah, as Al-Fustat in Al-Jami’, based on dictation from his book in Dhul-Qa’diyah, two years old. And twenty-three hundred. He said: Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman Al-Muradi told us, Asad bin Musa told us, Hammad bin Salma told us, on the authority of Abu Qaz’a, on the authority of Hakim bin Mu’awiya, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: You will be gathered on foot. And as riders and on your faces, you will present to God the ransom of your mouths, and the first thing to be expressed, from one of you: His thigh\n(Tabarani 1036)"
"37191","(37191) Muslimah informed us, Abu Ja’far Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Hamdani informed us, Abu Bakr Yahya ibn Ja’far informed us. Ibn Abi Talib, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata’ al-Ajli al-Khuffaff told us, Sa’id and Hisham told us about his leaders, he said: Abu al-Darda’ used to say: The first thing I will dispute about tomorrow, meaning the Day of Resurrection, is that it will be said to me: O Abu al-Darda’. You knew, so how did you act on what you knew?!"
"37192","(37192) Muslimah narrated to us, Abu Ali Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abi Raja’ al-Zayat al-Maliki narrated to us in Mecca, with dictation from He preserved it. Abu Harithah Ahmad bin Ibrahim Al-Ghassani told us about Ramla in the year two hundred and seventy-seven. My father told us On the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of a man from the army of Muslim ibn Uqba, who said: When I settled in Medina, I entered the mosque of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. I prayed next to Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan, and Abd al-Malik said to me: Security from this army. You, he said: I said: Yes, he said: Your mother has bereaved you. Do you know whom to go to? The first child born in Islam, and the son of To the disciples of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and to Ibn Asma’ of the same two scopes, and to those whom the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace in His hand. By God, if you come to him during the day, you will find him fasting, and if you come to him at night, you will find him standing. If the people of the earth had decided to kill him, God would have thrown them all into Hell on their faces. That man said: She had not passed until A few days until the caliphate came to Abd al-Malik, and he directed us to him and we killed him."
"37193","(37193) Abu Haritha told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: The first to be named Abdul Malik And Abd al-Aziz: Abd al-Malik, and Abd al-Aziz, son of Marwan, and the first to continue prayer between noon and afternoon prayers. And between the evening and the evening prayers, Abdul-Malik"
"37194","(37194) Muslimah, he said: I read to Abu Abbas Ahmad bin Issa, known as Ibn Al-Washay. Abu Ja’far told you. Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Fayrouz Al-Baghdadi, the righteous servant, said: Ali bin Khashram narrated to us, saying: Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Rabi’a bin Uthman, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of his father, that he said: The first to deliver a sermon on the pulpit was Ibrahim Khalil The Most Gracious, peace and blessings be upon him."
"37195","(37195) Muslimah narrated to us, Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Hamdani narrated to us, Ja`far ibn Ahmad al-Hamdani narrated to us. Abdul Rahman bin Ahmad Al-Zuhri narrated to us, Kathir bin Hisham narrated to us, Issa bin Ibrahim narrated to us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Abdullah, he said: I heard Ka’b say: The first person to multiply the dinar and the dirham was Adam, peace be upon him, and he said: A living is not suitable unless With what"
"37196","(37196) Ibn Al-Washā’ī narrated to us, Abu Uthman Sa’id bin Al-Hakam Al-Sulami Al-Dimashqī narrated to us, known as Al-Fundaqī. I read from Literally speaking, Hisham bin Khalid told us, Baqiyya told us, Al-Ala bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Al-Farwi, on the authority of Abu Dharr. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The first to enter Paradise is the honest merchant."
"37197","(37197) Ibn Al-Washa’ told us, Sa’id bin Al-Hakam told us, Hisham told us, Baqiya told us, Ibn Juraij told us, On the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, a similar narration."
"37198","(37198) Ibn Al-Washā’ī narrated to us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Muslim bin Ziyad, a client of Banu Hashim, narrated to us. Muhammad bin Amr bin Bakr narrated to us, saying: Yahya bin Al-Dharais narrated to me, Amr narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of Salman, he said: The blessed and pure Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told me: The first thing a believer is given good tidings of is the spirit of And basil and a garden of bliss, and the first thing a believer is given good tidings of is said to him: Give good tidings to God’s friend. You have given the best advance. He forgives. May God bless those who follow you. Sheikh Muhammad bin Ibrahim Abu Abdullah said: No one narrated this hadith except this one sheikh. And God responds to whoever asks for your forgiveness, and accepts whoever bears witness against you."
"37199","(37199) Muslima informed us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Makki al-Baghdadi told us, with al-Qalzum, he said: My father, may God have mercy on him, narrated to me, he said: My father Muhammad bin Yuss narrated to us, and he said: Abu Dawud Sulaiman bin Amr Al-Nakha’i narrated to us, he narrated to us Saeed bin Iyas, on the authority of Alqamah, Abdullah bin Abbas said: The first one to adopt the dog was Noah. He said: O Lord, You have commanded me to I make the ark, and I make it for days, but they come to me at night and spoil everything I have done. They spoil it, so I die. I will fulfill what you have commanded me to do. My matter has been prolonged for me, so God revealed to him: O Noah, take a dog to guard you. So Noah took a dog, and he worked during the day and slept at night, when his people came to him to spoil what he had done. The dog barks at them, and Noah notices it, so he takes the spear to them and jumps on them, and they flee from him, so he completes it. He has whatever he wants."
"37200","(37200) Muslimah informed us, Abu Ali Al-Hasan bin Mansour Al-Baghdadi informed us, Abu Salama, meaning Ibn Ismail Al-Manqari narrated to us: Aban, meaning Ibn Yazid Al-Attar, told us: His leaders informed us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Anas bin Hakim, on the authority of Abu Huraira, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The first thing a servant will be held accountable for on the Day of He will be judged by his prayers. If they are good, he will be successful and prosperous, and if they are bad, then he will be disappointed and lose."
"37201","(37201) Muslimah told us, Ibn Al-Washa’ told us, Bakkar bin Qutaybah Al-Qadi told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us. Al-Qaisi narrated to us, Shu’abi, on the authority of Asim Al-Ahwal, who said: I heard Abu Uthman Al-Nahdi saying: I heard Saad bin Malik and Abu Tomorrow they will say: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Whoever calls someone to someone other than his father while he knows, Because he is different from his father, heaven is forbidden for him.\n He said: Saad bin Malik was the first to throw an arrow in the path of God Almighty.\n He said: Abu Bakra was the first to seek protection from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the delegation of Thaqif."
"37202","(37202) Sharik bin Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Jabir bin Samurah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, stoned a Jew and a Jewish woman."
"37203","(37203) Abu Muawiyah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murra, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Azib; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stoned a Jew."
"37204","(37204) Abdul Rahim bin Suleiman told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Amer, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, stoned a Jew and a Jewish woman."
"37205","(37205) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ubaidullah narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, stoned two Jews. I am among those who stoned them."
"37206","(37206) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, stoned a Jew and a Jewish woman.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: They are not required to stone them."
"37207","(37207) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Aazib said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Should I pray in the sheep pens? He said: Yes, he said: Should I perform ablution from its meat? He said: No, he said: So should I pray in the blessing of camels? He said: No, he said: Should I perform ablution from its meat? He said: Yes."
"37208","(37208) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Mughaffal, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Pray in sheep’s pens, and do not pray in camels’ stalls, for they were created from Satan."
"37209","(37209) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Ash’ath ibn Abi Ash-Sha’tha’i, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Abi Thawr, On the authority of Jabir bin Samra, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us to perform ablution with camel meat, and not to perform ablution with camel meat. Sheep, and we should pray in the fat of sheep, and not pray in the fowl of camels."
"37210","(37210) Zaid told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah; On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: If you find nothing but sheep pens and camel pens, then pray in sheep pens, and do not Pray in the backs of camels."
"37211","(37211) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn al-Rabi’ ibn Sabra, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He should not pray in camels’ backs.\n It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: There is no harm in that."
"37212","(37212) Ibn Numayr and Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace; He apportioned two shares to the horse and two shares to the man."
"37213","(37213) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhoul; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave the horseman three shares: two shares for his horse, and one share for himself."
"37214","(37214) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Usama bin Zayd, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace On the Day of Khaybar, the horse will have two arrows, and the man will have two arrows."
"37215","(37215) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Saleh, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave the horseman three shares: one for himself, and two for his horse."
"37216","(37216) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Salih bin Kaysan; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, contributed two hundred horses on the Day of Khaybar, each horse receiving two shares.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: An arrow is for the horse, and an arrow is for its owner."
"37217","(37217) Ibn Numayr and Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade traveling with the Qur’an to the land of the enemy, for fear that the enemy would get to him.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: There is no harm in that. (Ahmad 55. Malik 7)"
"37218","(37218) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Hamid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Numan, on the authority of His father; That his father gave him honey as a boy, and that he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to testify and said: Your son ate your honey. Like this? He said: No, he said: So return it."
"37219","(37219) Abbad narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: I heard Al-Nu’man bin Bashir say: My father gave me Atiya, and my mother Amr bint Rawahiya said: I will not be satisfied until you bear witness to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: So he came to the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: I gave my son a gift from his lifetime, so you commanded me to appoint you to witness. He said: I gave Are all your children like this? He said: No. He said: So fear God, and be just among your children."
"37220","(37220) Ibn Mushir narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Bashir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: I do not bear witness to injustice.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: There is no harm in it."
"37221","(37221) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, he heard Jabir say: A man from the Ansar arranged a servant for him, but he was not there. He had other money, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sold it, and Al-Nahham bought it for a Coptic slave who died in the first year of his emirate. Ibn Al-Zubayr."
"37222","(37222) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Salama, on the authority of Ata’, and Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sold the money while turning his back.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: It will not be sold."
"37223","(37223) Hafs and Ibn Mushir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed. May peace and blessings be upon him on his grave after he was buried."
"37224","(37224) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Hakim, on the authority of Kharijiyah ibn Zayd, on the authority of his paternal uncle Yazid ibn Thabit, He was older than Zaid. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed for a woman after she was buried, so he prayed for her four times."
"37225","(37225) Sa`id bin Yahya al-Himyari narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Husayn, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Umamiya bin Sahl, on the authority of his father, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to visit the poor people of Medina, and he would witness Their funerals when they die. He said: Then a woman from among the people of Awali died. He said: Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, walked to He buried her and said “Allahu Akbar” four times."
"37226","(37226) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, on the authority of Abu Al-Muhallab, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: A brother of yours has died, so pray for him, meaning the Negus."
"37227","(37227) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed for the Negus, and he recited the “Allahu Akbar” four times."
"37228","(37228) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibn Abbas ; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed over the dead after he was buried."
"37229","(37229) Zaid bin Harun told us, Sulaym bin Hayyan told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Mina, on the authority of Jabir; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed for his companions, and said the “Allahu Akbar” for him four times.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: The funeral prayer is not performed twice over a dead person."
"37230","(37230) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Hassan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, felt his hair in his right hand, and blood was drawn from his hand."
"37231","(37231) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Al-Miswar bin Makhramah, and Marwan; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out in the year of Al-Hudaybiyyah with some fifteen hundred of his companions. The confederate imitated the hadith, combed it, and entered ihram."
"37232","(37232) Hammad bin Khaled told us, on the authority of Aflah, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, Ash’ar.\nIt was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: Notice is a proverb."
"37233","(37233) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Hilal bin Yassaf, who said: He took Ziyad bin Abi Al-Ja’d by the hand. So he brought me to a sheikh who was known as Al-Ruqyah, and it was said to him: And Bassa bin Ma’abad, who said: A man prayed behind the row alone, so the Prophet ordered him to do so. May God bless him and grant him peace."
"37234","(37234) Mulazim bin Amr narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Badr, he said: Abdul Rahman bin Ali bin Shayban narrated to me, on the authority of His father, Ali bin Shayban, who was part of the delegation, said: We went out until we came to the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So we pledged allegiance to him and we prayed behind him, and he saw a man praying behind the row. He said: Then the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, stood over him. Until he left and said: Continue your prayer, for there is no prayer for the one behind the row.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: His prayer is sufficient."
"37235","(37235) Abduh narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed between a man and his wife, and said: Perhaps you will bring him black and frizzy. So she came. It is black and frizzy."
"37236","(37236) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abbad bin Mansour, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed pregnancy. (Ahmed 355)"
"37237","(37237) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; Concerning a man who disavowed what was in his wife’s womb, he said: Curse her.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa did not consider the curse to be pregnant."
"37238","(37238) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, on the authority of Abu Al-Muhallab, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn; That a man had six slaves, so he freed them upon his death, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, cast lots among them. So he freed two, and enslaved four."
"37239","(37239) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Mukhtar, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ziyad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, something like it, or something similar to it.\n - It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: This is nothing, and he does not consider it a lot."
"37240","(37240) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Zayd bin Khalid, and Shibl And Abu Hurairah, they said: We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a man came to him and asked him about the mother who had committed adultery before. To fortify? He said: Flog her, and if she returns, flog her. On the third or fourth, he said: Then sell her, even if it is with a braid."
"37241","(37241) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Abu Jamil, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Establish limits on what your right hands possess."
"37242","(37242) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ayyub ibn Musa, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: If the mother of one of you commits adultery, he should flog her, and he should not retaliate against her. If she commits adultery, then he should flog her. If she returns, he may sell her, even if it is with a braid of hair. (Nasa’i 7247)"
"37243","(37243) Shababi told us, on the authority of Laith bin Saad, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Amara bin Abi Farwa, On the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Aisha; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If the mother commits adultery, flog her; if she repeats it, flog her; if she returns, flog her. If she commits adultery, flog her, then sell her, even if it is with a braid. And the braided rope. (Ahmed 65)"
"37244","(37244) Mu’alla bin Mansour narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Uwais, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Abbad bin Tamim, On the authority of his uncle, who was Badriya, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If the mother commits adultery, flog her, then if she commits adultery So flog her, then if she commits adultery, flog her, then sell her, even if it is with a braid.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: Her master should not flog her. (Nasa’i 7238. Daraqutni 197)"
"37245","(37245) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Walid ibn Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ka’b, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Abdullah Ibn Rafi’ Ibn Khadij, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri; It was said: O Messenger of God, should we perform ablution from the well of your goods, which is a well into which menstruation, dog meat, and rotten things are thrown? The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Water is pure, nothing can make it impure."
"37246","(37246) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Some of the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, took a bath. May God bless him and grant him peace in his eyelids, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to wash from her, or to perform ablution, and she said: O Messenger of God, I was junub. He said: Water does not junub."
"37247","(37247) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Walid ibn Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ja’far ibn Al-Zubair, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If the water is two ounces, it will not carry unclean\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: Water makes it impure."
"37248","(37248) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ayoub Abi Al-Ala’, Qatad narrated to us, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Whoever forgets a prayer, or falls asleep during it, his atonement is that he prays it when he remembers it."
"37249","(37249) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Jami’ ibn Shaddad, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Alqamiya, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Masoud said: We came with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, from Al-Hudaybiyah, and they mentioned that they had come down Trampling on the ground, meaning by trampling on sand, he said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Who are we to eat? He said: Bilal said: I, then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Then we sleep. He said: They slept until the sun rose, he said: Then he woke up. People, among whom was so-and-so and so-and-so, and among them was Omar ibn al-Khattab. He said: So we said: Get ready, meaning, speak. He said: Then he woke up. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do as you used to do. He said: So we did. He said: So he said: Likewise for those who fell asleep. Or he forgot"
"37250","(37250) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul-Jabbar bin Abbas, on the authority of Aoun bin Abi Juhayfa, on the authority of his father He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to those who slept with him until the sun rose, and he said: You were dead. May God protect your souls. Whoever sleeps after praying, or forgets to pray, let him pray it when he remembers it, and when Wake up"
"37251","(37251) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abu Ismail, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: We had a wedding with... The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, one night, and we did not wake up until the sun hurt us, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Let each man of you take the head of his camel, then step aside from this house, then call for water, perform ablution, and prostrate. You prostrated two times, then the prayer was established and you prayed.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: It is not sufficient for him to pray if he wakes up at sunrise or at sunset."
"37252","(37252) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ka’b ibn Ajra, on the authority of Bilal; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wiped over the socks and the veil."
"37253","(37253) Yunus told us, on the authority of Dawud ibn Abi al-Furat, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Zayd, on the authority of Abu Shurayh, on the authority of Abu Muslim My servant Zaid bin Suhan, he said: I was with Salman and he saw a man taking off his socks to perform ablution, and Salman said to him: Wipe over Your socks and your khimaar, and wipe with your forelocks, for I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wiping over your socks. And the veil."
"37254","(37254) Yazeed narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Bakr, on the authority of Ibn Al-Mughirah bin Shu’abi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; He wiped the front of his head, and the socks, and put his hand on the turban, and wiped over the turban.\n It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: Wiping over them is not sufficient."
"37255","(37255) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace. He prayed, whether it increased or decreased. Then when he greeted the people and turned to face him, they said: O Messenger of God, it happened in Is prayer something? He said: What is that? They said: I prayed such-and-such, so he bent his leg and prostrated twice, then he saluted and turned to face the people, and said: If anything had happened during the prayer, I would have informed you of it, but I am a human being and I forget just as you forget, so if I forget, remember me. And if one of you doubts about his prayer, let him investigate what is right and complete it, and when he says the salutation, he should prostrate two prostrations. (Bukhari 404 and Muslim 401)"
"37256","(37256) Gandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abraham, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet May God bless him and grant him peace; He prayed the noon prayer five times, and it was said to him: Did you pray five days? So he prostrated two prostrations after the salutation.\n It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: If he does not sit on the fourth day, he should repeat the prayer."
"37257","(37257) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr; He heard Jabir saying: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: If the ihram is not found If he does not find sandals, then he should wear socks."
"37258","(37258) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever cannot find sandals, let him wear socks, and whoever cannot find a loincloth, let him wear trousers."
"37259","(37259) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: A man said: O Messenger of God, what Should the ihram wear? Or what the pilgrim in ihram leaves behind? He said: He does not wear a shirt, trousers, a turban, or socks, unless he does not find two sandals. So whoever does not He finds two sandals, so he should wear them lower than the ankles.\n - It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: He should not do it, for if he did it, a bloodshed would be imposed on him."
"37260","(37260) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zayd, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I prayed with the Prophet, he prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace, eight in all, and seven in all. He said: I said: O Abu Al-Sha’tha’i, I think he delayed the noon prayer and hastened the afternoon prayer. He delayed Maghrib and hastened Isha. He said: I think so."
"37261","(37261) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father; When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was on a journey, he would combine Maghrib and Isha."
"37262","(37262) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Abu al-Tufayl, on the authority of Muadh ibn Jabal; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, combined the noon and afternoon prayers, and the sunset and evening prayers while traveling, in his campaign. Tabuk"
"37263","(37263) Ibn Mushir told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gathered He made peace in his campaign against Tabuk between noon and afternoon, and between sunset and evening."
"37264","(37264) Yazeed narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Hafs bin Ubaid Allah bin Anas, who said: We were traveling with Anas. To Mecca, when the sun had set and he was at home, he would not ride until he had prayed the noon prayer. When he departed, Then the afternoon prayer came and he prayed the afternoon prayer. If he walked from his house before the sun had set and the prayer was ready, we said: the prayer, and he said: walk. Even when it was between the two prayers, he descended, combining the noon and afternoon prayers, then he said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, when he joined his dawn with his spirit, he did such and such."
"37265","(37245) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, combined the two prayers during his campaign against the Banu Mutaliqs.\n It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: It is not sufficient for him to do that."
"37266","(37266) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Umar invaded the land of Khaybar, so he came. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, asked him about it, and he said: I acquired land in Khaybar. I have never acquired any wealth of which I have any, so what? Do you command us? He said: If you wish, you can keep the originals and give them in charity. He said: So Omar gave them in charity, except that the originals are not sold, nor It is given and not bequeathed, so give it in charity to the poor, to relatives, to free slaves, in the way of God, to the wayfarer, and to the guest. There is no sin on the one who is in charge of it if he eats from it in a reasonable manner, or feeds a friend who does not trust in it."
"37267","(37267) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father; Did you not see that Hijr al-Madri told me that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, spoke the truth: its people would eat from it? With what is good and not denied.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: It is permissible for the heirs to return that."
"37268","(37268) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Umar, he said: I made a vow in The pre-Islamic era, so I asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, after I converted to Islam, and he ordered me to fulfill my vow."
"37269","(37269) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos; Concerning a man who vowed during the pre-Islamic period, then converted to Islam, he said: He will fulfill his vow.\n - It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: The oath is waived if he converts to Islam."
"37270","(37270) Muadh bin Muadh told us, he said: Ibn Juraij told us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Musa, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, On the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever is a woman whose guardian or guardians have not married her Her marriage is invalid. He said it three times. If he agreed to her, then she gets her dowry for what he agreed to from her. If they quarreled, then the sultan is his guardian. He who has no guardian"
"37271","(37271) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Burda, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No. Marriage except with a guardian."
"37272","(37272) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of his father, he said : The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is no marriage except with a guardian.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa used to say: It is permissible if the husband is compatible."
"37273","(37273) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; Saad bin Ubadah consulted the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, regarding a vow he had made to his mother, and she died before She made up for it, and he said: Make it up for her."
"37274","(37274) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Ata, on the authority of Ibn Buraida, on the authority of his father, he said: I was sitting With the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when a woman came to him and said: My mother was required to fast for two months. Should I fast? About us? He said: Fast on her behalf. Do you think that if your mother had a debt that you had repaid, would that be sufficient on her behalf? She said: Yes, he said: Then fast on her behalf."
"37275","(37275) Abdul Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Kurayb, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Sinan bin Abdullah Al-Jinni, that his paternal aunt told him; She came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, my mother died and she has to go to... The Kaaba was a vow, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Are you able to walk away from it? She said: Yes. He said: So walk on behalf of your mother. She said: Or will that suffice on her behalf? He said: Yes. He said: Have you seen that if she had a debt she had to pay it off, would it have been accepted from her? She said: Yes, then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God has more right.\n It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: This is not sufficient."
"37276","(37276) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and Zayd ibn Khalid, And a young lion; They were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a man stood up and said: I adjure you by God, unless you judge between us according to the Book of God. Then his opponent, who was more knowledgeable than him, said: Judge between us according to the Book of God, and he gave me permission to say something. He said: Say, he said: Indeed, my son He was stubborn about this, and he committed adultery with his wife, so I ransomed him with a hundred sheep and a servant, so I asked men from the family Knowledge, so I was informed that my son is to be subjected to a hundred lashes and exile for a year, and that his wife is to be stoned. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: By the One in whose hand is my soul, I will judge between you according to the Book of God: A hundred sheep and a servant will be returned to you. Your son will be subjected to a hundred lashes and a year's exile, and go tomorrow, O Anis, to this woman. If she confesses, stone her."
"37277","(37277) Shabab bin Siwar told us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Qatad, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Hattan bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Take it from him. God has made a way for them: Al-Bakr For the virgin, and the unmarried for the married, the virgin will be flogged and banished, and the unmarried will be flogged and stoned.\n It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: It is not negated."
"37278","(37278) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Umm Qais bin Muhsin, she said: I entered Concerning the son of Ali, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not eat the food, so he urinated on him, so he called for water and sprinkled it on him."
"37279","(37279) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Qaboos ibn Al-Mukhariq, on the authority of Lubab ibn Al-Harith, she said: Al-Hussein bin Ali Ali the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so I said: Give me your dress and wear something else, and he said: It is only to be washed off. From the urine of the male, and it is washed from the urine of the female."
"37280","(37280) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought to the Prophet and he urinated on him, so he ran water on him and did not wash him."
"37281","(37281) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Isa, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of his grandfather. Abu Layla, he said: We were sitting with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, then Al-Hussein bin Ali came crawling until he sat on His chest, and he urinated on it. He said: So we hastened to take it, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: My son, my son. Then he called With water, he poured it on him.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: He should be washed."
"37282","(37282) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he heard Sahl bin Saad; Al-Muttalan witnessed the covenant of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He separated them and said: O Messenger of God, I lied to her. If I catch her."
"37283","(37283) Yazeed told us, on the authority of Abbad bin Mansour, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, dispersed. May peace and blessings be upon them."
"37284","(37284) Ibn Numayr and Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Cursing the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace between a man from the Ansar and his wife, so he separated them. (Bukhari 5314, Muslim 1133)"
"37285","(37285) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, separated them. (Muslim 1130, Darami 2231)"
"37286","(37286) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Omar; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, separated between the two who were cursing and said: O Messenger of God, my money. He said: You have no money, if you Tell the truth, then it is because of what you have permitted from her private parts, and if you are a liar, then that is farther for you than her.\n It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: He will marry her if he lies to himself."
"37287","(37287) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: I heard Anas bin Malik say: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, fell. He said the salaam on the back of a horse, and its right side parted, so we entered and returned to him, and the time for prayer came, and he led us in prayer sitting, so we prayed. And he was sitting behind him, and when he had finished the prayer, he said: The imam has only been appointed to be followed, so when he says “Allahu Akbar,” they should pronounce “Allahu Akbar,” and when he bows, “so they should bow.” And when he prostrates, then prostrate, and when he raises up, raise yourselves, and when he says: God hears those who praise Him, then say: O God, our Lord, and to You belongs all praise. He prayed sitting, and they all prayed sitting."
"37288","(37288) Abdou told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, complained. He greeted him, and some of his companions came to visit him, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed sitting, and they continued his prayer. Standing up, he motioned to them to sit down, so they sat down, and when he left, he said: The imam has only been appointed to be followed in prayer, so when he bows So bow down, and when he rises, rise up, and when he prays sitting, pray sitting."
"37289","(37289) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was struck by an epilepsy. A horse of his own, and it fell on the trunk of a palm tree, and its foot broke off. He said: So we entered upon him and went back to him while he was praying in a drinking place. Aisha was sitting, so we performed his prayer while we were standing, then we entered upon him another time while he was praying sitting. So we prayed his prayer while we were standing, so he motioned to us to sit down, and when he prayed, he said: The imam was appointed only to be followed by him. If he prays standing, pray standing, and if he prays sitting, pray sitting, and do not stand while he is sitting as the people of Persia do. With its greatness"
"37290","(37290) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The imam has only been appointed to be followed, so when he says “Allahu Akbar” then “Allahu Akbar” and when he recites “Allahu Akbar.” So listen, and when he says: {None of them is angry, nor those who go astray}, say: Amen, and when he bows, kneel, and when he says: He heard God is for those who praise Him, so say: O God, our Lord, and to You is praise. And when he prostrates, then prostrate, and if he prays sitting, then pray sitting.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: The imam should not lead while he is sitting."
"37291","(37291) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Omar bin Saeed bin Abi Hussein, he said: Ibn Abi Maliki narrated to us, he said Uqba bin Al-Harith narrated to us, saying: I married his son, Abu Ihab Al-Tamimi, and when she became king in the morning, she came A servant of the people of Mecca, and she said: I have breastfed you both. So he rode his heel to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. In Medina, so he mentioned that to him, and said: I asked the family of the slave girl, but they denied it, so he said: How is that, when it has been said? So he separated from her, and she married someone else."
"37292","(37292) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Uthaym, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Al-Bilamani, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked: What is permissible in breastfeeding from witnesses? He said: man or woman.\n It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: It is not permissible except more."
"37293","(37293) Yazeed bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Dawud bin Husayn, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned his daughter Zainab to Abu Al-Aas two years after her first marriage.\n(Abu Dawud 2233, Hakim 200)"
"37294","(37294) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, responded to him with her first marriage.\n - It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: The marriage will resume. (Abdul Razzaq 12440 and Saeed bin Mansour 2107)"
"37295","(37295) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Isa bin Talha, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: He came. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a man and said: Did I shave before I slaughtered? He said: Then slaughter it, and there is no harm. He said: Did I slaughter it before stoning the stone? He said: Shoot, and there is no harm."
"37296","(37296) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; That a questioner asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Did I throw stones after the evening? He said: There is no harm. He said: And he said: Did I shave before I slaughtered? He said: There is no harm."
"37297","(37297) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Ayyash, on the authority of Zayd bin Ali, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi’, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, a man came to him and said: I Did I break up before I shaved? He said: Shave it, or cut it short, and there is no embarrassment."
"37298","(37298) Asbat bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ziyad bin Allaqiya, on the authority of Asama bin Sharik; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked by a man and said: Did I shave before I slaughtered? He said: There is no harm."
"37299","(37299) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Asama bin Zayd, on the authority of Ata`, on the authority of Jabir, who said: A man said: O Messenger of God, I shaved Before I commit suicide? He said: There is no harm.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: There is blood on him."
"37300","(37300) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Yahya bin Abbad, on the authority of Anas bin Malik; Orphans inherited wine, so Abu Talha asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to make it vinegar. He said: No.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: There is no harm in it."
"37301","(37301) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Al-Bara’; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent him to a man who had married his father’s wife, so he ordered him to come to him. With his head"
"37302","(37302) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan bin Salih, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: I met my uncle And he has the opinion, so I said: Where are you going? He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me to a man who married his father’s wife to kill him or strike him. His neck\n It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: He only has to do the punishment."
"37303","(37303) Hafs and Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of al-Mujalid, on the authority of Abu al-Wadak, Jabr bin Nawf, on the authority of Abu Saeed, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The death of the fetus, the death of its mother when it feels.\n - It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: Her slaughter is not the slaughter of her mother. (Tirmidhi 1476. Abu Dawud 2820)"
"37304","(37304) Waki` and Abu Khalid al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of Fatima ibn al-Mundhir, on the authority of the names Ibn Abi Bakr, she said: We slaughtered a horse at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we ate of its meat, or We have become infected with His flesh."
"37305","(37305) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, fed us horse meat. And he forbade us from donkey meat."
"37306","(37306) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: We ate horse meat on the day Khaybara\n - It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: It should not be eaten."
"37307","(37307) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Zakariya, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he said: The zihar is to be ridden if it is mortgaged, and the milk of the pearl is to be drunk if it is mortgaged, and upon the one who rides and drinks Your expenses"
"37308","(37308) Wakī’ narrated to us, Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The mortgage is forfeited. And mounted."
"37309","(37309) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The mortgage is voidable. And mounted.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: It cannot be benefited from, nor can it be used."
"37310","(37310) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He said: The sale is for option in their sale as long as they do not separate, unless their sale is for option."
"37311","(37311) Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Salih Abi Al-Khalil, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Hakim bin Hazzam; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The sale is for option unless they separate."
"37312","(37312) Hashim bin Al-Qasim narrated to us, Ayoub bin Utba narrated to us, Abu Kathir Al-Suhaimi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Huraira, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A trade for option is a sale between them as long as they do not separate, or They can be sold at an option."
"37313","(37313) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Zayd, on the authority of Jamil bin Murra, on the authority of Abu Al-Wadhi, on the authority of Abi Barza, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The two trades are for option as long as they do not separate."
"37314","(37314) Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: The sale is at option as long as they do not separate.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: It is permissible to sell even if they do not separate. (Ibn Majah 2183. Ahmed 17)"
"37315","(37315) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, on the authority of Abdullah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness after speaking."
"37316","(37316) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, spoke, then he prostrated with two prostrations of forgetfulness."
"37317","(37317) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalab, on the authority of Abu Al-Muhallab, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed three rak’ahs, then left, and a man called Al-Kharbaq stood up to him and said: O Messenger of God, has the prayer been shortened? He said: What is that? He said: I prayed three rak'ahs, so he prayed one rak'ah, then he gave the salutation, then he prostrated with the prostration of forgetfulness, then he gave the salutation.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: If he speaks, he should not prostrate to them."
"37318","(37318) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Aamir bin Rabi’a, on the authority of his father; That a man got married at the time of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wearing two sandals, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, permitted Sexual intercourse"
"37319","(37319) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zayed, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to a man: Go, I have married you to her. So teach her a surah from the Qur’an."
"37320","(37320) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Labibă, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever declares permissible a dirham has declared permissible."
"37321","(37321) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn al-Mughirah al-Taifi, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Al-Bilamani, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, delivered a speech and said: “Marry the young women among you.” Then a man stood up to him, He said: O Messenger of God, what are the relations between them? He said: Whatever their families agree upon."
"37322","(37322) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas, who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf married Ali. The weight of a stone of gold is equal to three dirhams and a third."
"37323","(37323) Hafs told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Whatever the husband and wife agree upon is a dowry."
"37324","(37324) Mu’tamir told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: I asked Al-Hasan: What is the minimum for a man to marry? He said: The weight of a stone of gold."
"37325","(37325) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ismail ibn Umayyah, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, he said: If you were satisfied With a whip that was skillful."
"37326","(37326) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Umair al-Khathami, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn al-Mughirah al-Taifi, on the authority of Ibn Al-Bilamani, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: {And give the women charity, and we will freely give it to them.} They said: They said: O Messenger God, what are the relationships between them? He said: Whatever their families agree upon.\n It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: He should not marry her for less than ten dirhams."
"37327","(37327) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Suhayb, on the authority of Anas bin Malik; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, freed Safiyya and married her. He said: He was told: How truthful is she? He said: He befriended her soul, and made her emancipation befriend her."
"37328","(37328) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, who said: Ali said: If he wishes, he can free the man or his mother. He gave birth to her, and made her freed as her dowry."
"37329","(37329) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, who said: Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab said: Whoever frees his daughter, or The mother of his son and made that a dowry for her, I thought that was permissible for him.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: It is not permissible except with a dowry."
"37330","(37330) Hushaym told us, Ali bin Ata’ told us, he said: Jabir bin Al-Aswad told me, on the authority of his father, he said: I witnessed his proof with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I prayed the morning prayer with him in the Al-Khaif Mosque. When he finished His prayer and he turned aside when there were two men at the back of the people who did not pray with him, so he said: I have to do them, so he brought them to him while he was thundering. Their prayers, so he said: What prevented you from praying with us? They said: O Messenger of God, we had prayed in our travels. He said: Do not do that, if you prayed in your travels, then you came. A congregational mosque, so pray with them, for it is a voluntary prayer for both of you."
"37331","(37331) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zayd ibn Aslam, on the authority of Bishr, or Busr ibn Mihjan al-Du’ali, on the authority of His father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; In the same way\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: Do not repeat Fajr. (Ahmad 34. Malik 132)"
"37332","(37332) Abdi told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of Sulayman al-Naji, on the authority of Abu al-Mutawakkil, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, He said: A man came while the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had prayed. He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Which of you? Is he trading on this? He said: Then a man from the people stood up and prayed with him.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: Do not gather in prayer in it."
"37333","(37333) Abdul Rahim narrated to us, Ibn Abi Arouba narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he said: Whoever kills his servant, We will kill him, and whoever kills his servant, We will kill him.\n It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: He shall not be killed for it."
"37334","(37334) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Whoever performs the rak’ah of the afternoon prayer before the sun sets has performed the prayer. The Fajr prayer is performed by kneeling before the sun rises, as he has completed the prayer.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: If he prays two rak’ahs of dawn and then the sun rises, that is not sufficient. (Malik 5. Ahmad 462)"
"37335","(37335) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: A man came to the Prophet May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I was destroyed. He said: What destroyed you? He said: I had intercourse with my wife during Ramadan. He said: Free a slave. He said: I have no choice. He said: Fast for two months. He said: I cannot. He said: Feed sixty poor people. He said: I cannot find it. He said: Sit down. So he sat down, while he was like that when he was brought with a vein in it. Dates. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Go and give them in charity. He said: By the One who sent you with the truth, there is no evidence of Medina is the people of a household poorer than us. So he laughed until his fangs showed, then he said: Go and feed him. Your family\n It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: It is not permissible for him to feed his family."
"37336","(37336) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Abu Umair ibn Anas, who said: My Ansar cousins narrated to me from The Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The crescent of Shawwal fell upon us, so we began fasting, then another group came. Then they testified with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that they had seen the crescent yesterday, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded He granted that they should break their fast and that they should go out for their Eid the next day.\n It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: They will not go out the next day."
"37337","(37337) Waki’ narrated to us, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ziyad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Prophet said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Whoever buys an Egyptian property has the option to buy it. If he wishes, he can return it and bring back with it a saa’ of dates."
"37338","(37338) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of a man from among the companions of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever buys an estate will lose it. With the best of both worlds, if he returns it, he will return with it a saa’ of dates, or a saa’ of food.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said otherwise."
"37339","(37339) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, all dates and raisins, and all dates and dates, should be rejected."
"37340","(37340) Ibn Mushir told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade that dates and raisins be mixed together, and that raisins and raisins be mixed together. And he wrote about that to the people of Jerash."
"37341","(37341) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj bin Abi Uthman, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Abi Qatada, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: Do not reject dates and raisins altogether, nor Abandon the bright and the fresh, and reject each one of them separately."
"37342","(37342) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Abu Arta, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade fresh fruits and dates, and raisins and dates.\n It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: There is no harm in it."
"37343","(37343) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Qays, on the authority of Huzayl, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: Cursed The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, is the one who makes it lawful and the one who is made lawful to him."
"37344","(37344) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Musayyab ibn Rafi’, on the authority of Qubaysa ibn Jabir, he said, Omar said: I will not be given it. With a halal, and there is no halal for him, except I stone them both."
"37345","(37345) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid al-Hadha’i, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: May God curse him. The analyst and the one being analyzed."
"37346","(37346) Ibn Numair told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Amer, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: May God curse the one who makes it lawful and the one who is made unlawful to him."
"37347","(37347) Aidh bin Habib told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: May God curse the one who makes it lawful and the one who is made lawful to him.\n - It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: If he marries her to make her lawful, and he desires her, there is no harm in him holding her."
"37348","(37348) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Abi Abd al-Rahman al-Ra’i, on the authority of Yazid Mawla Al-Manba’th, on the authority of Zayd bin Khaled Al-Janni, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about the cat, and he said: Identify it. A year, if its owner comes, otherwise he will spend it."
"37349","(37349) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salama ibn Kuhayl, on the authority of Suwayd ibn Ghafla, who said: I went out, And Zaid bin Suhan and Salman bin Rabi’a even when we were with Al-Athib, I picked up a whip, and they said to me: Throw it, but I refused. When we came to Medina, I went to Ubayy ibn Ka’b and asked him, and he said: I collected a hundred dinars at the time of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, so I mentioned that to him, and he said: He taught her a Sunnah, so I knew her a Sunnah, but I did not find anyone who knew her. So I came to him, and he said: Acquaint her with her for a year, and if you find her companion, give her to him. Otherwise, find out her number and her container. And its trusts, then they will be like the way of your owner. \n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: If her companion comes, he will be fined."
"37350","(37350) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade He refrained from selling the fruit until its goodness was evident."
"37351","(37351) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade He said hello to the sale of the fruit until it becomes clear that it is good. (Bukhari 2381, Muslim 81)"
"37352","(37352) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Zaid bin Jubayr, who said: A man asked Ibn Umar about buying fruit? He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade selling the fruit until it appears to be good."
"37353","(37353) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Yazid bin Khumayr, on the authority of a servant of Quraysh, who said: I heard Abu Huraira narrates to Muawiyah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade selling the fruit until it has been removed from every bidder."
"37354","(37354) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: The Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him about selling fruit until it appears to be good. They said: What does it appear to be good? He said: Her defects will go away and her goodness will be removed."
"37355","(37355) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’abi, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, on the authority of Abu al-Bakhtari, who said: I asked Ibn Abbas about Selling palm trees? He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade selling palm trees until one has eaten from them, or one has eaten from them, and even It is weighed. I said: What is it weighed? A man with him said: Until he is scored. (Bukhari 2250, Muslim 1167)"
"37356","(37356) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade selling The fruit of the palm tree until it blossomed, so Anas was asked: What is its fruit? He said: It turns red or yellow."
"37357","(37357) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, he said: Al-Qasim and Makhul narrated to us, on the authority of Abu In front of him; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade selling the fruit until it appears to be good."
"37358","(37358) Ali bin Ubaid narrated to us, Fudayl bin Ghazwan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Na’am, on the authority of Abu Hurairah ; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade selling the fruit until it appears to be good.\n - It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: There is no harm in selling dates, but it is contrary to the effect."
"37359","(37359) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: I was presented to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) greeted him on the day of Uhud, and I was fourteen years old, so they looked down upon me, and I was presented to him on the Day of the Trench, and I was five years old. Ten days, so he rewarded me. Nafi’ said: I narrated it to Omar bin Abdul Aziz, he said: He said: This is a definition between the small and the great. He said: So he wrote to his workers to make an allotment for the son of fifteen years among the fighters, and for the son of fourteen years among the offspring.\n - It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: There is nothing owed to a slave woman until she reaches eighteen or seventeen years of age."
"37360","(37360) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered Attab bin Asid to prune grapes as palm trees are pruned, so that his zakat should be paid. Raisins, just as the zakat on palm trees is paid on dates. This is the Sunnah of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, regarding palm trees and grapes."
"37361","(37361) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent Abdullah bin Rawahih to the people of Yemen, and he planted palm trees for them."
"37362","(37362) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Khubayb bin Abdul Rahman, he said: I heard Abdul Rahman bin Masoud, He says: Sahil bin Abi Hathami came to our meeting, and it happened that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If you are silent, So they took and called."
"37363","(37363) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, that he heard him say: Ibn Rawahih chose it, meaning Khaybar, forty thousand wasqs, and he claimed that the Jews had not given Ibn Rawahih a choice for them. They took dates, and they owed twenty thousand wasqs."
"37364","(37364) Abu Khalid told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Bashir bin Yasar; Omar used to send Abu Hathmiya to harvest date palms.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa did not see khuras."
"37365","(37365) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: The best thing a man eats is from his own earnings, and his children from his earnings."
"37366","(37366) Ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ammar bin Ummar, on the authority of his paternal aunt, on the authority of Aisha, she said: He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: The best of what you eat is from your earnings, and your children are from your earnings."
"37367","(37367) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: A man from the Ansar came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: O Messenger of God, my father has seized my wealth from me. He said: You and your father’s wealth belong to you."
"37368","(37368) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Mundakir, who said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him and said: O Messenger of God, I have wealth, and my father has wealth. He said: You and your wealth belong to your father. (Abdul Razzaq 14628)"
"37369","(37369) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafla, on the authority of Aisha She said: A man may eat from his son’s wealth whatever he wants, and a child may not eat from his father’s wealth except with his permission."
"37370","(37370) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: A man came to The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: My father has invaded my wealth. He said: You and your wealth belong to your father.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: He does not take from his wealth unless he is in need and it is spent on him."
"37371","(37371) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, who said: People came from your den. They invaded Medina, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to them: If you wish, you can go out to the camels of charity and drink from Her urine and her milk, so do it."
"37372","(37372) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj bin Abi Uthman, he said: Abu Raja’i, the client of Abi Qalab, narrated to us, on the authority of Abi Qalaba, on the authority of Anas; A group of eight people from Uql came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and pledged their allegiance to him on the basis of Islam, so they took possession of the land. Their bodies became sick, so they complained about this to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Don’t you go out with our shepherd to his camels? So you get some of her urine and milk? They said: Yes, so they went out and drank from her urine and milk.\n It was reported that Abu Hanifa hated drinking camel urine."
"37373","(37373) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Hakim, on the authority of Aamir ibn Saad, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: I forbid what is between the two women of Medina; That its organs be cut off, or that its hunter be killed, and he said: Medina is better for them, if they only knew. (Muslim 992. Ahmad 181)"
"37374","(37374) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of his father, he said: Ali addressed us, He said: Whoever claims that we have anything to read except the Book of God, and this parchment, a parchment in which there are camels’ teeth, And some of the wounds. He said: And in it, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Medina is a sanctuary between bull"
"37375","(37375) Ali bin Musir told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Yusir bin Amr, on the authority of Saul bin Hanif, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, took shelter in Medina and said: It is a safe sanctuary."
"37376","(37376) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, he said: He said: Abu Huraira: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade what was between her two daughters. He meant Medina. Abu Hariri: If I had found the antelope still, I would not have panicked. (Tirmidhi 3921, Ahmad 487)"
"37377","(37377) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Abi Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God has forbidden to my tongue what is between the two women of Medina. (Bukhari 1869. Ahmed 286)"
"37378","(37378) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Kathir, he said: Sharhabeel Abu Saad narrated to me; He entered the trees and caught a bird with them, so Zayd ibn Thabit entered upon him, and he was with him, and he licked his ear. And he said: Leave his way, you have no mother. Did you not know that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade what was between her two daughters? (Ahmad 1811. Tabarani 4911)"
"37379","(37379) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Kathir, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abdul-Rahman bin Abi Sa’id. Al-Khudri, that Abd al-Rahman narrated to him, on the authority of his father, Abu Sa`id; He heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: I have forbidden what is between the two daughters of Medina, just as Abraham forbade Mecca, he said: Then Abu Sa’id used to find one of us with the bird in his hand, which he had taken, and he would free it from his hand. So He sends it to him. (Muslim 1003. Abu Ali 1006)"
"37380","(37380) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Asim Al-Ahwal, who said: I asked Anas bin Malik: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered ihram. And he delivered the city? He said: Yes, it is forbidden, God and His Messenger have made it sacred, do not leave it alone, so whoever does that will be cursed by God. And the angels and all mankind. (Bukhari 1867, Muslim 994)"
"37381","(37381) Ibn Abi Ghani told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Isa, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Ibn Abbas informed me; He heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Oh God, I have made Medina sacred for what You have made Mecca sacred.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: He does not have to do anything. (Ahmed 318)"
"37382","(37382) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Bakr, on the authority of Abu Masoud; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the dowry of a transgressor and the price of a dog."
"37383","(37383) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Hariri, who said: The Messenger of God forbade May God bless him and grant him peace about the dowry of a transgressor and the price of a dog."
"37384","(37384) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, who said: The most evil gain is the price of a dog. And the piper won."
"37385","(37385) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, he said: I think Abu Sufyan mentioned it, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade May God bless him and grant him peace, for the price of dogs and cats."
"37386","(37386) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul-Jabbar bin Abbas, on the authority of Aoun bin Abi Juhayfa, on the authority of his father He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the price of a dog."
"37387","(37387) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Qais bin Habtar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The price of a dog, the dowry of a prostitute, and the price of wine are forbidden.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa made a discount on the price of the dog."
"37388","(37388) Ibn Mushir told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, cut off And he said hello in a shield, worth three dirhams."
"37389","(37389) Yazeed told us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Kathir and Ibrahim bin Saad, they all said: Al-Zuhri informed us, On the authority of Omra, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: It is cut at a quarter of a dinar or more."
"37390","(37390) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Issa bin Abi Ezzah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdullah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, cut off five dirhams.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: It is not cut off for less than ten dirhams."
"37391","(37391) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Razin, on the authority of Abu Hariri, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: When one of you gets up at night, he should not dip his hand in the vessel until he has washed it three times, for he does not He knows where his hand has been."
"37392","(37392) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When one of you gets up from sleep, let him empty his vessel three times. For he does not know where his hand has spent the night."
"37393","(37393) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: When one of you gets up during the night, he should not dip his hand into the vessel until he has washed it."
"37394","(37394) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man wakes up from his sleep, he should not enter. His hand is in the vessel until he washes it.\n It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: There is no harm in it."
"37395","(37395) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: To purify the vessel of one of you when a dog empties it by washing it seven times, cover it with dirt."
"37396","(37396) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Razin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace. He says: If a dog licks the vessel of one of you, let him wash it seven times."
"37397","(37397) Shababah ibn Siwar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu al-Tayyah, who said: I heard Mutarrif, narrating on the authority of Ibn The fool; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered the killing of dogs, and said: If a dog licks a vessel, wash it seven times. And cover the eighth with dust.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: It is sufficient to wash oneself once."
"37398","(37398) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Malik ibn Anas, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Yazid, on the authority of Zaid Abi Ayyash, who said: I asked Saad about saltet with corn, and he thought about it, and Saad said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about dates with dates, and he said: Does it decrease when it dries? We said: Yes, he said: So he forbade it."
"37399","(37399) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He disliked rutab with dates, and he said: It is the smaller of the two in a bushel or in a qafiz."
"37400","(37400) Ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade selling grapes for raisins in bulk."
"37401","(37401) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Tariq, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; He disliked the date with dates, like for example, and said: Dates are swollen, and dates are rotten.\n It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: There is no harm in it."
"37402","(37402) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Sulayman al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; He forbade receiving sales."
"37403","(37403) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: Do not face each other, nor swear an oath."
"37404","(37404) Ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade May God bless him and grant him peace.\n It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: There is no harm in it. (Muslim 14. Ahmad 20)"
"37405","(37405) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; That a man was with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was in Ihram, and his she-camel calfed him and he died, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Wash him with water and lotus leaves, and shroud him in his garment, and do not cover his head, for God will resurrect him. On the Day of Resurrection, reciting the Talbiyah."
"37406","(37406) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: A man fell down from his camel and died, so he said: Wash him with water and lotus leaves, and wrap him in his clothes. Cover his head, for God will raise him with the talbiyah on the Day of Resurrection.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: He should cover his head."
"37407","(37407) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he heard Sahl bin Saad say: A man came out of a hole into his room. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was with him, scratching his head, and he said: If I had known that you were looking, I would have stabbed him in the mouth. Your eyes, permission is only from sight. (Tabarani 5585)"
"37408","(37408) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in his house, and a man came out through the door, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, closed it. He greeted someone like him with a broken heart, but he delayed."
"37409","(37409) Khaled bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Bilal, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: If a man were to look at a people without their permission, it would be permissible for them to remain silent. His eyes"
"37410","(37410) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Qays Abd al-Rahman bin Tharwan, on the authority of Huzayl, who said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: If a man were to look into a people’s house through a window and shoot at a window, and his eyes would go out. It would have been invalidated.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: He guarantees."
"37411","(37411) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Whoever keeps a dog, other than a hunting dog, or a livestock animal, two qirats will be deducted from his reward each day."
"37412","(37412) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, who said: I went with Ibn Umar to Bani Muawiyah. Then dogs barked at us, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever keeps a dog except a ferocious dog, or Walking, his wages are reduced by two qirats every day."
"37413","(37413) Affan narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaym bin Hayyan, he said: I heard my father narrating, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Whoever adopts a dog that is neither a farm dog, nor a hunter, nor a livestock dog, will be reduced from His reward every day is one Qirat."
"37414","(37414) Khalid bin Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Yazid bin Khusaifi, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid, On the authority of Sufyan bin Abi Zuhayr, he said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: Whoever keeps a dog will not become rich. He had no crops, but no udder. He lost a Qirat from his work every day, and it was said to him: You heard it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Oh, by the Lord of this mosque."
"37415","(37415) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Whoever keeps a dog Except for a hunting dog, or a livestock dog, which detracts from its action every day a Qirat.\n It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: There is no harm in taking it."
"37416","(37416) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was sent He greeted Mu'adh and ordered him to take from every thirty people, or one from every forty, so they asked him About the surplus between them, but he refused to take it until he asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Do not take anything."
"37417","(37417) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: There is nothing in it."
"37418","(37418) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked the arbiter, I said: What were the fifty cows? The arbitrator said: There is a sin in it."
"37419","(37419) Abdul Rahim told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ali, who said: There is nothing wrong with hanging."
"37420","(37420) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus; That Muadh said: There is nothing in the aqasas.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: In it, the excess will be accounted for."
"37421","(37421) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Asim ibn Kulayb, on the authority of his father, who said: We were in battles without being commanded. Except for the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. We were in Persia over us, a man from Muzainah from among the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him. Then the old man became overwhelmed by us, to the point where we used to buy the old man for two or three lumps, so this man rose up among us and said: : Indeed, this day came upon us, and the tooth became heavy upon us, to the point that we were buying the tooth for two or three lumps of stone, so he rose up among us. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The elderly person will be repaid from what the second person is repaid. (Ahmad 368, Hakim 226)"
"37422","(37422) Qasim bin Malik told us, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of a man from Muzainah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sacrificed while traveling."
"37423","(37423) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He saw no harm in, if a man traveled, instructing his family to perform the sacrifice on his behalf.\n It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: The traveler is not obligated to offer a sacrifice."
"37424","(37424) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: We went out with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace during the Farewell Hajj, joining the crescent of Dhul-Hijj. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever wants If one of you says Ihram for his life, let him say Ihram, for if I had not been guided, I would have declared Ihram for his life. She said: So he was one of the people. He who declared ihram for Hajj, and among them was he who performed ihram for Hajj. She said: So I was among those who declared ihram for Hajj. She said: So we went out until we arrived. He was in Mecca, and he found me on the day of Arafah while I was menstruating, and I had not been permitted to enter the state of Umrah. So I complained about that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him, and he said: Give up your Umrah, and finish your head, and walk, and complete the Hajj. She said: So I did, and when the night fell Al-Hasba, and God had completed our Hajj. He sent with me Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, and he brought me back and took me to al-Tan’im. So I swore by my life, and God completed our Hajj and our Umrah. There was no sacrifice, no charity, no fasting in that. (Bukhari 317, Muslim 872)"
"37425","(37425) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid and Ata, who said: I asked them On the authority of a woman who came to Mecca one year ago and had her period, so she was afraid that she would miss Hajj? They said: Perform Hajj and proceed.\n - It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: She refuses Hajj, and she must pay a blood sacrifice and a lifespan in her place."
"37426","(37426) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Tasbih is for men, and clapping is for women."
"37427","(37427) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadhru, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Prophet prayed, prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace. One day, when he stood up to say “Allahu Akbar,” he said: “The devil has made me forget some of my prayer.” Tasbih is for men, and applause is for women."
"37428","(37428) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Hamid bin Jafar, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Tasbih is for men, and applause is for women."
"37429","(37429) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, who said: Glorification in prayer. For men, and applause for women."
"37430","(37430) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid, who said: I sought permission from Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla and he... He prays, so the boy said “Tasbih” and it was opened for me."
"37431","(37431) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: A man asked permission from Ali Jabir bin Abdullah, so he said the tasbih, and he entered. So he sat until he left.\n It was reported that Abu Hanifa used to say: He should not do that, and he hated it."
"37432","(37432) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: There was a blind man from among the Muslims, and he was taking refuge in A Jewish woman, and she used to feed him, give him water to drink, and treat him kindly, but she still used to hurt him about the Messenger. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, when he heard that from her one night, he got up and strangled her until he killed her, so he raised That was brought to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he appealed to the people about her matter, so the man got up and told that she had been harming her. Concerning the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she cursed him and fell into her, so he killed her for that, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, invalidated Blood \n(Abu Dawud 4361. An-Nasa’i 3533)"
"37433","(37433) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Sheikh, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He defeated a monk who insulted the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with the sword, and said: We have not reconciled with you over insulting our Prophet. May God bless him and grant him peace.\n It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: He shall not be killed."
"37434","(37434) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Qais bin Wahhab, on the authority of a man from Banu Sawa’, who said: I said to Aisha: Tell me. About the character of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? She said: Or do you not read the Qur’an? {And indeed, you have a great character}. She said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was with his companions, so I prepared food for him, and she prepared Hafsiya has food, but Hafsiya outran me. She said: So I said to the maid: Go, and I will fill her bowl. She said: So she intended to place it in the hands of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he gave it to her, and the bowl broke and he scattered. Food, she said: So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gathered them and all the food in them on the ground, and they ate, then he sent two bowls. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave her to Hafsa and said: Take an envelope instead of your envelope, and eat whatever is in it. She said: I did not see him in the face of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Ibn Majah 2333. Ahmad 111)"
"37435","(37435) Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, who said: Some of the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave gifts to him. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was eating a bowl with porridge in it, and it was at the house of some of his wives. She hit the bowl and it fell. It broke, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, took the porridge and returned it to the bowl with his hand, and said: Eat. Your mother became jealous, then he waited until a healthy bowl came, so he took it and gave it to the owner of the broken bowl.\n(Bukhari 2481, Abu Dawud 3562)"
"37436","(37436) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: Whoever breaks a stick, it is his, and upon him. Like him\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said something different, and said: “I will stand by you.”"
"37437","(37437) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Zaid bin Thabit informed me; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made concessions regarding nakedness. (Musnad 120)"
"37438","(37438) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Kathir, he said: Bashir bin Yasar told me; He heard Sahil bin Abi Hathamiah and Rafi’ bin Abi Khadij say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade The areas and the barns, except for the owners of naked things, for He has given them permission.\n It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: This is not valid."
"37439","(37439) Ibn Uyaynah and Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Ibn Umar; Ghaylan bin Salamah embraced Islam and had eight wives, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered him to choose from among them. Four\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: The first four."
"37440","(37440) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The people of I wanted them to sell it and stipulate loyalty, so I mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Buy it. And free her, for loyalty belongs to the one who frees her. (Bukhari 1493, Tirmidhi 1256)"
"37441","(37441) Affan told us, Hammam told us, on the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; Her masters stipulated loyalty, so it was decided that loyalty belongs to whoever is freed."
"37442","(37442) Shabab bin Siwar told us, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Aisha wanted to You buy Breeira, and they say: Are you buying her on the condition that her loyalty is to us? So I mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: That will not prevent you. Of these, loyalty is only to the one who is freed.\n It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: This purchase is corrupt and not permissible. (Bukhari 2562 and Abu Dawud 2907)"
"37443","(37443) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ezra, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abd al-Rahman bin Abza. On the authority of his father, on the authority of Ammar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: Tayammum is striking the face and the palms."
"37444","(37444) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Suleiman bin Musa, on the authority of Abu Hurairah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, urinated, then struck his hand to the ground and wiped his face and palms with it."
"37445","(37445) Wakī’ narrated to us, Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Salmah ibn Kuhayl, on the authority of Ibn Abza, on the authority of his father, he said: He said: Omar to Ammar: Do you not remember the day we were in such-and-such, and we went out into a state of ritual impurity, but we did not find water, so we languished in the dirt, so when we came We mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: This was enough for you both, and he struck Al-Amash. He struck them with his hand, then blew them, then wiped his face with them and covered his hands with them.\n - It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: Two strikes, one strike is not sufficient."
"37446","(37446) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Shabib bin Gharqadiya, on the authority of Urwa al-Bariqi; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave him a dinar with which to buy a sheep for himself, so he bought two sheep with it, so he sold One of them was for a dinar, and he brought the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, a dinar and a sheep, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed for it. He acknowledged the blessing in his sale, and if he had bought dirt, he would have made a profit from it.\n(Bukhari 3442, Abu Dawud 377)"
"37447","(37447) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Hakim ibn Hazzam; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent a mission to buy a sacrifice for him for a dinar, so he bought it and then sold it. With two dinars, he bought a tea for a dinar, and he brought it to him with a dinar, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed for him with blessings. And he ordered him to give the dinar in charity.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: He is liable if he sells without his command. (Abu Dawud 3379. Tirmidhi 1257)"
"37448","(37448) Abu Muawiyah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ammar bin Umair, on the authority of Abu Muammar, on the authority of Abu Masoud said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A prayer is not sufficient, and a man does not straighten his cross while bowing. And prostration."
"37449","(37449) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Ali bin Yahya bin Khallad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his uncle, He was Badriya. He said: We were sitting with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when a man entered and was praying, and he prayed a short prayer. He did not complete bowing or prostration, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, looked at him without even noticing. He prayed, then came and greeted him. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, replied to him and said: Repeat, for you have not prayed. So he did that. Thirdly, all of this says: Repeat, for you have not prayed."
"37450","(37450) Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Al-Miswar bin Makramah. ; He saw a man who could not complete his bowing or prostration, so he said to him: Repeat, but he refused, so he did not leave him until he repeated it.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: It is sufficient, but he was wrong."
"37451","(37451) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Rafi’ ibn Khadij, who narrated it, saying: Whoever plants in the land A people without their permission. His expenses were returned to him, but he did not have any of the crops."
"37452","(37452) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Abu Ja’far al-Khutami, who said: My uncle sent me and a boy of his to Sa’id. Ibn Al-Musayyab, and he said: What do you say about the farms? He said: Ibn Umar did not see any harm in it, until he narrated a hadith about it: that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came Banu Harithah, and he saw crops in the land of Zahir, and they said: It is not Zahir. He said: Is not the land the land of Zahir? ? They said: Yes, but he farmed so-and-so. He said: Return his expenses and take your crops. Rafi’ said: So we took our crops and returned them. She has to spend on it.\n - It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: He uproots his crops."
"37453","(37453) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id, and Haram bin Sa’d; The she-camel of Al-Bara’ bin Aazib entered a wall and caused harm to them, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ruled: That he be preserved. Wealth is the responsibility of its owners by day, and the property of livestock is the responsibility of the livestock at night."
"37454","(37454) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Issa, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Haram bin Muhayisya, on the authority of Al-Bara’; A she-camel of the Al-Baraa family spoiled something, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, decided that it was up to her family to protect the wealth. By daylight, and the people of livestock are responsible for what their livestock spoiled by night. (Ibn Majah 2332. An-Nasa’i 5786)"
"37455","(37455) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad (h) and on the authority of Ibn Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; A sheep ate dough, and the other said: It was spun by day, so he invalidated it and recited: {When the people’s sheep scattered therein}"
"37456","(37456) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Tariq, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; A sheep entered upon a weaver and spoiled his spinning, so Al-Sha’bi was not liable for what it spoiled by fire.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: He guarantees you."
"37457","(37457) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Abi Yazid, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Siba’ ibn Thabit, on the authority of Umm Kurz, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Two sheep on the boy’s behalf, and a sheep on the slave-girl’s behalf, it will not harm you. Whether they are male or female."
"37458","(37458) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Habib Ibn Misra, on the authority of Umm Kurz, on the authority of The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: On behalf of the boy, two mature sheep, and on the behalf of the female slave, one sheep."
"37459","(37459) Shababi told us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Muslim, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, performed aqāt on behalf of Al-Hasan and Al-Husayn."
"37460","(37460) Muhammad bin Bishr al-Abdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: The boy is pledged for his aqeeqat, which will be slaughtered for him on the seventh day, and his head will be shaved. And he is called.\n It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: If he does not perform an aqeeqah on her behalf, then there is nothing wrong with him in that."
"37461","(37461) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: None of you should prevent your brother from placing a piece of wood on his wall. Then Abu said Huraira: Why do I see you turning away from it? By God, I will throw it between your shoulders.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: He does not have that."
"37462","(37462) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of Amr ibn Khuzaymah, on the authority of Amara ibn Khuzaymah, on the authority of Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said regarding the pillar: three stones. There is no return in it."
"37463","(37463) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Salman, he said: He said: Some of the polytheists said to him and they mocked him: “Indeed, your companion teaches you even nonsense.” Salman said: Yes, we commanded. That we should not face the Qiblah, nor seek refuge with our faith, nor be satisfied without three stones from which there is no return. And no bone."
"37464","(37464) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: He came out The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in need, so he said: Seek for me three stones, so I brought him two stones and dung. So he took the two stones and threw away the dung, and said: It is rubbish.\n - It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: This is not sufficient until he performs ablution if more than three stones remain after the three stones. The amount of a dirham."
"37465","(37465) Abd al-Aziz bin Abd al-Samad al-Ammi told us, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is no divorce except after marriage, and there is no emancipation except after possession. (Abu Dada 2184, Ahmed 189)"
"37466","(37466) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Saad, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: No. Divorce except after marriage."
"37467","(37467) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, on the authority of someone who heard a peacock saying: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: There is no divorce except after marriage."
"37468","(37468) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra, on the authority of al-Nazzal ibn Sabrah, on the authority of Ali He said: There is no divorce except after marriage.\n It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: If he swears to divorce her, then marries her, she will be divorced."
"37469","(37469) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ja’far bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided with an oath and a witness. He said: Ali judged it before you."
"37470","(37470) Zaid bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Saif bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided with an oath and a witness."
"37471","(37471) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Siwar, on the authority of Rabi’i, who said: I said to him: What is the name of a witness and the right hand of the student? He said: It was found in Saad’s books."
"37472","(37472) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Abul Zinad; Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote to Abdul Hamid: to judge by oath with the witness.\n Abu Al-Zanad said: A sheikh from their sheikhdom, or from their elders, told me; Shurayh ruled that."
"37473","(37473) Yahya bin Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bai, on the authority of Husayn, who said: Abdullah bin Utba was judged. With the testimony of a witness, and the oath of the student.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: This is not permissible."
"37474","(37474) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: Whoever sells a slave and has money, his money goes to the seller, unless the buyer makes a stipulation."
"37475","(37475) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salmah ibn Kuḥayl, on the authority of someone who heard Jabir ibn Abdullah say: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever sells a slave and has money, his money belongs to the seller, unless the buyer stipulates."
"37476","(37476) Hatim bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, he said: Ali said: Whoever sells a slave and has money, his money is his. To the seller, unless the buyer stipulates, this was decided by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"37477","(37477) Abd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Abd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: : Whoever sells a slave who has property, his property belongs to his master, unless the one who bought him makes a stipulation."
"37478","(37478) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Ata’, and Ibn Abi Mulkiah, saying: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever sells a slave, his property belongs to the seller, unless the buyer makes a stipulation, saying: I will buy him. From you and your money\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: If the slave’s wealth is more than the price, that is not permissible."
"37479","(37479) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Aroub, on the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The period of a slave’s period is three days. (Ahmad 1521 Hakim 21)"
"37480","(37480) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is no promise above Four (Ibn Majah 2245. Ahmed 143)"
"37481","(37481) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, who said: He only made Ibn Al-Zubair promised the slave three times, according to what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Munqidh bin Amr: Say: No, if you You made a sale, then you have three options. (Bukhari 2117, Abu Dawud 3494)"
"37482","(37482) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, who said: I heard Aban bin Othman, And Hisham bin Ismail teaches the covenant regarding the slave: fever, and the stomach for three days, and the covenant is a year in Insanity and leprosy.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: If they separate, he has no right to return it unless there is a defect in it."
"37483","(37483) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Ride the sacrificial animal in a reasonable manner, until you find a back."
"37484","(37484) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a man driving his body, and he said: Ride it. He said: It is his body, he said: Ride it, even if it is fat."
"37485","(37485) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a man He drove his body, and he said: Ride it. He said: Is it a body? He said: Ride it."
"37486","(37486) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: A man said to Ibn Abbas: Shall we ride the body? He said: Not heavy. He said: So you milk it? He said: Not Mujahid."
"37487","(37487) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of the one who narrated to him, on the authority of Anas, who said: Ride it, he said: It is His body, he said: Ride it."
"37488","(37488) Abu Malik al-Janabi told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ali, who said: He rides his camel. With kindness.\n It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: Do not ride it unless its owner suffers hardship."
"37489","(37489) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata’ (h) and on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Muadh bin Sa’wah, On the authority of Sinan bin Salamah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him regarding the voluntary gift: He must not eat, for if he eats, he will be fined."
"37490","(37490) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Omar, who said: Whoever gives a sacrifice voluntarily and it is defective, we will slaughter him. He left the sanctuary and did not eat from it, but if he did eat from it, he must replace it."
"37491","(37491) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Tayyah, on the authority of Musa bin Salamah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent eighteen people with a man, and instructed him to do what he commanded about them, so he set off, then He returned to her and said: What do you think if any of it creeps up on us? He said: Slaughter it, then dip its sandal in its blood, then place it on its surface, and do not eat from it, you or anyone else. From the people of your company."
"37492","(37492) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Najiya Al-Khuza’i, who said: I said: O Messenger of God, What do we do with what is damaged in the body? He said: Slaughter him, dip his sandals in his blood, and leave him alone among the people, so that they may eat him.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: The people of companionship eat from it."
"37493","(37493) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Safwan bin Umayyah was one of the freedmen, so he came to the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he mounted his camel and placed his cloak on it, then he stepped aside to fulfill his need. Then a man came and stole So he took it and brought it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he ordered that his hand be cut off. He said: O Messenger of God. Do you cut it in a cloak? I love it. He said: So come before you bring it to me."
"37494","(37494) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Tawus, who said: It was said to Safwan bin Umayyah, and he is at the highest level. Mecca: There is no religion for the one who does not emigrate, so he said: By God, I will not reach my family until I come to Medina. So he came to Medina. So he descended upon Al-Abbas, and he lay down in the mosque, with his khamisah under his head. Then a thief came and stole it from under his head. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: This is a thief, so he ordered him to be cut off, and he said: Let him go, so he said: No, he accepted. To bring it to me.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: If he gives it to him, the punishment will be avoided."
"37495","(37495) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar; He prayed upon his camel and performed the Witr prayer upon it. He said: And the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to do that."
"37496","(37496) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Abbad bin Mansour, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He performed the Witr prayer, and he said: The Witr prayer is performed on a camel."
"37497","(37497) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Thuwair, on the authority of his father; That Ali used to pray Witr on his camel."
"37498","(37498) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, he said: Al-Hasan did not see any harm in a man performing Witr on his camel."
"37499","(37499) Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Omar bin Nafi’; That his father used to pray the Witr prayer for a camel."
"37500","(37500) Amr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Rawwad, on the authority of Musa ibn Uqba, who said: I accompanied Salim but lagged behind him. On the road, he said: What left you? So I said: I performed Witr. He said: So let him take care of your camel?\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: It is not sufficient for him to pray the Witr prayer for her."
"37501","(37501) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Malik ibn Anas, on the authority of Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talha al-Ansari, on the authority of Hamidah Ibn Ubaid Ibn Rafi’, on the authority of Kabsha Ibn Ka’b, and she was under one of the descendants of Abi Qatada; She poured water for Abu Qatada with which he could perform ablution, and then a cat came to drink, so the vessel listened to her, so I began to look. He said: O my nephew, do you wonder? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It is not impure. It is from those who go around you, or from the circumambulations."
"37502","(37502) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Abu Qatada used to bring the animal closer to the animal. He rinses it, then performs ablution with his question."
"37503","(37503) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: A cat is one of the household’s belongings."
"37504","(37504) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Rukain, on the authority of Safiyya Ibn Dab, who said: I asked Hussein bin Ali about the cat? He said: He is from Ahl al-Bayt."
"37505","(37505) Al-Bakrawi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, who said: A woman hurried while performing ablution for Abu Al-Ala, so he performed ablution. Thanks to her\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said that he hated the feline’s secrets."
"37506","(37506) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Qais Al-Awdi, on the authority of Al-Huzayl bin Shurahbil Al-Awdi, On the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’ba: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, urinated, then performed ablution, and wiped over his socks and sandals."
"37507","(37507) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, who said: I saw a wet Ali standing, then he performed ablution and wiped On her sandal."
"37508","(37508) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Zaid; That Ali urinated and wiped on his sandals."
"37509","(37509) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Ukil, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafali; That Ali urinated and wiped his sandals."
"37510","(37510) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Ata’, on the authority of Aws bin Abi Aws, on the authority of his father, he said: I was with My father came to some water from the Bedouins, so he performed ablution and wiped over his sandals. I told him about that, and he said: I will not add more to you. As I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, do."
"37511","(37511) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Wasil, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abdullah bin Dirar; Anas bin Malik performed ablution and wiped over two socks from my socks."
"37512","(37512) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed, on the authority of Khalas, who said: I saw Ali conceited in Al-Rahba. Then he wiped over his socks and sandals.\n It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa disliked wiping over socks and sandals, unless they were underneath them. Skins"
"37513","(37513) Yazid told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed; That Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban informed him, on the authority of Ibn Muhayriz al-Qurashi, that he informed him, on the authority of Al-Mukhdajji, A man from the Banu Kinanah, who told him that a man from the Ansar was in the Levant and was nicknamed Abu Muhammad, and he had He accompanied him and told him that the Witr prayer is obligatory, so Al-Mukhdaji mentioned that he went to Abbad bin Al-Samit and told him, so he said His servants: Abu Muhammad lied. I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: Five prayers that God has ordained for His servants. He brought them without losing any of their rights. He came and has a covenant with God that He will admit him to Paradise. And whoever detracts from their rights, He came and had no covenant with God. If He wished, He would punish him, and if He wished, He would admit him to Paradise."
"37514","(37514) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muslim, a client of Abd al-Qais, who said: A man said to Ibn Umar: Have you seen? Witr, is it Sunnah? He said: What is your age? The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed the Witr prayer, and the Muslims performed the Witr prayer. He said: No, is it Sunnah? He said: Do you understand? The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed the Witr prayer, and the Muslims performed the Witr prayer."
"37515","(37515) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, on the authority of Ali, who said: He was told: Is Witr obligatory? He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed the Witr prayer, and the Muslims remained steadfast in it."
"37516","(37516) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, he said: Ali said: The string is not Definitely like the written prayer."
"37517","(37517) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: The Sunnah of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He performed the Witr prayer, just as he did for breaking the fast and the sacrifice."
"37518","(37518) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The Witr is a Sunnah."
"37519","(37519) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; He was asked about a man who forgot the Witr prayer. He said: It does not matter, as if it was an obligatory prayer."
"37520","(37520) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He did not consider Witr to be obligatory."
"37521","(37521) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ata’, and Muhammad bin Ali, who said: The sacrifice and the Witr prayer. Our age\n It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: Witr is obligatory."
"37522","(37522) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Jabir ibn Samarra, who said: It belonged to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Two sermons, between which he sits, recites the Qur’an and reminds the people."
"37523","(37523) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to deliver a sermon. He stands, then sits, then gets up and delivers two sermons."
"37524","(37524) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Salih, the client of the twins, who said: Marwan succeeded Abu He came to Medina, and he used to lead us in congregational prayer, delivering two sermons and sitting for two sessions.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: He should not sit except once."
"37525","(37525) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Saad bin Sa’id, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim al-Taymi, on the authority of Qais bin Amr, He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a man praying two rak’ahs after the morning prayer, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He said: Did he perform the Fajr prayer twice? The man said: I had not prayed the two rak'ahs before, so I prayed them now, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, remained silent. May God bless him and grant him peace."
"37526","(37526) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; That a man prayed the morning prayer with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, finished the prayer, he stood up. The man prayed two rak'ahs, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: What are these two rak'ahs? He said: O Messenger of God, I came while you were praying, and I had not prayed the two rak’ahs before dawn, so I thought that I prayed them while you were praying, and when I finished the prayer, I got up and prayed them. He said: He did not command him, nor did he forbid him."
"37527","(37527) Hushaym told us, he said: Musami bin Thabit told us, he said: I saw an Ata’ who did the same thing."
"37528","(37528) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: If he missed the two rak’ahs of Fajr, they prayed after Fajr prayer."
"37529","(37529) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, who said: I heard Al-Qasim saying: If I prayed them until I prayed Fajr, I prayed them after sunrise."
"37530","(37530) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He prayed the two rak'ahs of Fajr after the sacrifice.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: He does not have to pay them off."
"37531","(37531) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade praying between people. Graves"
"37532","(37532) Hafs told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, who said: Omar saw me praying to a grave, so he started saying: Oh. Anas, the grave, so I started raising my head to look at the moon, and they said: Rather, he means the grave."
"37533","(37533) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: He does not pray until The grave"
"37534","(37534) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Ala, on the authority of his father and Khaythamah, who said: He should not pray facing the wall of a bathroom or in the middle. Cemetery"
"37535","(37535) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Al-Hasan Al-Arni, who said: The entire earth is mosques except three: The graveyard, the bathroom, and the courtyard."
"37536","(37536) Hafs and Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Anas; He disliked having the funeral prayer performed in the grave."
"37537","(37537) Gandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to hate to pray. Between the graves.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: If he prays, his prayer is sufficient."
"37538","(37538) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, narrating, he said: I have exceeded your command. About the truthfulness of horses and slaves."
"37539","(37539) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar, on the authority of Aarak bin Malik, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was informed of this. He said: A Muslim has no obligation regarding his slave, nor his horse. He spoke the truth"
"37540","(37540) Hatim bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Ibn Arak, he said: I heard my father saying: I heard Abu Hurairah saying: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is no charity owed to a believer regarding his slave or his horse."
"37541","(37541) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Khaled, on the authority of Shubil ibn Awf, and he had caught up with the Jahiliyah, He said: Omar bin Al-Khattab ordered the people to give charity, so the people said: O Commander of the Faithful, our horses and our slaves, impose upon us ten Ten times, he said: As for me, I am not imposing that on you."
"37542","(37542) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: It is not upon the invading horse. For the sake of God, charity."
"37543","(37543) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, who said: Saeed bin Al-Musayyab was asked: Did Al-Barathin give the truth? He said: Should the horse be repaid in charity?"
"37544","(37544) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Osama, on the authority of Nafi’; Omar bin Abdul Aziz said: There is no charity in horses."
"37545","(37545) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: There is no zakat in horses or slaves, except the zakat of the fitrah.\n It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: If there are horses in which there are males and females and their offspring are sought, then there is truth in them."
"37546","(37546) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he raised him up, he said: When he believes The reader believed, so whoever’s assurance coincides with the assurance of the angels, his previous sins will be forgiven."
"37547","(37547) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdul-Jabbar bin Wa’il, on the authority of his father, he said: I prayed with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when he said: {Not those with anger upon them, nor those who go astray}, he said: Amen."
"37548","(37548) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salamah, on the authority of Hajr ibn Anbas, on the authority of Wa’il ibn Hajr, who said: I heard The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited: {And not those who go astray}, and said: Amen, extending his voice with it.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: The imam does not raise his voice in “Amen” and those behind him say it."
"37549","(37549) Hushaym told us, Khalid told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Ibn Umar; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The night prayer is twofold, the Witr prayer is one, and two prostrations before sunrise. Fajr"
"37550","(37550) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: The night prayer is two by two, so if you fear the dawn, perform your rak’ah Witr."
"37551","(37551) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: The night prayer is two by two, so if you fear the dawn, perform Witr with a rak’ah, to perform Witr for your previous prayer."
"37552","(37552) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, the client of the family of Talha, on the authority of Abu Salama, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say the salutation in every two rak’ahs of the night prayer."
"37553","(37553) Yazeed narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Raja’i, on the authority of Qubaisyah ibn Dhu’ayb, who said: Abu He saw me while I was praying, and he said: Separate, but I did not know what he said, so when I left, I said: What should I separate? He said: Separate the night prayer from the day prayer."
"37554","(37554) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Amr, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, he said: In every Two rak'ahs of prayer."
"37555","(37555) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Omar ibn al-Walid, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Indicate a salutation between every two rak’ahs."
"37556","(37556) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Dinar, on the authority of Salem; He said: The night prayer is two by two."
"37557","(37557) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: The night prayer is two by two, and the Witr A rak'ah at the end of the night.\n - It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: If you wish, you may pray two rak’ahs, and if you wish, four rak’ahs, and if you wish, six rak’ahs, do not separate them."
"37558","(37558) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Ibn Umar; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The Witr is one."
"37559","(37559) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: If you fear dawn, perform the rak’ah Witr prayer."
"37560","(37560) Hushaym told us, Hajjaj told us, about Ata’; That Mu'awiyah performed the rak'ah Witr prayer, but that was denied to him, so Ibn Abbas was asked about it, and he said: He followed the Sunnah."
"37561","(37561) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Saad, on the authority of his father; He used to pray Witr in a rak'ah, and he was told? He said: I only kept it short."
"37562","(37562) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, who said: I asked Ata’: Should I perform the rak’ah Witr prayer? He said: Yes, if you wish."
"37563","(37563) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Samar Ibn Masoud, and Hudhayfy at Al-Walid bin Uqba, then they went out and fought each other, and when the morning came, each one of them bowed as he bowed."
"37564","(37564) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: : The night prayer is two by two, so if you fear dawn, pray Witr with one. (Muslim 164. Ibn Majah 1320)"
"37565","(37565) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith; Abu Bakr used to pray Witr with one rak’ah, and he would speak between the two rak’ahs and the last rak’ah."
"37566","(37566) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: The Witr rak’ah is performed at the end of the night."
"37567","(37567) Marhum narrated to us, on the authority of Asal bin Sufyan, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He performed the rak'ah Witr prayer."
"37568","(37568) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: The family of Saad and the family of Abdullah used to say the salaam in two rak’ahs. The Witr, and they perform the Witr with a rak’ah."
"37569","(37569) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Saeed and Nafi’, who said: We saw Muadh the reader greeting In the two rak'ahs of Witr."
"37570","(37570) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Al-Hasan used to say the salaam in the two rak’ahs of Witr.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: It is not permissible to perform Witr with one rak’ah."
"37571","(37571) Abdullah bin Mubarak and Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abi Al-Malih, on the authority of his father, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the skins of wild beasts. Yazid said: That they be spread out. \n(Tirmidhi 1770 and Abu Dawud 4129)"
"37572","(37572) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; Ibn Masoud borrowed an animal, and it was brought to him wearing a pack of tigers. He took it off and mounted it."
"37573","(37573) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Hakam, who said: I asked Al-Hakam about tiger skins? He said: The skins of wild beasts are disliked."
"37574","(37574) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hikam; Omar wrote to the people of the Levant forbidding them to ride on the skins of lions."
"37575","(37575) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Zaid Al-Rashk, on the authority of Abu Al-Malih, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade He spared the skins of wild beasts from being spread. (Tirmidhi 1771 and Abd al-Razzaq 215)"
"37576","(37576) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ali; He hated praying in fox skins.\n It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: There is no harm in sitting on it."
"37577","(37577) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to deliver a sermon, and he said: To the people: Sit down. Abdullah bin Masoud heard him while he was at the door, so he sat down and said: O Abdullah, come in."
"37578","(37578) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, who said: My father and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came. He was giving a sermon, so he stood in front of him in the sun, so he ordered it to be done and he was turned into the shade."
"37579","(37579) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, who said: They used to greet the imam while he was on the pulpit, and he would respond."
"37580","(37580) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: They used to ask the imam for permission. While he was on the pulpit, when Ziyad was present and this was increasing, he said: Whoever puts his hand on his nose, it is his ear."
"37581","(37581) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: Salik Al-Ghatfani came, and the Prophet prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace, he delivered a Friday sermon, and he said to him: Did you pray? He said: No, he said: Pray two rak'ahs, and you will pass through them.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: The imam does not speak to anyone during his sermon."
"37582","(37582) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hisham bin Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Kinanah, on the authority of his father, who said: One of the princes sent me to Ibn Abbas to ask him about rain, and Ibn Abbas said: What prevented him from asking me? The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went out humbly, humbly humbled, supplicating, and praying, and prayed two rak’ahs as he prays in Eid, and he did not propose this engagement to you."
"37583","(37583) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: We went out with Abdullah bin Zayd al-Ansari. We asked for water, so he prayed two rak'ahs, and Zaid bin Arqam succeeded him."
"37584","(37584) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Hilal; Omar bin Abdul Aziz testified that he started praying for rain before the sermon. He said: And he asked for rain and wrapped his robe around it."
"37585","(37585) Shabab bin Siwar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abbad bin Tamim, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Zayd, who was one of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, the day he went out to draw water, so he turned his back to the people, praying, and received He kissed him, then changed his robe, then prayed two rak’ahs, reciting them aloud and reciting them aloud.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: The rain prayer should not be performed in congregation, nor should a sermon be given during it."
"37586","(37586) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Harith bin Ayyash bin Abi Rabi’ah, on the authority of Hakim bin Hakim bin Abbad bin Hanif, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr bin Mut’im, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Gabriel approached me at the House twice, and he led the evening prayer with me when twilight had passed, and he led with me Tomorrow is evening, a third of the first night, and he said: This time is the time of the prophets before you, the time between these two times."
"37587","(37587) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Badr bin Othman, he heard it from Abu Bakr bin Abi Musa, on the authority of his father; That a questioner came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him about the times for prayer, but he did not answer him anything, then he ordered Bilal performed the last night prayer when twilight fell, then he prayed the night prayer the next third of the night, then he said: Where is the one who asked about the time? There is time between these two times."
"37588","(37588) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Kharijiyah ibn Abdullah ibn Sulaiman ibn Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: He narrated to me. Hussein bin Bashir bin Salman, on the authority of his father, said: Muhammad bin Ali and I entered Jabir bin Abdullah, and we said to him: Tell us how was the prayer with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, led the evening prayer for us when twilight had set, then the next day he led the evening prayer for us when a third of the night had passed. The night"
"37589","(37589) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Safiyya Ibn Abi Ubaid; Omar ibn al-Khattab wrote to the army commanders setting the time for prayer for them. He said: Pray the evening prayer when twilight sets. You have been busy, so what is between you and a third of the night? Do not be distracted from prayer, for whoever sleeps after that will not May God rest his eyes, saying it three times."
"37590","(37590) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Isha time until a quarter of the night.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: Isha time until midnight."
"37591","(37591) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id; The Qasamah existed during the pre-Islamic period, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, approved it regarding a murdered Ansar who was found in He collected the Jews. He said: So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, started with the Jews and assigned them fifty shares. She said: The Jews: We will not swear. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to the Ansar: Will you swear? The Ansar said: We will not swear, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, fined the Jews his blood money because he was killed in front of them."
"37592","(37592) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: Omar bin Abd al-Aziz called me and asked me about Al-Qasamah, and he said: It seemed to me that I should return it, for the Bedouin is witnessing, and the absent man will come and witness, so I said: O Commander of the Faithful, you will not be able to reject it. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the caliphs after him have decreed it."
"37593","(37593) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed bin Ubaid Al-Tai, on the authority of Bashir bin Yasar; A man from the Ansar, called Saul bin Abi Hatham, told him that a group of his people had gone to Khaybar. So they dispersed there and found one of them dead, so they said to those who found him: You killed our companion. They said: We did not kill. We did not know of a killer. He said: So they went to the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Prophet of God, we have gone to Khaybar. Then we found one of us dead, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Pride, pride. So he said to them: You will bring the clear evidence. Who killed? They said: We do not have anything between us. He said: So they will swear to you. They said: We are not satisfied with the faith of the Jews. The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, disliked it. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him to stop his bloodshed, so he ransomed him with a hundred camels of charity."
"37594","(37594) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather; Huwaysiyya and Muhaysiyya, the sons of Masoud, and Abdullah and Abdul Rahman, the sons of so-and-so, went out to meet in Khaybar. Then Ali Abdullah was attacked and killed. He said: They mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Do you swear by fifty and are you entitled to it? They said: O Messenger of God, how can we take an oath if we do not bear witness? He said: Will the Jews acquit you? They said: O Messenger of God, when the Jews kill us? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, paid tribute to him from his presence."
"37595","(37595) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders; That Suleiman bin Yassar said: The Qasamah is a right, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided for it, while the Ansar were at The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when a man came out of them, then they left from the presence of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and then They found their companion covered in his blood, so they returned to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: The Jews killed us. They named a man from among them, but they had no proof of evidence, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to them: Two witnesses from Other than you, until I gave it to you in its entirety, but they had no proof of it, so he said: Be entitled to fifty shares. Should I hand it over to you in its entirety? They said: O Messenger of God, we hate to take an oath in the absence. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wanted to take The Jews divided it with fifty of them, and the Ansar said: O Messenger of God, the Jews do not care about swearing, whenever We accept this from them. They come to the last of us, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, greeted him from his presence.\n It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: The oaths of those who claim blood will not be accepted."
"37596","(37596) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Babah, on the authority of Jubair bin Mut’im, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; He said: O Banu Abd Manaf, do not prevent anyone from circumambulating this House and praying for any hour, day or night."
"37597","(37597) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I saw Ibn Umar circumambulating the Kaaba after dawn, He prayed two rak'ahs before sunrise."
"37598","(37598) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I saw Ibn Omar and Ibn Abbas circumambulating after the afternoon prayer and praying."
"37599","(37599) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abu Shuabi; He saw Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein approaching Mecca, so they circumambulated the Kaaba after the afternoon prayer and prayed."
"37600","(37600) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Juma’, on the authority of Abu Tufayl; He used to circumambulate after the afternoon prayer and pray until the sun became yellow."
"37601","(37601) Ali told us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Ata’, he said: I saw Ibn Umar and Ibn Al-Zubayr circumambulating the Kaaba before Fajr prayer, then they prayed two rak’ahs before sunrise.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: He should not pray until he sets or rises, and prayer is permitted."
"37602","(37602) Abdullah bin Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed bin Yazid, who said: I heard Khaled bin Abi Imran, narrating on the authority of Hanash, on the authority of Fadalah bin Ubaid, who said: On the day of the news of the news, he, may God bless him and grant him peace, brought necklaces with beads strung on them. With gold, a man bought it for seven dinars, or nine dinars, and it was brought to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he mentioned That is for him. He said: No, until you distinguish what is between them. He said: I only wanted the stones. He said: No, until you distinguish what is between them. He said: He separated him until he distinguished him."
"37603","(37603) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Anas, who said: The letter of Omar came to us while we In the land of Persia: Don’t you sell swords with silver rings on them for a dirham?"
"37604","(37604) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, he said: Shurayh was asked about a gold collar with stones in it. He said: The cloves are removed, then the gold is sold weight for weight."
"37605","(37605) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Muhammad; He disliked buying a local sword unless it was an accident."
"37606","(37606) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; He used to hate buying a sword decorated with silver, and he would say: Buy it with gold, hand in hand.\n It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: There is no harm in buying it with dirhams."
"37607","(37607) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Hilal Al-Wazzan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace, if he missed four prayers before noon, he prayed after them."
"37608","(37608) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If he missed four days before noon. Pray after her."
"37609","(37609) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of a man from Banu Awud, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, who said: Whoever missed four before noon, then let him pray it after the two rak’ahs.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: He does not perform her prayer or make up for it."
"37610","(37610) Shabab bin Siwar narrated to us, on the authority of Laith bin Saad, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ka’b bin Malik; That Jabir bin Abdullah told him; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to gather the two men who had killed someone in one grave, and he ordered that they be buried. With their blood, and he did not pray over them, and they were not washed."
"37611","(37611) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Usama ibn Zayd, on the authority of Az-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas, who said: When the Uhud, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by Hamza, who had been mutilated and mutilated, and said: If you had not found Safiyya, I would have left him. Until God gathers him from the bellies of wild beasts and birds, and does not bless any of the martyrs, and says: I am a witness over you. Today\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: May the blessings of God be upon the martyr."
"37612","(37612) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Hassan bin Bilal, who said: I saw Ammar bin Yasir performing ablution. And he trimmed his beard, so I said to him? He said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, do it."
"37613","(37613) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Aamir bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, who said: I saw Uthman performing ablution. He mixed his beard three times, then said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, doing it."
"37614","(37614) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to comb his beard."
"37615","(37615) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Hamza, he said: I saw Ibn Abbas combing his beard."
"37616","(37616) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ma’n, who said: I saw a man combing his beard."
"37617","(37617) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to comb his beard."
"37618","(37618) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Omar ibn Sulaym al-Baili, on the authority of Abu Ghalib, who said: I saw a father in front of him. He performed ablution three times, trimmed his beard, and said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, do that."
"37619","(37619) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, Hassan bin Salih narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Aisha, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Yazid Al-Raqqashi, on the authority of Anas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, grew his beard."
"37620","(37620) Waki’ told us, Al-Haytham bin Jamaz told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Aban, on the authority of Anas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Gabriel came to me and said: When you perform ablution, rinse your beard.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa did not consider perming the beard."
"37621","(37621) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abdul Rahman bin Abza, on the authority of his father, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite in the Witr verses: {Glorify the name of your Lord Most High}, and {Say, O The disbelievers}, and {Say, “Allah is One.”"
"37622","(37622) Muhammad bin Abi Ubaidah narrated to us, my father narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Dhar, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abd al-Rahman bin Abza, on the authority of Ubayyah, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray Witr with: {Glorify the name of your Lord Most High}, and {Say, O disbelievers}, and {Say God is One}"
"37623","(37623) Shababi told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray Witr with three times, reciting in them: {Glorify the name of your Lord Most High}, and {Say, O O you disbelievers}, and {Say: He is God, One}"
"37624","(37624) His youth told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited the prayer with: {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High}.\n It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa disliked singling out a surah to be recited in Witr prayer."
"37625","(37625) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Rafi’, who said: He was appointed successor. Marwan Aba Hurairah came to Medina and went out to Mecca, so Abu Hurairah led us in prayer in congregation, and he recited a surah. The plural in the first prostration, and in the last prostration: (When the hypocrites come to you)"
"37626","(37626) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of people from the people of Medina, among whom I saw Abu Ja’far. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite in congregation the surahs of the congregation and the hypocrites. As for the surah of the congregation: So he gives good tidings to the believers and encourages them, and as for the Surah of the Hypocrites: he comforts the hypocrites with it and rebukes them."
"37627","(37627) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Al-Muntashir, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Habib bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Numan Bin Bashir; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite during the two Eids and in the Friday prayers: {Glorify the name of your Lord Most High}, and {Has the hadith of al-Ghashiya reached you?} And when the two vows come together on a day, it is recited between them."
"37628","(37628) Waki` narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin al-Muntashir, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Habib Bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Bashir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; Similar to the hadith of Jarir."
"37629","(37629) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ma’abad bin Khalid, on the authority of Zaid, on the authority of Samarra, he said: It was The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited in congregation: {Glorify the name of your Lord Most High}, and {Has the hadith of the cheater reached you}."
"37630","(37630) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Damra bin Sa’id, who said: I heard Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah bin Utba, He says: Omar went out on the day of Eid, and he asked Abu Waqid Al-Laythi: What did the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, recite about this? Today? He said: With: (Q) and (I approached).\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa disliked that a surah be designated for Friday and the Eid days."
"37631","(37631) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, Muhammad bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Subaq, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Sahl Ibn Hanif, he said: I used to shed a lot of precum, and I used to wash from it frequently, so I mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Only one ablution is sufficient for you. He said: I said: O Messenger of God, how about what befalls you? My dress? He said: Only a handful of water is sufficient for you to sprinkle on your garment wherever you see that it has reached it."
"37632","(37632) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: If a man commits sexual intercourse with his clothes If he sees traces on it, let him wash it. If he sees no traces on it, let him sprinkle water on it."
"37633","(37633) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: A man from the neighborhood said to Abu Misra: I am in a state of junub. My dress, so I look and see nothing? He said: If you take a bath and wrap yourself in it while you are wet, that will be sufficient for you."
"37634","(37634) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who has a wet dream while wearing a garment but does not know where his position is. He said: The garment is sprinkled with water."
"37635","(37635) Mahboub Al-Qawariri narrated to us, on the authority of Malik bin Habib, on the authority of Salem, who said: A man asked him, and he said: I am having a wet dream. In my dress? He said: Wash it. He said: It was hidden from me. He said: Sprinkle it with water."
"37636","(37636) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Zayd ibn al-Salt; Omar sprinkled what he did not see."
"37637","(37637) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: If you go astray, sprinkle with water.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: He should not sprinkle it, nor should he add water to it, except that it is evil."
"37638","(37638) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: Salik Al-Ghatfani came. And the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was giving a Friday sermon, and he said to him: Did you pray? He said: No, he said: Pray two rak'ahs, and you will complete them."
"37639","(37639) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: If you come on the day of Friday prayer and the imam is delivering the sermon, then... If you wish, you may pray two rak'ahs, and if you wish, you may sit."
"37640","(37440) Azhar told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Al-Hasan used to come while the imam was delivering the sermon and pray two rak’ahs."
"37641","(37641) Hushaym told us, Mansour, Abu Hurriyah, and Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He came as a companion. Al-Ghatafani, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, delivered the Friday sermon, and he did not pray the two rak’ahs, so he commanded him The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was required to pray two rak’ahs, during which he passed them.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: He does not pray."
"37642","(37642) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Zainab, the son of Umm Salama, on the authority of Umm Salama, She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: You are disputing before me, and perhaps some of you will be more sensitive to your argument than... Some, but I only judge between you according to what I hear from you. For whomever I have decreed anything of his brother’s rights, do not He took it, I only cut out for him a piece of fire, and he will bring it on the Day of Resurrection."
"37643","(37443) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rafi’, on the authority of Umm Salamah, who said: Two men came from The Ansar disputed to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, regarding inheritances between them. You have studied, but not between them. Clearly, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: You dispute with me, but I am only human, and perhaps some of you He will be more consistent with his argument than some of them, but I will only judge between you. For whomever I have decreed anything of his brother’s rights, then do not He took it, but I cut for him a piece of the Fire, and he will bring it with it on the Day of Resurrection. She said: Then the two men cried. And each one of them said: My right to my brother, O Messenger of God. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: As for what you did, So go, divide yourselves, and strive for what is right, then ask each other, then let each one of you make his companion lawful."
"37644","(37644) Muhammad bin Bishr al-Abdi narrated to us, Muhammad bin Amr narrated to us, Abu Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: We are only human, and perhaps some of you are more sensitive to your argument than others. I have fulfilled for him the right of his brother, so I am only severing a piece of Hell for him.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: If two false witnesses testified before a judge against a man that he divorced his wife, then he would make a difference. The judge agreed between them, based on their testimony, that it was okay for one of them to marry her."
"37645","(37645) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever changes his religion, kill him."
"37646","(37446) Hafs bin Ghayath, Abu Muawiyah, and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murra, on the authority of Stolen, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It is not permissible to shed the blood of a Muslim man who bears witness that there is no god but God, and I am the Messenger of God, except with one of three: the married adulterer, a life for a life, and the one who abandons his religion and separates from the community."
"37647","(37647) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said regarding an apostate: She must be asked to be repented, if she repents, otherwise She killed you"
"37648","(37648) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: You shall be killed."
"37649","(37649) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hammad, who said: You will be killed.\n - They mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: She shall not be killed if she apostatizes."
"37650","(37650) Hushaym told us, Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Bakra, he said: The sun or the moon was eclipsed. At the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: Indeed, the sun and the moon are two signs of God, and they will not be diminished by the death of anyone. from the people, so if that is the case, then pray until you are cleared."
"37651","(37651) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, who said: So-and-so bin so-and-so; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The solar eclipse is one of the signs of God, so if you see it, be terrified. Prayer"
"37652","(37652) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ata`, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The verses prayer is six rak’ahs with four prostrations."
"37653","(37653) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah; If you are frightened by one of the horizons of the heavens, then hasten to prayer."
"37654","(37654) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim ibn Abi al-Najjoud, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, on the authority of al-Nu`man ibn Bashir; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed in an eclipse similar to your prayers, bowing and prostrating.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: He should not pray during a lunar eclipse."
"37655","(37655) Hushaym told us, Abu Al-Zubair told us, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abd God, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, occupied the polytheists on the Day of the Trench with four prayers. He said: So he ordered Bilal, and he gave the call to prayer. He stood and prayed the noon prayer, then he stood up and prayed the afternoon prayer, then he stood up and prayed the sunset prayer, then he stood up and prayed the evening prayer."
"37656","(37456) Zaid bin Harun told us, Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Saeed Al-Khudri, on the authority of his father, said: We were imprisoned on the day of the ditch for noon, afternoon, sunset, and evening prayers. Until that is sufficient for us, and that is the saying of God, Blessed and Most High: {And God is sufficient for the believers from fighting, and God is Powerful. Mighty}, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and ordered Bilal, so he stood up and prayed the noon prayer as he had prayed before. That is, then he stood up and prayed the afternoon prayer as he had prayed it before that, then he stood up for the sunset prayer, so he prayed it as he had done it before. He prayed for her before that, then he performed the evening prayer, and he prayed for her as he used to pray for her before that, and that was before that. He revealed: {Then if you fear, then on foot or mounted}"
"37657","(37657) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he heard Malik bin Aws bin Al-Hadathan say: I heard Omar, He says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Righteousness for righteousness is usury, except for a sin, and barley for barley is usury, except"
"37658","(37658) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, on the authority of Abu al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Ubadah ibn The silent one, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Barley for barley, like for like, hand to hand."
"37659","(37659) Waki’ narrated to us, Ismail bin Muslim Al-Abdi narrated to us, Abu Al-Mutawakkil Al-Naji narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sa’id. Al-Khudri said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Wheat for wheat, and barley for barley, like for like, hand to hand.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa used to say: There is no harm in selling the absent wheat in exchange for the present wheat."
"37660","(37660) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Habashi bin Junadiya, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: Charity is not permissible for a rich person, nor for a straight person."
"37661","(37661) Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: It is not permissible to give charity to a rich person, nor to someone who is bitter."
"37662","(37662) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Rayhan bin Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It is not permissible to give charity to a rich person, nor to a straight man.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa permitted giving charity to him, and said: It is permissible."
"37663","(37663) Yahya bin Zakaria bin Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Jabir; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: I took your camel for four dinars, and you can take it back to Medina. (Muslim 1224, Ahmad 397)"
"37664","(37644) Yahya bin Zakariya narrated to us, on the authority of Zakariya, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Jabir, who said: He was sent by him. With a Uqiyah, and I left his lambs to my family, so when I reached Medina, I went to him, and he criticized me and said: Do you think it is just Did I harass you to take your camel and your money? So what is yours?\n - They mentioned that Abu Hanifa did not see him."
"37665","(37645) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman bin Al Harith bin Hisham, on the authority of Abu Hurairah ; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever finds his belongings with a bankrupt man, he has more right to them.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: He is the worst of fines."
"37666","(37646) Abu Osama told us, Ubaid Allah bin Umar told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, treated the people of Khaybar with half of the crops or fruits that they brought forth. (Muslim 1186)"
"37667","(37667) Ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, dealt with the people of Khaybar fairly."
"37668","(37668) Ismail bin Aliya told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah bin Muhammad bin Ammar, On the authority of Al-Walid bin Abi Al-Walid, on the authority of Urwah bin Al-Zubayr, he said: Zayd bin Thabit said: May God forgive Rafi’ bin Khadij Two men came to him who had fought, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If this is your situation, do not rebel. Farms"
"37669","(37669) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Al-Muhajir, on the authority of Musa bin Talha, who said: No, my neighbor, I have seen him. He gives his land for a third and a quarter: Abdullah and Saad."
"37670","(37670) Fudayl bin Iyad narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: Mu’adh came upon us and we were to give our land for a third. And the half, and that did not bother us."
"37671","(37671) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Harith ibn Husayriyah Al-Azdi, on the authority of Sakhr ibn Walid, on the authority of Amr ibn Sali`a, on the authority of Ali, said: There is no harm in farmers receiving half.\n It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa hated that."
"37672","(37672) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, he heard Jabir say, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: No. He sells a present to a country."
"37673","(37673) Waki’ narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: He does not sell a present person to a remote person."
"37674","(37674) Waki’ narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Salih the guardian of the twins, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: A present person cannot be sold to a remote person. (Ahmed 481)"
"37675","(37675) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: A present person cannot be sold to a remote person. (Bukhari 2723. Muslim 1033)"
"37676","(37676) Waki’ narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus bin Ubaid, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Anas, he said: We forbade That a slave should be sold to Babad, even if he is his brother to his father and mother."
"37677","(37677) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Muslim Al-Khattab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah and Ibn Umar, one of them said: No, The other said: A present person should not be sold to a past person.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa permitted it."
"37678","(37678) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ziyad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah; The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw Al-Hasan bin Ali taking some dates from the charity, and he licked them in his mouth, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: K-k-k-k-k-k-k-k-k-k-k-k-k-k-k-k-k-k-k-k-k-k-k-k-k-k-k-k-k."
"37679","(37679) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Ibn Abi Rafi’; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent a man from Banu Makhzum to Al-Sadaqah, and Abu Rafi’ wanted to follow him, so he asked The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Did you not know that it is not permissible for us to give charity, and that the people’s master is from themselves?"
"37680","(37680) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, Zuhair narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Issa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Abu Layla, he said: I was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he got up and entered the House of Charity, and the boy entered with him. He means Hassan, or Hussein, so he took dates and put them in his mouth, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, took them out and said: : Indeed, charity is not permissible for us."
"37681","(37681) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, Ma’rif narrated to us, Hafsiya Ibn Talaq, a woman from the neighborhood, narrated to me. Ninety, on the authority of my grandfather, Abu Umayra Rashid bin Malik, who said: I was with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sitting at one time. One day, a man came with a plate of dates on it, and he said: What is this, charity or Hadiya? So the man said: Rather, he spoke the truth, so he presented them to the people, while Al-Hasan was rotting in his hands, so he took some dates and put them in his mouth. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, looked at it and inserted his finger into it, then spoke with it, then said: We are the family of Muhammad. We do not eat charity."
"37682","(37682) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sharik, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulkiah; That Khaled bin Saeed bin Al-Aas sent to Aisha with cows, and she returned them and said: We, the family of Muhammad, do not eat charity."
"37683","(37683) Zaid bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Hussein bin Waqid, who said: Abdullah bin Buraydah narrated to me, on the authority of his father; When Salman came to Medina, he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a gift on a plate, and placed it among His hand, and he said: What is this? So he reminded him of his heroism."
"37684","(37684) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of Anas; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, found a date and said: If it were not for you being charitable, I would have eaten you.\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: Charity is permissible for the clients of Banu Hashim and others. (Muslim 752. Abu Dawud 1449)"
"37685","(37685) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered He entered the mosque of Banu Amr bin Awf and was praying in it, and men from the Ansar entered it, and Suhayb entered with them, so I asked Suhayb: How did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, do wherever he greeted him? He said: He used to gesture. With his hand\n - It was mentioned that Abu Hanifa said: He does not do it."
"37686","(37686) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Amr bin Yahya bin Amara, on the authority of his father On the authority of Abu Saeed, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is no truth in less than five times."
"37687","(37687) Abu Asama narrated to us, saying: Al-Walid bin Kathir narrated to me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Sa`sa’. On the authority of Yahya bin Amara and Abbad bin Tamim, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, says: There is no charity on anything less than five wasqs of dates. (Ibn Majah 1793. Bayhaqi 134)"
"37688","(37688) Ali bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Mubarak, on the authority of Muammar, he said: Suhail narrated to me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: There is no truth in anything less than five times.\n - It was reported that Abu Hanifa said: In a few things it is narrated, but in a lot of it it is truthful. (Ahmed 402 and Abd al-Razzaq 7249)"
"37689","(37689) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Ismail, he said: Sa`id bin Jubayr told me, he said: Abu Kassum, the companion of Abyssinia, had an elephant with him. When he reached the sanctuary, he blessed the elephant, but it refused to enter the sanctuary. He said: So when he is faced with a return, he hastens to return, and when he is returned to the Sanctuary he refuses, then he sends small white birds to them, in Their mouths are stones like chickpeas. They do not fall on anyone but they are destroyed."
"37690","(37690) Abu Asama said: Abu Makin told me, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: So I shaded them from the heavens, so when God made them Like a consuming storm, God sent rain, which poured with them until He took them to the sea."
"37691","(37691) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; {Ababil birds} He said: They had hoses like those of birds, and paws like the paws of dogs."
"37692","(37692) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, who said: Black birds carry The stones with their beaks and nails."
"37693","(37693) Al-Hasan bin Musa told us, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Yahya, he said: Abu Salamah told me that Abu He told him; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rode his camel and delivered a sermon, and said: God has withheld the elephant from the place of his place, and has given power to Peace be upon her, his Messenger and the believers. (Bukhari 112. Muslim 989)"
"37694","(37694) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umayr, he said: When God wanted He destroyed the companions of the elephant. He sent upon them birds raised from the sea like hawks, each bird carrying Three stones in pieces: two stones in his feet, and a stone in his beak. He said: It came until it lined up over their heads. Then it shouted and dropped what was in its legs and beaks. Not a stone falls on a man’s head without it coming out of his back, and it does not fall. On some part of his body, but it came out from the other side. He said: And God sent a strong wind, and it hit the stones and increased it. Severely, he said: So destroy them all."
"37695","(37695) Abu Asama told us, he said: Mujalid told us, he said: Amir told us, he said: Omar went to Jews, and said: I adjure you. God, who sent down the Torah to Moses, do you find Muhammad in your books? They said: Yes. He said: What prevents you from following him? They said: Indeed, God has not sent a messenger except that he had one of the angels as a guarantor, and indeed Gabriel is the guarantor of Muhammad, and he is the one who He comes to Him, and He is our enemy from among the angels, and Michael makes us safe. If Michael were the one who He comes to us and accepts Islam. He said: I adjure you by God who sent down the Torah to Moses. What have you sent down from the Lord of the worlds? They said: Gabriel is on his right and Mikael is on his left. Omar said: I bear witness that they will not descend except by God’s permission. Michael would not make peace with the enemy of Gabriel, and Gabriel would not make peace with the enemy of Michael.\n While he was with them, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and said: This is your companion, Ibn Al-Khattab, so he stood up. To him, so he came to him, and it had been revealed to him: {Whoever is an enemy of Gabriel - it is He who has sent it down to your heart, by the permission of God} His saying: {For God is an enemy to the unbelievers}"
"37696","(37696) Qarad Abu Nuh narrated to us, saying: Yunus bin Abi Ishaq informed us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abi Musa, on the authority of His father, he said, Abu Talib went out to the Levant, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and elders from Quraysh went out with him. They looked over the monk, landed and unhitched their saddlebags, and the monk came out to them. Before that, they were passing by him but he did not come out. To them and he did not turn around. He said: They are dismounting, so he began to penetrate them until he came and took the hand of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. Then he said: This is the Master of the Worlds. This is the Messenger of the Lord of the Worlds. This is the Messenger of God, may God have mercy on him. To the worlds, and the sheikhs of Quraysh said to him: What did he teach you? He said: When you approached Al-Aqaba, not a tree or a stone remained but it fell down in prostration, and they do not prostrate except to a prophet, and I I will recognize him by the seal of the Prophethood, lower than the cartilage of his shoulder, like an apple.\n Then he came back and made food for them, and when he brought it to them while he was in the camel pasture, he said: Send for him, and he came. And upon him are clouds that shade him. He said: Look at him, upon him are clouds that provide shade. So when he approached the people, he found that they had preceded him. To the tree, and when he sat down, the tree leaned towards him and said: Look at the tree, he leaned towards him.\n He said: While he was standing over them and imploring them not to take him to the Romans, for if the Romans had seen him They recognized him as a group and killed him. He turned and saw that nine people of the Romans had come from the Romans. He met them and said: He did not come. How much? They said: We have come, because this prophet is leaving this month, and there is no way left except that people have been sent to him, and we We told him his story, so we were sent to this path of yours. He said to them: Have you not left behind you anyone who is better than you? They said: No, we only told him about this path of yours. He said: Have you seen a matter that God wanted to accomplish? Can He be able to do it? Did any of the people respond? They said: No. He said: So they followed him and stayed with him.\n So he came to them and said: I adjure you by God, who of you is his guardian? Abu Talib said: I am. He continued to appeal to him until Abu Talib rejected him, and Abu Bakr sent Bilal with him and provided him with supplies. The monk of cakes and oil. (Tirmidhi 3420, Hakim 615)"
"37697","(37697) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; Indeed, there was no tribe of the jinn except that they had seats for listening. He said: And when the revelation came down, the angels heard a voice. Like the sound of iron that you threw on Al-Safa. He said: When the angels heard it, they fell down in prostration, and did not raise their heads until It descends, and when it descends, they say to one another: What did your Lord say? If it is from what is taking place in the heavens, they will say: The Truth, and He is the Most High, the Great. And if it is from what is taking place on earth, The unseen, or death, or something that will happen on earth that they spoke about, and they said: It will be such-and-such, and you will hear it. Satans, and they send it down to their friends.\n When God sent Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, they were defeated by the stars, and the first to know about them was Thaqif, who was the one with the sheep. Some of them go to his sheep and slaughter a sheep every day, and the one with the camels slaughters a camel every day, so the people hastened to Their money, so some of them said to one another: Do not do it, for if the stars by which you are guided are there, otherwise it is a matter that has happened. So they looked, and behold, the stars by which he was guided were as they were, and nothing of them was thrown at them. So they restrained themselves, and God sent away the jinn. So they heard the Qur’an, and when they attended it, they said: Listen. He said: And the devils went to Satan, so they informed him, and he said: This An event happened on earth, so bring me soil from every land. When they brought him the tihama soil, he said: Here is the event."
"37698","(37698) Abdullah bin Idris, Abu Asama, and Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Amr bin Muriya, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Salamah, on the authority of Safwan bin Assal, said: A Jew said to his companion: Take us to this prophet, and he said His companion: Do not say prophet, for if he had heard you, he would have four eyes. He said: So come to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him and asked him about nine clear signs, so he said: “Do not associate anything with God, do not commit adultery, do not steal, and do not kill.” The soul which God has forbidden except in truth, and do not take an innocent person to a person of authority and let him kill him, and do not make magic, and do not consume usury, And do not slander chaste women, and do not turn to flee on the day of the advance, and specially upon you are the Jews: Do not transgress on the Sabbath. He said: So they accepted. His hands and feet, and they said: We bear witness that you are a true prophet. He said: What prevents you from following me? They said: Indeed, David prayed that there would never cease to be a prophet in his descendants, and we fear that the Jews will kill us. (Ahmad 2391 Hakim 10)"
"37699","(37699) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: It was revealed to The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was forty years old, then he stayed in Mecca for thirteen years, and he was He spent ten years in Medina, then he was arrested when he was sixty-three years old."
"37700","(37700) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Hisham, who said: Al-Hasan said: It was revealed to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, was forty years old. He stayed in Mecca for ten years and in Medina for ten years."
"37701","(37701) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: Shaiban narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Aisha, And Ibn Abbas; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, remained in Mecca for ten years, while the Qur’an was revealed to him, and in Medina for ten years.\n(Bukhari 4444, Ahmed 296)"
"37702","(37702) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Ammar, a client of Banu Hashim, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet passed away. May peace and blessings be upon him, who is sixty-five years old."
"37703","(37703) Abdou bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed; The Qur’an was revealed to the Prophet, may the peace and blessings of God be upon him, when he was forty-three years old, and he stayed in Mecca ten times, and in Medina. Ten years ago, and he died when he was sixty-three years old."
"37704","(37704) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ammar, a client of Banu Hashim, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent when he was forty years old, and he stayed in Mecca for fifteen days, and in Medina ten, and he was arrested. He is sixty-five years old."
"37705","(37705) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Al-Ala bin Salih narrated to us, saying: Al-Minhal bin Amr narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id Ibn Jubayr, that a man came to Ibn Abbas and said: The Prophet, may the peace and blessings of God be upon him, was sent down ten in Mecca and ten in Medina, and he said: Whoever says that, ten, sixty-five and more verses were revealed to him in Mecca."
"37706","(37706) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was revealed to him when he was forty years old, and he stayed in Mecca for thirteen years. He lived in Medina for ten years, and he died when he was sixty-three."
"37707","(37707) Khalid bin Mukhlid told us, he said: Suleiman bin Bilal told us, he said: Rabi’ bin Abi Abd al-Rahman told me, He said: I heard Anas bin Malik saying: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent at the head of forty, and he stayed in Mecca ten. And in Medina ten, and he died at the age of sixty."
"37708","(37708) Affan told us, he said: Wahib told us, he said: Khaled Al-Hadha’ told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq; That a man asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: When were you a prophet? He said: I was a prophet and Adam was between the soul and the body. (Ahmed 66. Ibn Abi Asim 2918)"
"37709","(37709) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad bin Al-Hadd, who said: It was revealed Gabriel looked at the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he felt sad and then said to him: Read. He said: What should I read? He said: He felt sad, then he said to him: Read. He said: What should I read? He said: {Recite in the name of your Lord who created}, so he went to Khadija and told her what he saw, so she came to Warqa bin Nawfal and mentioned That was for him, so he said to her: Has your husband seen his companion in the presence of you? She said: Yes, he said: Your husband is a prophet and calamity will befall him among his nation."
"37710","(37710) Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Misra; Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, appeared, he would hear someone calling to him: O Muhammad. When he heard the voice, he would run away. Then he came to Khadija and mentioned that to her, and he said: O Khadija, I was afraid that something had gotten into my mind. When I stand out, I hear someone calling, but I don’t see anything, so I run away, and then he is with me calling me. She said: God would not do that to you, for you did not know how to believe the hadith, fulfill trusts, and maintain family ties. God would not have done that. To do that to you.\n So she confided that to Abu Bakr, and he was sorry for her in the pre-Islamic period, so Abu Bakr took it by the hand and set off. He brought it to his paper, and he said: What is that? So he told him what Khadija had told him, so he came to Waraqa and mentioned that to him, and Waraqa said: Do you see anything? He said: No, but when I stand out, I hear the call, but I don’t see anything, so I run away. If he is with me, he said: Don’t do it. So, when you hear the call, stand still until you hear what he says to you.\n When he emerged, he heard the call: O Muhammad. He said: Here you are. He said: Say: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant. And His Messenger, then he said to him: Say: {Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, Master of the Day of Judgment} until he finished his Fatihah The book, then he came to Waraqiya and mentioned that to him, and Waraqayyah said to him: Give good news, then give good news, then give good news, for I bear witness. Indeed, you are the Messenger whom Jesus, peace be upon him, was given good tidings about: {A Messenger will come after me, whose name is Ahmed}, so I bear witness that it is you Ahmad, and I bear witness that you are Muhammad, and I bear witness that you are the Messenger of God, and you will soon be ordered to fight, and if you are commanded to fight And while I am alive, I will fight with you, and Warqa died, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I saw the priest in Paradise, may God bless him and grant him peace. Green clothes."
"37711","(37711) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: God sent the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he greeted once to admit a man to Paradise. He said: He passed by one of the Jewish churches, and he entered into them while they were reciting. Their book, and when they saw him, they closed the book and left, and on one side of the church was a dying man. He said: So he came to him. He said: He only prevented them from reciting that you had come to them while they were reciting that you called a prophet, and he called you. Then he came to the journey. So he opened it, then read, and said: I bear witness that there is no god but God, and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, then he was arrested, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: He is your brother. He said: So they washed him, shrouded him, and embalmed him, then he prayed upon him."
"37712","(37712) Yunus bin Muhammad told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Gabriel came to him while he was playing with the boys, so he took him and struck him, so he broke his limb. He turned it over, so he extracted the heart, then he extracted a clot of clots from it, and said: This is Satan’s share of you, then he washed it in a golden basin. With a hundred Zamzam waters, then to his mother, then he returned it to its place. He said: And the boys came running to his mother, meaning his back. They said: Muhammad has been killed. He said: So they received him while he was stained. Anas said: I could see the traces of the stitches on him. His chest (Muslim 1471, Ahmad 121)"
"37713","(37713) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsa, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Jabir, who said: He withheld revelation from the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, at the beginning of his command, and he made private rooms beloved to him, so he made himself alone in private women. While he was coming from Hira’, he said: I saw something above me, so I raised my head, and I saw something on a chair. When I saw him, I ran to the ground and came to my family quickly, and I said: Cover me, cover me. Then Gabriel came to me and made He says: {O you Muddathathir, arise and warn, and your Lord, so exalt, and purify your clothes, and abstain from disgrace}. (Bukhari 3238, Muslim 143)"
"37714","(37714) Abd al-A’la ibn Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Ikrimah, regarding his saying: {O ye al-Muddaththir}, He said: You have gathered up this matter, so do it. (Ibn Jarir 124)"
"37715","(37715) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Dhiyal bin Harmala, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: It was gathered Quraysh one day, and they said: Look, who is the most knowledgeable of you in magic, divination, and poetry. Let this man who divided our group come. He has distorted our affairs and disgraced our religion, so let him speak to him and see what he will respond to. They said: We do not know anyone except Utba bin Rabia, and they said: You, Abu Al-Walid. Then Utbah came to him and said: O Muhammad, are you better, or Abdullah? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, remained silent, and then\nHe said: Are you better, or Abdul Muttalib? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, remained silent and said: If you claim that these people are better than you, then they have worshiped gods. Which you criticized, and if you claim that you are better than them, then speak so that we may hear what you say. By God, we have never seen him alone. He was more disgraceful to his people than you, you divided our group, you scattered our affairs, you disgraced our religion, and you disgraced us among the Arabs, to the point that you disgraced them. There is a sorcerer among the Quraysh, and there is a soothsayer among the Quraysh, and by God, we only wait like the days of a pregnant woman, for some of us to rise up. To each other with swords until we are cut to pieces.\nO man, if it is only yours, then choose any of the wives of Quraysh and we will marry you ten; Al-Hajjah, we have gathered together for you until you are the richest man of Quraysh. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Have you finished? He said: Yes, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited: In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful {Ham is a revelation from the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful} until it reached: {If Turn away, and say, “I warn you of a thunderbolt like the thunderbolt of Ad and Thamud.” Then Utba said to him: “It is enough for you. It is enough for you. You have nothing else.” This? He said: No, so he returned to the Quraysh, and they said: What is behind you? He said: I did not leave out anything that I thought you were talking to him about unless I spoke to him about it. They said: Did he answer you? He said: Yes;\nHe said: No, by the One who made it clear, I did not understand anything of what he said, except that he warned you of a thunderbolt like the usual thunderbolt. And Thamud, they said: Woe to you, a man speaks to you in Arabic and you do not know what he said. He said: No, by God, I did not understand anything of what he said. Other than mentioning the thunderbolt. (Abdullah bin Hamid 1123. Abu Ali 1812)"
"37716","(37716) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Aas, he said: I did not see Quraysh wanted to kill the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, except one day when they conspired against him while they were sitting in the shade of the Kaaba, and the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was praying at the shrine, then Uqba bin Abi Mu’it stood up to him and put his robe around his neck. Then he pulled him until he reached his knees and fell, and the people shouted and thought that he had been killed, so Abu Bakr came and rallied. Until he seized the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, behind him with his frog, and he said: “Will you kill a man because he says, ‘My Lord? Allah}? Then they turned away from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.\n So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and prayed. When he finished his prayer, he passed by them while they were sitting in the shade of the Kaaba, and he said: O people of Quraysh, by the One in whose hand is Muhammad’s soul, I have not been sent to you except for slaughter, and he pointed with his hand to He shaved him, he said: Then Abu Jahl said to him: O Muhammad, you were not ignorant, he said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: You are one of them. (Abu Yali 7301)"
"37717","(37717) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Ikrim, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Abu Jal passed by and said: Pain. Did he break it? Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, rebuked him, and Abu Jahl said to him: Why did you rebuke me, Muhammad? By God, you know that there is no man who is more vocal than you. He said, so Gabriel said: {Then let him call his caller} He said, then Ibn Abbas said: By God, if he had called his caller, the harlots would have taken him. The torment. (Tirmidhi 3349. Ahmad 329)"
"37718","(37718) Ja`far ibn Aoun told us, he said: Sufyan informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Masoud, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray in the shade of the Kaaba. He said: Abu Jahl and some people said Quraysh, and camels were slaughtered in the vicinity of Mecca. He said: So they sent and brought some of her baskets, so they threw him on top of him. He said: So she came. Fatimah until she threw him away from him. He said: Then he used to recite three times, saying: O God, grant you the reward of Quraysh. O God, grant you the reward of Quraysh. By the Quraysh, O God, bless you by the Quraysh: by Abu Jal bin Hisham, Utbah bin Rabi’ah, and Shayba bin Rabi’ah. Al-Walid bin Utba, Umayyah bin Khalaf, and Uqba bin Abi Muait.\n He said: Abdullah said: I saw them killed in the heart of Badr. Abu Ishaq said: I forgot the seventh. (Bukhari 2934, Muslim 1419)"
"37719","(37719) Abu Asama told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, he said: Abbad told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: When Abu Talib fell ill, a group of Quraysh came to see him, and among them was Abu Jahl. He said: They said: Your nephew is insulting you. Our machine, and he does and does, and says and says, and if I were sent to him, he forbade him, so he was sent to him, or said: he came The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the house, and between him and Abu Talib a man was sitting. He said: Then Abu Jal was afraid. If the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sat next to Abu Talib, seeking to be more gentle with him, then he jumped up and sat there. The sitting, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not find a sitting near his uncle, so he sat at the door.\n Abu Talib said: O my nephew, why do your people complain about you? They claim that you insult their gods, and you say and say, and do and do. He said: So they used a lot of language against him. He said: Then the Prophet spoke. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: O uncle, I want them to have one word that they say, and by which you will be obligated to them. The Arabs, and you give them the non-Arab tribute. He said: They were frightened by his speech and his words. He said: So the people said: Speak to him. One, yes, and your father and ten, and what? Abu Talib said: What word did he say, my nephew? He said: There is no god but Allah. He said: Then they stood up and were terrified, shaking off their clothes, and they said: {Make the gods one god. This is a wondrous thing. He said: And he read from this place to his saying: {When they will taste the torment}"
"37720","(37720) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Yazid bin Ziyad told us, he said: Abu Sakhrah Jami’ bin Shaddad told us, On the authority of Tariq Al-Muharbibi, he said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the market of Dhul-Majaz, and I was in the market. Sell it, he said: Then he passed by, wearing a red robe, and he was calling out in a loud voice: O people, say there is no god but May God grant you success, and a man follows him with stones, his ankles and ankles have turned bloody, and he says, “O people! Do not obey him, for he is a liar. He said: I said: Who is this? They said: This is a boy of Banu Abdul Muttalib. I said: Who is this who follows him and throws stones at him? They said: His uncle is Abdul-Ezza, and he is Abu Lahab. (Bukhari 1491 Hakim 2311)"
"37721","(37721) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: : I have been harmed for the sake of God and no one is harmed, and I have been harmed for the sake of God and no one is afraid, and three things have come upon me from among A day and a night, and Bilal and I have no food that any living person would eat except what Bilal’s armpits saw to him."
"37722","(37722) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Mundhir, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafiyyah; In his saying: {And they will bear their burdens, and burdens with their burdens} He said: Abu Jahl and the Quraysh pawns used to receive When people come to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, they say hello, they say: He forbids alcohol, and he forbids adultery. And what the Arabs used to do is forbidden, so return, for We will bear your burdens. So these verses were revealed: {And they will bear Their burdens}"
"37723","(37723) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was wounded in the face, his quads were broken, and he threw a stone at his shoulder, so he made He wipes the blood from his face and says: How can a nation succeed that did this to its Prophet while he is calling them to God? Then God revealed: “You have nothing of the matter, or turn to them, or punish them, for they are wrongdoers.” (Tirmidhi 3002. Ahmed 201)"
"37724","(37724) Abu Asama told us, Mujalid told us, on the authority of Amir, who said: Quraysh said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: You were a prophet, as you claim, so set these two mountains at a distance of four or five days’ journey from Mecca. Indeed, it is a hardship until we plant and graze therein, and raise for us our fathers from the dead so that they may speak to us and inform us that you Prophet, and carry us to the Levant, or to Yemen, or to Al-Hira, until we go and come in a night, as You claimed that you had done it, so God revealed: {And if it were a Qur’an with which the mountains were moved, or the earth was divided with it, or with which The dead}"
"37725","(37725) Al-Hasan bin Musa Al-Ashhab narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salma narrated to us, saying: Thabit narrated to us, on the authority of Anas; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I have been brought with Buraq, which is a white animal that is better than a donkey and less than a mule. He placed his hoof at its end, so I rode him, and he walked with me until I came to the Holy House, and I tied the animal to the ring. which the prophets used to associate with it. Then I entered and prayed two rak’ahs in it, then I went out and Gabriel brought me a vessel. Of wine and a vessel of milk, so I chose milk, and Gabriel said: You have become unwell.\n He said: Then he ascended with us to the lowest heaven, and Gabriel asked for prayers, and it was said: Who are you? He said: Gabriel. It was said: And who is with you? He said: Muhammad, so it was said: He was sent to him? He said: It was sent to him, and it was opened for us, and behold, I was with Adam. He welcomed and prayed well for me, then he took us up to the second heaven. Then Gabriel asked for the prayer, and it was said: Who are you? He said: Gabriel, then it was said: And who is with you? He said: Muhammad, so it was said: He was sent to him? He said: It was sent to him, and it was opened for us, and then I saw my cousin Yahya and Isa. They welcomed me and prayed well for me.\n Then he took us to the third heaven, and Gabriel asked for the door to be opened, and it was said: Who are you? He said: Gabriel,It was said: Who is with you? He said: Muhammad. They said: He was sent to him? He said: It was sent to him, and it was opened for us, and behold, I was with Joseph, and behold, he had been given half of good deeds, so he welcomed and prayed for him. Fine, then he took us up to the fourth heaven, and Gabriel asked for the prayer, and it was said: Who are you? He said: Gabriel, then it was said: And who is with you? He said: Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. They said: He was sent to him? He said: It was sent to him, so it was opened for us, and behold, I was with Idris. He welcomed me and prayed well for me. Then he said: God says: {And We raised him to a high place}"
"37726","(37726) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, on the authority of Malik bin Sa`sa’, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; In a similar way to it, or similar to it. (Bukhari 3207, Muslim 149)"
"37727","(37727) Dhudha bin Khalifa told us, he said: Awf told us, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, he said: Ibn Abbas said, he said The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: When I was taken captive that night, I was in Mecca in the morning. He said: I was appalled by his situation. And I knew that the people were lying to me, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sat isolated and sad, then Abu Jahl passed by him, and he came Until he sat next to him and said as if he was mocking: Was there anything wrong with him? He said: Yes, he said: What is it? He said: Take me away for the night. He said: Where? He said: To the Holy House. He said: Then you were in front of us in the morning? He said: Yes, but he did not think that he would be a liar, for fear that he would deny the hadith if he called his people to him. He said: Should I speak to your people? What did you tell me if I invited them to you? He said: Yes, he said: Come on, the people of Banu Ka'b bin Luayyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyām. He said: Then the gatherings broke up, so they came until they were seated. To them, he said: Tell your people what you told me.\n The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I was taken on a journey during the night. They said: Where? He said: To the Holy House. They said: Then you appeared among us in the morning? He said: Yes, he said: Who among those who applaud, and who among those who place his hand on his head in astonishment tell lies, he claimed, and they said: Can you? Will you designate the mosque for us? He said: Among the people are those who traveled to that country and saw the mosque. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: So I went and said: To them, and I continued to pronounce and pronounce, until I became confused about some of the epithet, so I came to the mosque and I was looking at it, until it was put without Dar Uqayl, or Dar Aqal, so I described him while I was looking at him, and the people said: As for the description, by God, he was right."
"37728","(37728) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Hudhafi bin Al-Yaman; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought with Buraq, a tall white animal, placing his hoof at its end. He and Gabriel said: He and Gabriel did not move until they came to the Holy House, and the gates of heaven were opened to them. He saw Paradise and Hell.\n He said: And Hudhayfy said: He did not pray in the Holy House. Zirr said: So I said: Yes, he prayed. Hudhaifi said: What is your name, O Bald? I know your face, but I do not know what your name is? He said: I said: Zurr bin Hubaysh, he said: So he said: How do you know? And do you find him praying? He said: I said: God says: {Glory be to Him who took His servant by night from the Sacred Mosque to the Far Mosque. We have blessed Turn him around so that we may show him of Our signs. Indeed, He is the All-Hearing, the All-Seeing. He said: And do you find him praying? If he had prayed in it, we would have prayed in it, just as we pray in the Sacred Mosque, and it was said to Hudhayf: And he tied the animal to the ring. What are the prophets associated with? Hudhayf said: Was he afraid that she would go, and God had given her to him?"
"37729","(37729) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salma narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd bin Jud’an, on the authority of Abu Al-Salt, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I saw the night when I was taken on a captivity, when we had finished To the seventh heaven, and I looked above me, and behold, there was thunder, lightning, and lightning bolts. He said: And I came upon a people whose stomachs were like houses. In it are snakes seen from outside their bellies, so I said: Who are these, O Gabriel? He said, “These are the people who consume usury.” When I descended to the lowest heaven, I looked down at something and saw a tower, smoke, and sounds. So I said: What is this, O Gabriel? He said: These devils hover over the eyes of the children of Adam. They do not think about the kingdom of the heavens and the earth. Otherwise, they would see Wonders (Ibn Majah 2273. Ahmad 353)"
"37730","(37730) Al-Hasan bin Musa told us, he said: Hammad bin Salma told us, he said: Suleiman Al-Taymi and Thabit Al-Bunani told us, On the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I came to Moses on the night he was taken captive by the Red Hill. And he is standing and praying in his grave. (Muslim 1650, Ahmad 148)"
"37731","(37731) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salama, on the authority of Ali ibn Zayd, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: One night I was taken on captivity among a people whose lips were being cut with scalds of fire, so I said: Who? These? It was said: These are preachers from the people of the world, from those who used to command people to be righteous but forget themselves while they follow The Book, will they not then understand? (Ahmad 120, Abu Ali 3983)"
"37732","(37732) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, he said: When he was captured By the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, an animal was brought above the donkey and below the mule, placing its hoof at its tip. It is said to him: Buraq, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by a camel for the polytheists, and it fled, and they said: O these, what This? They said: We do not see anything, it is only a smell, until he came to the Holy House, and two vessels were brought; In one was wine, and in the other was milk, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, took the milk, and Gabriel said to him: You have been guided. And your nation has been guided.\n Then he went to Egypt."
"37733","(37733) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When You came to the sidra. When its leaves were like the ears of an elephant, and when its leaves were like the ears of a goat, then it was covered by the command of God. What changed, it changed, and I mentioned rubies."
"37734","(37734) Ibn Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhail, on the authority of Ghazwan, he said: Sidrat al-Munta is patient. Heaven"
"37735","(37735) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Al-Hasan Al-Arni, on the authority of Dhail bin Sharhabeel, on the authority of Abdullah; In his saying: (Sidrāt al-Muntaha) he said: The patience of the jinn, meaning its middle, on it are the virtues of Sundus and Istabraq."
"37736","(37736) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Misra, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: Sidră The final destination is the command of every prophet and angel."
"37737","(37737) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Salem bin Abi Al-Jaad, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to present himself to the people in a situation. He says: Is there a man who will introduce me to his people? So the Quraysh have?? They prevented me from conveying the word of my Lord. He said: Then a man from Hamadan came to him and said: Who are you from? He said: From Hamdan. He said: Is there anything forbidden by your people? He said: Yes, he said: So the man left, then he was afraid that his people would fear him, so he returned to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I will go and present myself to my people, then I will come to you from Qabil. Then he went and delegations of the Ansar came in Rajab. (Bukhari 157, Tirmidhi 2925)"
"37738","(37738) Waki` ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, saying: Shu`ba narrated to us, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, he said: I came to Ibrahim, So I asked him? He said: The first to convert to Islam was Abu Bakr."
"37739","(37739) A sheikh of ours told us, he said: Mujalid told us, on the authority of Amir, he said: I asked, or Ibn Abbas was asked: Which of the people were Is it the beginning of Islam? He said: Did you not hear Hassan bin Thabit say:\nIf you remember something from your brother, trust him.\nSo remind your brother Abu Bakr of what they did.\nThe best of human beings are the most pious and just.\nExcept the Prophet, and he fulfilled what was burdened.\nAnd the second, the next, is the praised one.\nAnd the first of the people among them to believe the Messengers"
"37740","(37740) Abu Asama told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwah told us, he said: My father told me, he said: Abu Bakr converted to Islam. On the day he converted to Islam, he had forty thousand dirhams."
"37741","(37741) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The first to demonstrate Islam were seven people: the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, and Abu Bakr, and Bilal, and Kabbab, and Sahib, and Ammar, and her name was Umm Ammar, as for the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace, so his uncle prevented him, and as for Abu Bakr, his people prevented him, and the others were taken and put on iron armor, then They fasted in the sun, until the effort of every one of them reached its limit, so they gave them what they asked for, so he came to every man of them. He made his people carry water on their sides, and they threw them into them, then they were carried on their sides, except for Bilal. When it was evening, Abu Jahl came and started cursing and cursing at a beautiful woman, then he stabbed her and killed her. He was the first martyr to be martyred in Islam. Except for Bilal, for he was distressed by God until they were bored, so they put a rope around his neck, then they ordered their boys to So they marched with him between the two woods of Mecca, and he began to say: “One, One.”"
"37742","(37742) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid; Like him (Ibn Abi Asim 280)"
"37743","(37743) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, he said: They were given what they asked for, except for a messenger, so they made them stick together. Its back was flattened, until the water of its surface was gone."
"37744","(37744) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, who said: Abu Bakr, meaning Bilal, was bought. For five uqiyahs, and he was buried with stones. They said: If you had refused to pay more than an uqiyah, we would have sold him. He said: If you had refused only A hundred ounces I would have taken it."
"37745","(37745) Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Qays, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, who said: Khabab was one of the immigrants. And he was among those who were punished by God."
"37746","(37746) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Kurdous saying: Indeed, Khabab bin Al-Art converted to Islam sixth. Six, he had one-sixth of Islam."
"37747","(37747) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Laila al-Kindi, he said: Khabbab came To Omar, he said: Come closer, for I do not find anyone more deserving of this assembly than you except Ammar. He said: Then Khabab began to show him traces of It appears from what the polytheists tortured you with."
"37748","(37748) Yahya bin Abi Bukair told us, he said: Zayed told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The first to demonstrate their Islam were seven: the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Abu Bakr, Ammar, and his mother Sumayyah. And Sahib, Bilal, and Al-Miqdad. As for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, God prevented him because of his uncle Abu Talib. Abu Bakr, so God protected him from his people, and as for the rest of them, the polytheists took them and dressed them in iron armor. And they fasted in the sun, and there was not one of them who did not give them what they wanted, except Bilal, for he was distressed by his soul. God, and He treated his people with contempt, so they gave him children, and they began to circumambulate him around the streets of Mecca, and he said: One, one, one."
"37749","(37749) Shababā told us, he said: Shu’bā told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Abu Hamza, the client of the Ansar, on the authority of Zaid bin Arqam said: The first to convert to Islam with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"37750","(37750) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Salem, who said: I said to Ibn al-Hanafiyyah: Abu Bakr was the first of the people to convert to Islam? He said: No, I said: Why did Abu Bakr excel and preceded, so that no one is mentioned except Abu Bakr? He said: He was the best of them in Islam when he converted to Islam until he joined his Lord."
"37751","(37751) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Layya’, he said: Zayd bin Amr Al-Ma’afiri informed me, he said: I heard Abu Thawr al-Fahmi says: Abd al-Rahman ibn Udays al-Balawi came to us, and he was one of those who pledged allegiance under the tree, so he went up The pulpit, so he praised and praised God, then he mentioned Othman, and Abu Thawr said: So I entered upon Othman while he was besieged, and he said: I am the fourth of Islam."
"37752","(37752) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, who said: Al-Zubayr converted to Islam when he was sixteen years old, and he did not He left behind a raid that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, invaded."
"37753","(37753) Abu Asama told us, he said: Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah told us, he said: Humaid bin Hilal told us, he said: He told us Abdullah bin Al-Samit, on the authority of Abu Dharr, who said: We left our people forgiven, me, my brother Unays, and our mother, and they used to practice lawful the month. forbidden, so we set off until we came down to a maternal uncle of ours, who had wealth and a good appearance. He said: So our maternal uncle honored us and did good. To us, but his people envied us, so they said: If you leave your family, Anais will disobey them. He said: Then our uncle came and complained. What was said to him is upon us. He said: I said: As for your past kindness, you have disturbed it, and you will not have intercourse after that. He said: So we approached. She made us cry, so we bore her. He said: And he covered his head and began to cry.\n He said: So we set off until we landed in the presence of Mecca. He said: Then Anis departed from our ram and a similar one. He said: So they came. The priest gave Anis the choice. He said: Then Anis brought us our basket and a similar one along with it. He said: O my nephew, you prayed before. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, met with three years, he said: I said: for whom? He said: To God. He said: I said: Where were you directing? He said: Wherever God sent me, I prayed the evening prayer until, at the end of the night, I was cast down, as if I were invisible, until the sun overtook me.He said: Unais said: I have a pilgrimage in Mecca, so support me until I come to you. He said: So Farath set off on me, then came to me, and I said: What? Imprisonment? He said: I met a man in Mecca who followed your religion, and he claimed that God had sent him. He said: I said: What do the people say to him? He said: They claim that he is a magician, that he is a soothsayer, and that he is a poet. Anis said: By God, I have heard what the soothsayer said. So what is their saying, and I have imposed its saying on the readers of poetry, so it does not come to pass on anyone’s tongue that it is poetry, and by God it is. He is telling the truth, but they are liars. And Anis was a poet.\n He said: I said: Allow me to go and see. He said: Yes, and be careful among the people of Mecca, for they have attacked him. And they frowned at him. He said: So I set off until I reached Mecca.\n He said: So I hosted a man from among them. He said: I said: Where is this whom you call Al-Sabi? He said: Then he pointed to me. He said: The Sabi’. He said: Then the people of the valley descended upon me with all their might and might, until I fell unconscious. He said: When I rose, I rose as if I were a red monument. He said: So I went to Zamzam and washed the blood off him and drank from its water.\n He said: While the people of Mecca were offering a sacrifice on a moonlit night, God struck the tops of their ears. He said: What is tawaaf? In the house, none of them except two women.He said: So they came to me while calling on Essaaf and Naeel. I said: They married each other. He said: What did that prevent them from doing? What they said, he said: Then they came upon me, and I said: They are like wood, except that I was not. He said: So they went off, howling. And you say: If only one of our people were here.\n He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr met them as they were descending from the mountain. He said: What is the matter with you? They said: The Sabian is between the Kaaba and its curtain. They said: What did he say to you? They said: He told us a word that fills the mouth.\n He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came until he reached the Hijr, and he and his companion touched it. He said: He circumambulated. At home, then he prayed his prayer. He said: So I came to him when he finished his prayer. He said: I was the first to greet him with my greeting.\n Islam. He said: May God’s mercy and blessings be upon you. Who are you from? I said: From Ghifar. He said: So he put his hand towards his head. He said: I said to myself that I hated that I belonged to Ghifar. He said: So I went and took him by the hand. He said: Then his friend missed me, and he was more knowledgeable about it than me. He raised his head and said: When were you? Here? He said: I said: You have been here for ten days, between a day and a night. He said: Who has been feeding you? He said: I said: I had no food other than Zamzam water.So I became so fat that the joints of my stomach broke, and I did not feel any pain in my liver like hunger. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It is blessed, it is delicious food. He said: Then his companion said: Give me permission to feed him tonight.\n So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr set off, and I went with them. He said: Then Abu Bakr opened a door and came to me. From the raisins of Taif. He said: That was the first food I ate with. He said: I remained for as long as I remained, or I was covered, then I met the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: I have been directed to a land full of palm trees, and there is no I think it will be Yathrib, so will you inform your people about it, perhaps God will benefit them through you and reward you for them? I said: Yes.\n So I set off until I came to Unais, and he said: What did you do? I said: I believed that I had embraced Islam and believed. Anis said: I do not desire your religion. Indeed, I have embraced Islam and believed. He said: So we went to our mother, and she said: I have no desire for your religion, for I have submitted to Islam and have spoken the truth. He said: So we endured until we came. Our people were forgiving. He said: Some of them converted to Islam before the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Medina. He said: And it was Their leader was Ima bin Rahdha, and he was their master.He said: And the rest of them said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, comes, we will submit to Islam. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came. He surrendered Medina, then he surrendered the rest of them.\n He said: And she came to greet me, and they said: Our brothers, we greet the one upon whom they greeted. He said: So they embraced Islam. He said: So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Forgiving, may God forgive her, and may God grant her peace. (Muslim 1919. Ahmad 174)"
"37754","(37754) Yahya bin Ali Al-Aslami told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mu’mal, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said : It was the first Islam of Omar. He said: Omar said: My sister went into labor at night, so I was taken out of the house, and I went into shelter. The Kaaba is on a hot night. He said: Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and entered the Hijr, wearing his sandals, and he prayed for a while. God willing, then he left and said: I heard something the likes of which I had never heard, so I went out and followed him, and he said: Who is this? So I said: Omar. He said: O Omar, do not leave me day or night. He said: I was afraid that he would supplicate against me. He said: So I said: I bear witness. That there is no god but Allah, and that you are the Messenger of Allah. He said: So he said: O Omar, cover him up. He said: So I said: By the one who sent you with the truth. We will declare it as I declared polytheism."
"37755","(37755) Abd bin Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, who said: Omar bin Al-Khattab converted to Islam after Forty men and eleven women."
"37756","(37756) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Naama, he heard it from Khalid bin Umair, on the authority of Utba bin Ghazwan, he said: You saw me with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the seventh of the seven."
"37757","(37757) Muhammad bin Abi Ubaidah narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of His father, he said: Abdullah said: You have seen me on the sixth of six days, and there is no Muslim on the surface of the earth except us."
"37758","(37758) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Utbah, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, he said: It was The first to reveal the Qur’an in Mecca among the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was Abdullah bin Masoud, and the first to build it. A mosque in which Ammar bin Yasir prayed, and the first to call the call to prayer was Bilal, and the first to shoot an arrow in the way of God was Saad bin Malik, the first of the Muslims to be killed is Mija', the first to gallop his horse for the sake of God, Al-Miqdad, and the first to be alive The people who gave alms from their own hands were the Banu Adhurah, and the first living group to be united with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was Jahaina."
"37759","(37759) Abu Asama told us, he said: Abdul-Malik told us, he said: Abu Fazara told us, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, Zayd ibn Harithha, a boy with a wolf, whom his people had stopped at Al-Batha’i, where they were selling him, so he came to Khadija. He said: I saw a boy in al-Batha’i that they had stopped to sell. If I had had his price, I would have bought him. She said: How much is he? He said: Seven hundred. She said: Take seven hundred and go and buy it. So he bought it and brought it to her. He said: If only It was mine, so I would free it. She said: So it is yours, so I freed it. (Ibn Asakir 352)"
"37760","(37760) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Qurayh al-Kindi, On the authority of Salman, he said: I was one of the sons of Persia, and I was in a courtyard, and with me were two young men, and when they returned from Their teacher came to a priest, so they entered upon him, so I entered with them, and he said: Did I not prohibit you from bringing anyone to me? He said: So I started to disagree with him, even though I was more beloved to him than either of them. He said: Then he said to me: If your family asked you: Who? Did he imprison you? So say: My teacher, and if your teacher asks you: Who imprisoned you? So say: Hello.\n Then he wanted to change, so I said to him: I will change with you, so I changed with him, so we camped in a village, and it was a woman. She came, and when he came, he said to me: O Salman, dig at my head. So I dug at his head, and I extracted a jar of pearls. Then he said to me: Pour it on my chest, so I poured it on his chest, and he was saying: Woe to me for keeping it. Then he died, so I fell asleep. With dirhams that I took, then I mentioned it and I left it, then I announced it to the priests and monks and they attended it, so I said To them: He had left behind money. He said: Then young men in the village stood up and said: This is our father’s money, so they took it.\n He said: So I said to the monks: Inform me of a learned man whom I should follow.They said: We do not know of a man on earth more knowledgeable than a man about Homs, so I went to him, met him, and told him the story. He said: He said: Did he not bring you anything but the pursuit of knowledge? I said: He brought me nothing but the pursuit of knowledge. He said: I do not know anyone on earth today who is more knowledgeable than a man who visits the Holy House at all times. A year ago, if you go now, you will find his donkey. He said: So I went off and behold, I was with his donkey at the gate of the Holy House, so I sat with him. And he left, and I did not see him until around the age of one year, so he came and I said to him: O Abdullah, what have you done to me? He said: Are you here? I said: Yes, he said: By God, I do not know a man more knowledgeable today than a man who set out in the land of Taima, and if you go now, you will agree with him. It contains three verses: He eats a gift, but he does not eat charity, and at the cartilage of his right shoulder is the seal of the Prophet. Like the white of a dove, its color is the color of its skin.\n He said: So I set off, one land lifted me up and another lowered me, until I passed by a group of Bedouins, who enslaved me and sold me, until... A woman bought me something in Medina, and I heard them mentioning the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the livelihood was difficult. So I said to her: Give me a day, and she said: Yes, so I set off, gathered firewood, sold it, and prepared food.So I brought it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and it was easy, so I placed it in his hands, and he said: What is this? I said: He spoke the truth. He said: So he said to his companions: Eat, but he did not eat. He said: I said: This is one of his signs.\n Then I stayed as long as God wished that I should stay, then I said to my mistress: Give me a day. She said: Yes, so I went and gathered firewood. I sold firewood for more than that, and I made food with it and brought it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was sitting. Among his companions, so I placed it in his hands. He said: What is this? I said: Hadiyyah, so he put down his hand and said to his companions: Take the name of God. And I stood behind him, so he put on his robe, and behold, a ring. Prophethood, so I said: I bear witness that you are the Messenger of God. He said: What is that? So I told him about the man, then I said: Will he enter Paradise, O Messenger of God? He told me that you are a prophet. He said: Only a Muslim soul will enter Paradise."
"37761","(37761) Hussein bin Muhammad told us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah bin Hudhayf A man said: I said: I am asking about a hadith on the authority of Adi bin Hatim while I am in the vicinity of Kufa, so I will be the one who I heard from him, so I came to him and said: Do you know me? He said: Yes, you are so-and-so, son of so-and-so, and he called him by his name. I said: Tell me. He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent. I hated him more than I had ever hated anything, so I set out until the furthest of the Arabs had come down from what was in charge of the Romans, and I thought My place is more severe than what I hated my first place, so I said: I will come to this man. If he is a liar, he will not harm me. He was honest and not hidden from me.\n So I arrived at Medina, and the people looked towards me and said: Udayy ibn Hatim has come. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Oh Udayyy. Ibn Hatim, he converted to Islam. I said: I am of a religion. He said: I know your religion better than you. He said: I said: You know better. Do you want me? He said: Yes, I know your religion better than you. I said: Are you more knowledgeable about my religion than me? He said: Yes, he said: Aren't you a Rakusian? I said: Yes, he said: Aren't you the leader of your people? I said: Yes, he said: Did you not take the square? I said: Yes. He said: That is not permissible for you in your religion. He said: So I humbled myself.\n He said: O Adi bin Hatim, submit to Islam, for I do not think, or I think, that anything is preventing you from accepting Islam except your own personal secrets. Who do you see around me, and you see people as one support and one hand over us, so has confusion come? I said: No, and I knew her location. He said: The snake is about to leave Al-Hira and circumambulate the Kaaba without any neighbours. And the treasures of Kisra ibn Hurmuz will be opened to you. He said it three times. A man will soon be concerned about who will accept his charity.\n I saw the two snakes coming out of confusion and circumambulating the Kaaba without any neighbours, and I was in the first place of the horse. It raided the cities of Medina, and the third time has come. This is according to what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him. (Ahmad 257. Ibn Hibban 6479)"
"37762","(37762) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Yunus bin Abi Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shubail bin Awf, on the authority of Jarir bin Abdullah, who said: When I approached Medina, I mounted my camel, then untied my cloak, and put on I undressed, so I entered while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was delivering a sermon, so I greeted the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the people rejected me. With a stare, he said: So I said to someone who was sitting with me: O Abdullah, did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mention anything about my affair? He said: Yes, he reminded you of the best of remembrance. He said: While the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was delivering a sermon, he was presented to him in I proposed to him, and he said: He will enter upon you from this dawn, or from this gate, from the best of the people. Indeed, Ali A face anointed by an angel. Jarir said: So I thanked God for what He had given me."
"37763","(37763) Abu Asama told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwah told us, on the authority of his father, and Fatima, on the authority of Asma, she said: I made the journey of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the house of Abu Bakr, when he wanted to migrate to Medina. She said: We did not find anything to connect them with for his journey or for his watering, so I said to Abu Bakr: By God, I do not find anything to connect with except My scope, she said: So he said: Pair it with two, so attach water to one to drink, and to the other to travel, so that is why it was called Dhat. The two ranges.\n(Bukhari 5388, Ahmed 346)"
"37764","(37764) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Umair ibn Ishaq, who said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out He and Abu Bakr greeted him, meaning to Medina. Suraq ibn Malik followed them, and when he came to them, he said: These are the Quraysh who fled. If I returned to the Quraysh, and he said: So his horse was kind to them, and the horse became ungrateful, and he said: Pray to God to bring her out, Nor did he bring you closer. He said: So she left, and he repeated it until he did that twice or three times. He said: So he refrained, then he said: Come to me for the provisions. And the lambs, and they said: We do not want to, nor do we have any need for that."
"37765","(37765) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, he said: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’ ibn Azib, he said: Abu Bakr bought a saddlebag from a single man for thirteen dirhams. Abu Bakr said to the single man: Pass Al-Baraa’ and let him carry it to me. He left, and a single man said to him: No, until you tell us what you and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did where you left. And the polytheists seek you both.\n He said: We departed from Mecca, so we lived our night and our day until we appeared, and the leader of the afternoon rose, so I threw With my sight, I see a shadow to which we seek refuge. Then, lo, I am in a rock, and we end up there, and when a shadow remains No, so I looked at the dome for a shade for her, so I covered it, then I spread a blanket for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a fur coat in it, then I said: Lie down, O Messenger of God, and he lay down. Then I went and cleared my surroundings to see anyone seeking, and behold, I was a shepherd of sheep. He drove his sheep to the rock, wanting what I wanted from it, so I asked him and said: Who are you for, boy? He said: To a man from Quraysh. He said: So he named him, so I recognized him.\n So I said: Is there any milk in your sheep? He said: Yes, I said: Are you a milkmaid for me? He said: Yes, he said: So I ordered him to seize a sheep from his sheep, so I ordered him to shake off the dust from its udder.Then I ordered him to shake his hands, and he said: Thus, and he struck one hand with the other, and he milked a pile of Milk, and with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a medicine for her mouth, a rag, so I poured on the milk until the bottom of it became cold. So I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I met him when he had woken up, so I said: Drink, O Messenger of God, and the Messenger of God drank. May God bless him and grant him peace until I am satisfied.\n Then I said: I am leaving, O Messenger of God, so we set out while the people were looking for us, but none of them reached us except Suraq bin Malik bin Jasham, on a horse of his, so I said: This request has come to us, O Messenger of God, and I cried, so he said: What Does he make you cry? So I said: By God, I do not cry for myself, but I cry for you. He said: So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed for him. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: O God, suffice us with whatever You wish. He said: So his horse spread it across the ground to its belly, so he jumped off of it. Then he said: O Muhammad, I know that this is your deed, so pray to God to save me from what I am in, for God is indeed blind. On the one who is behind me from the group, and this is my quintessence, so take an arrow from them, for you will pass by my camels and sheep in a place Such and such, so take what you need from her.Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: We have no need of your camels, and he departed from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed for him and went back to his companions, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, departed. And I was with him until we came to Medina at night, and the people disputed with him as to which of them should descend upon him. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Indeed, I sent down the night upon the Banu al-Najjar, the maternal uncles of Abdul-Muttalib, and I honored them with that, so the people went out until He entered Medina, and on the way there were servants and servants over the houses: Muhammad came, the Messenger of God came, and when the morning came, he set off and stayed where I am commanded\n He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had prayed towards the Holy House for sixteen months, or seventeen. month, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, liked to face it towards the Kaaba, so God revealed: (We may see Your face turned toward the heavens, so We will surely give you a direction that will please you, so turn your face toward the Sacred Mosque.) He said: So face it. Towards the Kaaba, and the foolish people said: (What turned them away from the qiblah which they used to follow? Say to God, “The East” And Morocco,He guides whomever He wills to a straight path.) He said: A man prayed with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, then he left after he had prayed. Then he passed by a group of Ansar who were kneeling in the afternoon prayer towards the Holy House, and he said: He bears witness that he prayed. With the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and that he faced towards the Ka’b. He said: Then the people turned away until they faced towards The Kaaba\n Al-Bara’ said: One of the immigrants, Mus’ab bin Umair, the brother of Banu Abd al-Dar bin Qusay, descended upon us, and we said to him: What he did. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: This is his place and his companions are on my trail. Then after Amr bin Umm Maktum, the blind brother of Banu Fihr, came to us, so we said: His: what he did behind you; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace and his companions? He said: Come on my trail, then Ammar bin Yasir, Saad bin Abi Waqqas, and Abdullah bin Masoud came to us after him. And Bilal, then Omar bin Al-Khattab came to us after them with twenty riders, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us after them. He greeted us, and Abu Bakr was with him. He did not come to us until I had recited a surah from the surah of al-Mufassal. Then we went out to meet the caravan. We found them warned. (Bukhari 2439 and Muslim 2310)"
"37766","(37766) Affan told us, he said: Shuabi told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Al-Baraa’, saying: The first to come to us Among the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, were Mus’ab bin Umair and Ibn Umm Maktum. They started reciting the Qur’an to the people, then Ammar, Bilal, and Saad came, then Omar bin Al-Khattab came with twenty riders, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came. He said: I have never seen the people of Medina rejoice over anything that made them happy with it. He said: No one came forward until I had recited: {Glorify the name of your Lord The highest} in a surah from Al-Mufassal."
"37767","(37767) Aswad bin Amir narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that Suraqih bin Malik Al-Mudalji, told them: The Quraysh granted the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr forty uqiyas. He said: While I was sitting When a man came to me and said: The two men with whom Quraysh were placed were not close to you, in such-and-such a place. He said: So I brought my horse while it was grazing, so I ran off with it, then I took my spear. He said: So I rode it. He said: So I made the spear drag. For fear that the people of the water would involve me in it. He said: When I saw them, Abu Bakr said: This is a transgressor who wants us to transgress. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, turned to me and said: Oh God, suffice us with what you wish. He said: So he stripped my horse, and he was wrapped in skins. from the ground, then I fell on a stone, turned over, and said: Leave the one who did what I thought to my horse to save her, and he promised not to He disobeyed him. He said: So he prayed for him, and the horse was saved. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Are you my father? I said: Yes, and he said: Here he is, he said: So he spread the people about us.\n And the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, took the road to the coast from the side of the sea. He said: So I was at the beginning of the day seeking them.And at the end of the day he armed them, and said to me: When we have settled in Medina, if you decide to come to us, then come. He said: When he came to Medina and defeated the people of Badr and Uhud, and the people and those around them submitted to Islam, Suraqih said: I was informed that He wanted to send Khalid ibn al-Walid to Banu Mudlij. He said: So I went to him and said to him: I seek blessings from you. The people said: : Meh, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: His invitation, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: What do you want? So I said: I have heard that you want to send Khalid ibn al-Walid to my people, and I would like you to bid farewell to them. If he converts to Islam, Their people accepted Islam with them, and if they did not submit, the hearts of their people would not fear for them. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took He greeted Khalid bin Al-Walid and said to him: Go with him and do what he wants."
"37768","(37768) Affan told us, he said: Hammam told us, he said: Thabit told us, on the authority of Anas; That Abu Bakr told him, he said: I said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while we were in the cave: If only one of them would look at We saw under his feet. He said: O Abu Bakr, what do you think of two? God is the third."
"37769","(37769) Abu Asama told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of his father; Abdullah bin Abi Bakr was the one who used to dispute about food to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr, and they were In the cave"
"37770","(37770) Shababah told us, on the authority of Warqa’, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid; In his saying: {Unless you support him}, then he mentioned what was the beginning of his situation when he was sent, and he says: God is the one who will do that to him. We support him just as he supported him the second time."
"37771","(37771) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Ibn Muhajir, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Abu Bakr stayed with The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in the cave three times."
"37772","(37772) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi` ibn Umar, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Abu Bakr; When they reached the cave, he said: When he saw a hole, he said: Then Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, touched his foot to him, and he said: O Messenger of God, if it was a sting or a sting, it would be on me."
"37773","(37773) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; {You were the best of people raised to mankind}. He said: They are those who migrated with Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, to Medina."
"37774","(37774) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ali bin Rabah, on the authority of his father, who said: I heard Maslamah bin Mukhlid, saying: I was born when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and died when I was ten years old."
"37775","(37775) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he heard Anas say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came He entered Medina when I was ten years old, and he was arrested when I was twenty years old, but my mothers urged me to serve them."
"37776","(37776) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father; When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, migrated to Medina, he, Abu Bakr, and Amer bin Fayra, he said: Talha brought them to Abu Bakr on the road, wearing white clothes, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered. Peace be upon him and Abu Bakr in Medina."
"37777","(37777) Khalid ibn Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ali ibn Mushir, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his son’s names. Abi Bakr; She migrated to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while she was pregnant with Abdullah bin Al-Zubair, so she placed him in a cloak. She did not breastfeed him until she brought him to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he took him and placed him in his lap. They asked for dates. They kneaded it until they found it and kneaded it. The first thing that entered his stomach was the saliva of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he named him Abdullah."
"37778","(37778) Ja’far bin Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Sa’d, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Abdullah, who said: Abdullah said: The first to emigrate from this nation were two young men from Quraysh."
"37779","(37779) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, he said: I said to him: What a difference, what a difference. Between the first immigrants and the others? He said: The difference between them is the two qiblahs, so whoever prays with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, by the two qiblahs, is one of the emigrants. The first two"
"37780","(37780) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Thabit told us, on the authority of Anas; That Abu Bakr was the companion of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, from Mecca to Medina, and Abu Bakr differed. To the Levant, and he was known, but the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, was not known, so they used to say: O Abu Bakr, who is this? Is the boy in your hands? He said: This is a guide who guides me to the path. He said: When they approached Medina, they descended upon the heat, and sent for the Ansar and they came. He said: I witnessed him on the day he entered Medina, and I have never seen a day better or brighter than the day he entered upon us. And I witnessed the day he died, and I have never seen a day more uglier or more unjust than the day he died, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he greeted you. (Ahmad 122 Hakim 12)"
"37781","(37781) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, who said: Khosrau wrote to Badham: I was informed that a man is saying something and I do not know what it is, so a message was sent for him, so he should stay in his house and not be among the people there. Something, otherwise he will make me a date with him. He said: So he sent Badham to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Two men were shaving their beards, grooming their mustaches, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: What will make you bear it? This? He said: So they said to him: We are commanded by him who they claim is their Lord. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: But we We go against your Sunnah, we accomplish this, and we send that.\n He said: Then a man from Quraysh with a long mustache passed by him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered him to reward them both.\n He said: So he left them for twenty-few days, then he said: Go to the One whom you claim is your Lord, so they told him that My Lord killed the one who claimed to be his Lord. They said: When? He said: Today. He said: So they went to Badham and told him the news. He said: So he wrote to Kisra, and they found that today is The one who was killed in Kasra."
"37782","(37782) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmali al-Aslami, who said: I heard Sa`id bin al-Musayyab He says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote to Khosrau, Caesar, and the Negus: As for what follows, “Come to a word.” It is the same between us and you, that we worship none but Allah, and do not associate anything with Him, and do not take one another as lords other than Him. God, but if they turn away, then say, “Bear witness that we are Muslims.”\n Saeed bin Al-Musayyab said: Then Kisra tore up the letter and did not look at it. The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He tore it up. His nation was torn apart, but as for the Negus, he believed, and those who were with him believed, and he was sent to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He presented it as a gift, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Leave him as he has left you.\n As for Caesar; Then he read the book of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: This is a book I have not heard of after Solomon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him (in the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful). Then he sent to Abu Sufyan and Al-Mughirah bin Shu’abi, and they were merchants in his land. So he asked them about some of the affairs of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they asked them about those who followed him, and they said: The women and weak men followed him. The people, and he said: Have you seen those who go in with him return? They said: No. He said: He is a prophet. He will rule over what is under my feet. If I were with him, I would kiss his feet. (Saeed bin Mansour 2480)"
"37783","(37783) Hatem bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ya’qub, on the authority of Ja’far bin Amr, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was sent He delivered four people to four parties: a man to Kisra, a man to Caesar, and a man to Muqawqis, and he sent Amr ibn Umayyah went to the Negus, and each of them began speaking in the language of the people to whom he was sent. When he came Amr ibn Umayyah al-Najashī found for them a small gate through which they could enter as disbelievers. When Amr saw that, he turned away from it. Al-Qaqaqari said: This was difficult for the Abyssinians when they were sitting with the Negus, so much so that they were concerned about it, to the point that they said to the Negus: This man did not enter as we entered. He said: What prevented you from entering as they entered? He said: We would not do this to our Prophet, and if we had done it to anyone, we would have done it to him. He said: He spoke the truth. He said: His supplication.\n They said to the Negus: This man claims that Jesus was a slave. He said: What do you say about Jesus? He said: The word of God and His Spirit. He said: Jesus could not go beyond that."
"37784","(37784) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mujalid, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote to my grandfather, and this His letter is with us: In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, from Muhammad, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to Umair Dhu Maran, and to Whoever converts to Islam from Hamdan, peace be upon you, for I praise God to you, there is no god but Him. As for after that, Your Islam has reached us, our return from the land of the Romans, so rejoice, for God has guided you with His guidance, and when you You bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, and you establish prayer and pay zakat, then indeed you are under the protection of Allah. And Muhammad is the Messenger of God, upon your blood, your property, and the land of the Bones, which you surrendered to, he leveled it and created it. And its eyes and its pastures, you will not be oppressed, nor will there be any hardship upon you, for charity is not permissible for Muhammad and his family. It is only zakat with which you purify your wealth for the poor Muslims, and Malik ibn Mararaa, the narrator, memorized the unseen. And the news has reached, and I command you to do it well, O Dhu Maran, for it is awaited. Ali bin Abi Talib wrote: Peace be upon you, and may your Lord revive you.\n(Abu Dawud 3021; Abu Ali 6829)"
"37785","(37785) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Qays bin Abi Hazim, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was sent to Khath’am, to the people who were among them. When the Muslims invaded them, they held fast. By prostration, he said: They prostrated, he said: Some of them were killed, and that reached the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Give them half. The reason for their prayers. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Indeed, I am free from every Muslim who associates with a polytheist."
"37786","(37786) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Asama, who said: We sent the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, in peace, and in the morning we passed the fires from the side of Jehanna, and I met a man, and he said: There is no god but God, so I stabbed him. Then something came to my mind about that, so I mentioned it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He said, No. There is no god but Allah and you killed him? He said: I said: O Messenger of God, he only said it as a group of weapons. He said: So do not break his heart until you know what it says, a group of Weapon, or not? He kept repeating it until I wished I had converted to Islam that day."
"37787","(37787) Zayd ibn Harun told us, saying: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, on the authority of Umar ibn al-Hakam ibn Thawban, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri; The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent Alqamah bin Mahriz to accompany me, and when he reached the head of his battles Or it was in some way, a group of the army asked for permission, so he gave them permission, and appointed Abdullah bin Hudhafiya bin over them. Qais Al-Sahmi, I was among those who fought with him, and when we were some way away, the people lit a fire to warm themselves up, or to make... She did a good deed to them, so Abdullah said, and there was a sense of humor in her: Is it not incumbent on you to listen and obey? They said: Yes, he said: I do not command you to do anything unless you do it? They said: Yes. He said: I am determined that you do not jump into this Fire. He said: Then some people stood up and took shelter. When he thought that they And jump. He said: Hold yourselves, for I was only joking with you. When we came, they mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Whoever of them commands you to disobey him, do not obey him."
"37788","(37788) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Hudhayl, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was sent May God bless him and grant him peace, Khalid ibn al-Walid handed over to al-Uzza, so he began to strike her with his sword, saying:\n O glory be to your disbelief, no, Glory be to you, I saw that God had insulted you.\n(Nasa’i 11547. Abu Ali 898)"
"37789","(37789) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Uthman bin Mawhib, who said: I heard Abu Burda saying: The Messenger of God wrote May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said to a man from the People of the Book: You are a Muslim. He said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did not finish his book. Until a letter came to him from that man; He recited his greetings to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned his peace. Bottom of his book."
"37790","(37790) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Qur’a bin Khalid al-Sadusi, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin al-Shakhir, who said: We were While sitting in this shrine in Basra, a Bedouin came with a piece of human skin, or a piece of a sock, and said: This A letter written to me by the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: So I took it and read it to the people, and behold, in it was: In the name of God. God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, from Muhammad, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to the Banu Zuhair bin Uqish: If you establish the prayer And you paid the zakat, and you gave from the five spoils, and the arrows of the Prophet, and the pure, then you are secure in the security of God and the security of His Messenger, he said: Did you not hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say anything? He said: I heard him say: Fasting is the month of patience, and three days of each month go with a free heart. (Abu Dawud 2992. Ahmed 78)"
"37791","(37791) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ja’far bin Al-Zubair; The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent Abdullah bin Anis to Khaled bin Sufyan. He said: When I approached him, This was at the time of the afternoon prayer, and I was afraid that there would be someone trying to do it, or practicing it, so I prayed while I was walking."
"37792","(37792) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Qais, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent Amr on the army of Dhat al-Silsilah to Lakhm, Judham, and Masaif al-Sham. He said: There were a few of its companions. He said: Then Amr said to them. “None of you should light a fire, for that would be difficult for them.” So they spoke to Abu Bakr to speak to Omar, and he spoke to him, and he said: No. If someone lights a fire, you throw him into it, and he fights the enemy and defeats them, and his army becomes permissible. Then the people say: Why? Shall we follow them? He said: No, I fear that they will have a place behind these mountains from which they will cut off the Muslims. So they complained to him. When they returned, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Are you telling the truth, Amr? He said: There were few of my companions, so I was afraid that the enemy would want to kill them. So when God made me prevail over them, they said: Follow them. I said: I fear that behind these mountains they will have a place with which to cut off the Muslims. He said: So it was. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, praised his command."
"37793","(37793) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Qais; That the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to Bilal: Have you prepared the horse-mounted mounts? He said: No, he said: So prepare them, and start with the Ahmasiyin before the Qariyyin."
"37794","(37794) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote a letter to the people of As-Sahimiyya, so he took the letter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He broke his bucket with it, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent a convoy, and they took his family and property. And his flock escaped on his horse, while he was naked and had nothing on him, so he went to her daughter, who was married to the children of the family.\n He said: They had converted to Islam, and I had embraced Islam with them, and they had invited him to Islam.\n He said: He came to his daughter, and the people were sitting in the courtyard of her house, so he came to the house behind her, and when she saw him His daughter was naked, and she threw a garment over him and said: What's wrong with you? He said: All evil. I have no family or money left. He said: Where is your husband? She said: About camels. He said: So he came to him and told him. He said: Take your camel as it comes, and we will provide you with a supply of milk. He said: There is no need for it. But give me a shepherd’s lodging and a source of water, for I will hasten with Muhammad and he will not divide my family and my property. So he set off with it. A garment that when he covers his head with it, his head comes out, and when he covers him with it his head comes out.\n So he set off until he entered Medina at night, and was in the shoes of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, extended your hand and I will pledge allegiance to you. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, extended it. And he gave his hand, and when his flock went to wipe over it, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took hold of it, and then he said to him: He said: O Messenger of God, extend your hand. He said: Who are you? He said: Ra’i’ al-Suhaymi. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took his arm and raised it, then said: Yes. People, this is the flock of As-Sahimi to whom I wrote, so he took my letter and covered his bucket with it, and he converted to Islam.\n Then he said: O Messenger of God, my family and my wealth. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: As for your wealth, it was divided between Muslims, and as for your family, see who among them I have gained power over. He said: So I went out and behold, a son of mine recognized the departed woman, and behold He was standing there, so I went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: This is his son, so he sent Bilal with him, and he said: Go with him and ask him: Who is your father? If he says yes, then hand him over to him. He said: Then Bilal came to him and said: Is he your father? He said: Yes, so he brought him to him. He said: Bilal came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: By God, I did not see anyone. Some of them were conveyed to their companion, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: That is the harshness of the Bedouins. (Ahmad 285. Tabarani 4635)"
"37795","(37795) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of Abu Musa said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered us to go with Jafar bin Abi Talib to the land of the Negus. He said: This reached our people, so they sent Amr bin Al-Aas and Ammarah bin Al-Walid, and they collected a gift for the Negus, so they came and they came to Ali. Negus, and they brought him his gift, and he accepted it and prostrated to him. Then Amr ibn al-Aas said to him: Some of us turned away from Our religion, and they are in your land. Then the Negus said to them: In my land? They said: Yes, so he sent to us.\n Then Ja`far said to us: None of you should speak. I am your fiancé today. He said: So we ended up with the Negus and he was sitting. In his assembly, Amr ibn al-Aas was on his right, Ammar was on his left, and the priests and monks were sitting as magistrates. Amr bin Al-Aas and Ammar said to him: They will not prostrate to you.\n He said: When we reached him, we asked the priests and monks who were with him: Prostrate to the king, and Ja`far said: No. We prostrate only to Him. When we came to the Negus, he said, What prevents you from prostrating? He said: We do not prostrate except to God. The Negus said to him: What is that? He said: God has sent among us His Messenger.And He is the Messenger whom Jesus, son of Mary, peace be upon them, was given the good news of: {A Messenger will come after me, whose name is Ahmed}, so he commanded us That we should worship God, and not associate anything with Him, and perform prayer, and pay zakat, and enjoin us to do what is right, and forbid us from doing evil. Al-Munkir, he said: The Negus admired what he said.\n When Amr bin Al-Aas saw this, he said: May God bless the king. They are disagreeing with you regarding the son of Maryam, peace be upon him. Al-Najashi said to Ja`far: What does your friend say about the son of Maryam? He said: It says about it the saying of God: It is the spirit of God and His word. He brought it out of a virgin who had not been approached by human beings. He said: Then the Negus took a stick from the ground and said: O priests and monks, there is nothing more than what these people say. You say about the son of Maryam, “He does not weigh this.” Welcome to you, and to whomever you come from, for I bear witness that he is the Messenger of God. And what Jesus, son of Mary, was given good tidings about, and if it were not for the kingdom I have, I would have come to him and even carried his sandals. Stay. In my land whatever you wish, and he commanded us to be given food and clothing, and said: Return to these two gifts of yours.\n He said: Amr ibn al-Aas was a short man, and Ammar ibn al-Walid was a handsome man. He said: So they headed toward the sea. Al-Najashi, he said: So they drank.He said: Amr ibn al-Aas was with his wife. When they drank the wine, Amr said to Amr: Command your wife and let her kiss me. Amr said to him: Aren't you ashamed? So Amara took him and threw him into the sea, so Amr started pleading with him until he got him into the ship, so he became angry. Amr agreed upon that, so Amr said to the Negus: If you go out behind Ummar in your family, he said: So the Negus called for Ummar So he blew into her urethra and it became with the beast. (Abu Dawud 3197, Hakim 309)"
"37796","(37796) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, he said: When Ja’far came from... The land of Abyssinia, Omar bin Al-Khattab met Asma bint Umays, and said to her: We preceded you in emigrating, and we are better. Of you. She said: I will not return until I come to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: So she entered upon him and said: O Messenger of God. I met Omar, and he claimed that he was better than us, and that they had preceded us in migration. She said: The Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He said: “Rather, you emigrated twice.”\n Ismail said: Saeed bin Abi Barda told me, he said: She said to Omar at that time: It is not like that, we were being sent away. In the land of the hated and hostile people, while you are with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He advises the ignorant of you and gives food. You are hungry"
"37797","(37797) Abd bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, in his saying: {You will see their eyes overflowing with tears. Of the truth they knew. He said: This was revealed about the Negus."
"37798","(37798) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came when Khaybar was conquered, and it was said to him: Ja`far has come from the Negus. He said: I do not know which of the two I should be happy with, with the arrival of Ja`far, or with the arrival of Khaybar. With the conquest of Khaybar? Then he met him, adhered to him, and accepted what was between his eyes."
"37799","(37799) Khalid bin Mukhlid told us, he said: Abd al-Rahim bin Abdul Aziz told us, he said: Al-Zuhri told me, he said: Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman bin Al Harith bin Hisham Al Makhzoumi told me, he said: Al Negus called Jafar bin Abi Talib. And he gathered the heads of the Christians to him, then he said to Ja`far: Recite to them what you have of the Qur’an. So he recited to them (K"
"37800","(37800) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; Othman bin Affan was mentioned in his presence. A man said: They are taking him captive. He said: Woe to them! They are captivating a man who entered upon him. Al-Najashi said about a group of the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and all of them gave him temptation other than him. They said: What is temptation? Which they gave her? He said: No one would enter upon him unless he nodded his head to him, but Othman refused, so he said: What prevented you from prostrating as you did? Did your companions prostrate? He said: I would not prostrate to anyone besides Allah."
"37801","(37801) Zaid bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Husayn bin Waqid narrated to us, saying: Abdullah bin Buraida narrated to us, on the authority of His father; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, launched nineteen campaigns and fought in eight. (Muslim 1448)"
"37802","(37802) Zaid bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Laith bin Saad narrated to me, on the authority of Safwan bin Sulaym Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Busra, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Azib; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, launched nineteen campaigns."
"37803","(37803) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, he said: Zuhair narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Zaid bin Arqam, he heard it from him. ; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, launched nineteen campaigns. Abu Ishaq said: So I asked Zayd ibn Arqam: How much? Did you fight with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Seventeen. (Bukhari 3949, Muslim 916)"
"37804","(37804) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, he said: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: I fought with The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, made fifteen campaigns, and I and Abdullah bin Omar were with him.\n(Bukhari 4472, Ibn Hibban 7176)"
"37805","(37805) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to me, saying: Matar al-Warraq narrated to me, on the authority of his leaders; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, invaded nineteen battles and fought on eight: the Day of Badr, the Day of Uhud, and the Day of Al-Ahzab. And the day of Qudayd, and the day of Khaybar, and the day of the conquest of Mecca, and the day of water for Banu al-Mustaliq, and the day of Hunayn."
"37806","(37806) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Alaqi, on the authority of Saad ibn Abi Waqqas, he said: When the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to Medina and said: You have descended before our backs, so strengthen us. Until we believed in you and you believed in us, then he strengthened them, but they did not submit. So we sent the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Rajab, and no We will be a hundred, and he commanded us to attack Hayy from Kinanah to the side of Jahinah. He said: So we attacked them, and they were Many times, so we took refuge in Jahaina, but they prevented us and said: Why do you fight in the sacred month? So we said: We are only fighting those who expelled us from the Sacred Land during the Sacred Month, and some of us said to each other: What do you see? They said: We will go to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and inform him. Some people said: No, but we will stay here, and I said, “I am among people.” With me: No, rather we will go to this caravan of Quraysh and share it, so we set off for the caravan, and the booty at that time was: who He took something and it was his, so we went to the caravan, and our companions went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and informed him. At the news, an angry man stood up, his face and face turning red, and said: Did you leave me all together, and came separately? Indeed, those who were before you were destroyed by the factions. They sent against you a man who was not the best of you. I will make you patient in the face of hunger. And thirst, so he sent Abdullah bin Jahsh Al-Asadi to us, and he was the first prince in Islam."
"37807","(37807) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders; In his saying: {And do not fight them at the Sacred Mosque until they fight you there} so his Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded And he granted that they should not fight them at the Sacred Mosque, unless they begin fighting there. Then it was abrogated: {They ask you about The sacred month is a fight in it} abrogated by these two verses; His saying: {So when the sacred months have passed, kill the polytheists wherever you find them, and capture them and besiege them}"
"37808","(37808) Hatim bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: Badr was on the seventeenth day of Ramadan, on the authority of On Friday."
"37809","(37809) Affan told us, he said: Khalid bin Abdullah told us, he said: Amr bin Yahya told us, on the authority of Amr bin Amir. Ibn Abdullah Ibn Al-Zubayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aamir Ibn Rabi’a Al-Badri, who said: Badr was on a Monday. For the seventeenth of Ramadan."
"37810","(37810) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: He said: Investigate it. It is eleven days before the morning of Badr."
"37811","(37811) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Amr bin Shayba narrated to us, saying: I asked Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman bin Al-Harith bin Hisham: Which night was the night of Badr? He said: It is the night of Friday, the seventeen nights of Ramadan that have passed."
"37812","(37812) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Amir, who said: Badr was indeed a man’s well. It is called Badr."
"37813","(37813) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Khathim, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The angels did not fight except on the Day of Resurrection. Full moon"
"37814","(37814) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Aoun, on the authority of Abu Salih al-Hanafi, on the authority of Ali, He said: It was said to Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, my guardian, on the day of Badr: With one of you is Gabriel, with the other is Michael, and Israfil is an angel. Great to witness the fight, or stand in line."
"37815","(37815) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr al-Laythi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: He came out The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went to Badr, and when he was speaking to people through spirits, he said: How do you see? Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of God, we have heard that they are doing such-and-such. He said: Then he addressed the people, and said: How do you see? Omar said the same as Abu Bakr said, then he delivered a sermon and said: What do you see? Saad bin Muadh said: Which of us do you want? By the One who honored you and sent down to you the Book, you have never walked it, and I have no knowledge of it. And if you travel until you come to Barak Al-Ghimad from Dhu Yemen, we will certainly travel with you, and not be like those who said to Moses, “From the children of Israel: Go, you and your Lord, and fight. Indeed, here we will sit. But go, you and your Lord, and fight. We will follow you both. Perhaps you went out for a matter, and God told you something different, so look at what God told you and go to it. Separate the ropes of whomever you wish, cut the ropes of whomever you wish, be safe with whomever you wish, return to whomever you wish, and take from our property whatever you wish. Then the Qur’an was revealed. Based on Saad’s saying: {Just as your Lord brought you out of your house in truth, and indeed a party of the believers were averse} to his saying: {And He will cut off the backs of the disbelievers} Indeed, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, only went out to want his spoils, what was with Abu Sufyan. So God made fighting happen to His Prophet."
"37816","(37816) Abd al-A’la ibn Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: When it happened On the day of Badr, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever does such-and-such will have such-and-such. He said: So he hastened to do it. These are the young men, and the old men remained under the banners, and when the spoils were in, they came seeking what had been appointed for them, and he said The sheikhs: Do not have any influence over us, for we were your enemy and we were under the banners, and if you were exposed, you would be exposed to us. So they quarreled, so God revealed: {They ask you about the Anfal} to His saying: {And obey God and His Messenger if you are believers}"
"37817","(37817) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; {The crowd will be defeated}. He said: That was the day of Badr. They said: We are all victorious, so these verses were revealed."
"37818","(37818) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, on the authority of al-Rabi`, on the authority of Abu al-Aaliyah; {The crowd will be defeated and they will turn back.} He said: The Day of Badr."
"37819","(37819) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; {Until when We open upon them a gate of severe punishment, when they are in confusion therein} He said: That was the day of Badr."
"37820","(37820) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ikrimah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was jumping in his armor on the day of Badr, and saying: The crowd will be defeated, the crowd will be defeated. (Bukhari 2915, Ahmed 329)"
"37821","(37821) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Harithah ibn Mudharib, on the authority of Ali, who said: He You saw us on the Day of Badr as we were seeking refuge with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was the closest we were to the enemy."
"37822","(37822) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ikrimah; The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said on the Day of Badr: This is Gabriel holding the head of his horse. The war"
"37823","(37823) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Umair bin Ishaq, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Be straight, for the angels have done straight.” He said: “It was the first day the wool was laid.”"
"37824","(37824) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Harithah ibn Mudharib al-Abdi, on the authority of Ali, who said The Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace on the Day of Badr, were distinguished by their white wool."
"37825","(37825) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Amir, who said: When it was the day of Badr, he spoke The Muslims were informed that Ibn Jabir was preached to support the polytheists, but that was difficult for the Muslims, so the following verse was revealed: “Yes, if you are patient and fear And they will come to you from this point of view. Your Lord will provide you with five thousand angels appointed in harmony.} He says: I supplied you with these angels, but they did not support them with anything. (Tabari 76)"
"37826","(37826) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, and Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab; {And He sends down upon you water from the sky to purify you thereby.} They said: Tashsh on the day of full moon."
"37827","(37827) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: I used to ask my companions for water one day. Full moon (Bukhari 2208)"
"37828","(37828) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah; {The Day We will strike with great brutality} He said: The Day of Badr."
"37829","(37829) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Tha’labah bin Su’air. The virgin; That Abu Jahl said on the day of Badr: Oh God, sever us from the ties of kinship, and give us that which is not known, so grant him lunch, he said: And it was That is an opening on his part, so these verses were revealed: {If you open, then indeed conquest has come to you, but if you desist, that is better. May you be blessed with the verses. (Ahmad 431, Hakim 328)"
"37830","(37830) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud; He came to Abu Jahal on the day of Badr, and he looked down upon him. He said: God has disgraced you. He said: Are you more baptized than the man you killed? (Bukhari 3961)"
"37831","(37831) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Saad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, he said: I was in the classroom on the day of Badr, and I turned to my right and to my left, and behold, there were two young boys, and I thought. They were in their place, and one of them said to him secretly from his friend: Uncle, show me Abu Jahl. He said: I said: What do you want from him? He said: I have made it a duty to God that if I see him, I will kill him. He said: The other also said secretly from his companion: Yes, uncle, show me a father. He was ignorant. He said: I said: What do you want from him? He said: I made it a duty for God that if I saw him, I would kill him. He said: We were not pleased with the place of them other than them. He said: I said: That is it. He said: I pointed to them, and they ran away as if they were hawks, and they were the sons of Afra until they struck him. (Bukhari 3141)"
"37832","(37832) Ja’far bin Aoun told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, on the authority of Abdullah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: O God, kill the Quraysh three times: May Abu Jahl bin Hisham be sacrificed, and he admonished you. Bin Rabi’ah, Shaybah bin Rabi’ah, Al-Walid bin Utba, Umayyah bin Khalaf, and Uqba bin Abi Mu’it. He said: Abdullah said: I saw them killed in the heart of Badr."
"37833","(37833) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of his brother Yazid bin Hazim, on the authority of Ikrimah Mawla Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Muslims camped at Badr and the polytheists approached, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, looked at Utbah ibn Rabi`ah was riding a red camel, and he said: If any of the people have goodness, then it is with the owner of the red camel. If they obey him, they will be guided. Utbah said: Obey me, and do not fight these people, for if you do, he will never cease. That is in your hearts, when a man looks at the killer of his brother and the killer of his father, so put cowardice on me and go back.\n He said: Then it reached Abu Jahl, and he said: He was swollen, by God, his magic whenever he saw Muhammad and his companions, and by God, that was not the case with him, but rather This is because his son is with them, and he knew that Muhammad and his companions would have eaten him valiantly if they had met. He said: Then Utba said: The whistleblower will know that he is a coward who is corrupting his people, but by God, I see under the straw a people who are beating you severely. They will call Al-Baqi’ for you. Do you not see that their heads are the heads of snakes and their faces are swords? He said: Then he called his brother and his son and walked between them, until when he separated from the class he called for a duel."
"37834","(37834) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Harithah ibn Mudharib, on the authority of Ali, he said: When we came to Medina and acquired some of its fruits, we invaded it and a malaise struck us, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, telling about Badr. He said: When we heard that the polytheists had arrived, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, walked To Badr, and Badr was a well, so we preceded the polytheists to it, and found therein two men from among them; A man from Quraysh, and a servant of Uqba bin Abi Mu’it. As for the Quraysh, he escaped to her, and as for the master, So we took him and made us say to him: How many people are? So he says: They, by God, are numerous in number and mighty in their power. So, when the Muslims said that, they beat him to the point of They brought him to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said to him: How many are the people? He said: By God, they are numerous in number and powerful in their strength. So the people struggled to tell them how many they were. He refused.\n Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked him: How much should they sacrifice? He said: Ten times every day. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The people are a thousand, each one of the tribes of a hundred, and they followed them.\n Then a shower of rain struck us during the night.So we went under the trees and the hut to seek shade from the rain. He said: And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spent the night to seek refuge. He called on his Lord, and when dawn came he called out: Prayer, servants of God. Then people came from under the trees and from the graves, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, led us in prayer. May God bless him and grant him peace, and he incited the fighting, then he said: The Quraysh gathered at this red side of the mountain, so when they approached Our people were among us and we lined up with them. When a man from them was riding a red camel walking among the people, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He greeted me: O Ali, call Hamza for me, and he was the closest of them to the polytheists. Who is the owner of the red camel, and what does he say to them?"
"37835","(37835) Waki’ told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Sa’d, on the authority of his father, he said: I was correct. A sword on the day of Badr and I admired it, so I said: O Messenger of God, grant it to me. So the verses were revealed: {They ask you about the Anfal} verses.\n(Muslim 34, Ahmad 181)"
"37836","(37836) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; That Abu Jahl was the one who opened the Day of Badr and said: O God, which of us has been most merciful to you and most severe of his ties of kinship? Then the day came, and God revealed: {If you seek victory, victory has already come to you}"
"37837","(37837) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Yunus bin Abi Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Eizar bin Harith, he said: The herald of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called out on the day of Badr: None of the people, meaning safety, except Abu al-Bakhtari. So whoever was taken prisoner should let him go, for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had made him safe, but they found him killed."
"37838","(37838) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hashim al-Wasiti, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Qays ibn Abbad, He said: I heard Abu Dharr swear: These verses were revealed in these six groups on the day of Badr: Ali and Hamza. And Ubaidah bin Al-Harith, Utbah, Shaybah ibn Rabi’ah, and Al-Walid bin Utbah: {These are two adversaries who disputed In their Lord}"
"37839","(37839) Qarad Abu Nuh narrated to us, saying: Ikrimah bin Ammar Al-Ijli narrated to us, saying: Samak Al-Hanafi Abu narrated to us. A colleague, he said: Ibn Abbas told us, he said: Omar bin Al-Khattab told me, he said: When it was the day of Badr, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, looked May God bless him and grant him peace to his companions, who were three hundred and one-hundred. And he looked at the polytheists and saw that they were a thousand. And more, so he faced the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and then extended his hand, and was wearing his robe and garment. Then he said: Oh God, fulfill what You promised me. Oh God, if this group of people of Islam destroys you, you will never be worshiped on earth. He said: He continued to seek help from his Lord and to call upon Him until his robe fell off, so Abu Bakr came to him and said: So he took his robe. He sent him back, then followed him closely, then said: O Prophet of God, it is sufficient for you to appeal to your Lord, for He will accomplish for you what you He promised you, so God revealed: {When you sought help from your Lord, and He responded to you. Indeed, I will reinforce you with a thousand of the angels, in succession} When that day came and they met, God defeated the polytheists, killing seventy of them, and taking seventy of them prisoner. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, consulted Abu Bakr, Omar, and Ali, and Abu Bakr said: O Prophet of God,These are the cousins, the clan, and the brothers. I think you should take the ransom from them, and it will be what we took. Some of them are strong against the disbelievers, and perhaps God will guide them and they will be a support to us.\n Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: What do you see, O Ibn Al-Khattab? I said: By God, I do not see what Abu Bakr saw, but I think that you will enable me to kill so-and-so, a relative of Omar, so that I behead him. And Ali gained power over Aqeel and beheaded him, and Hamza gained power over his brother So-and-so and beheaded him, until God knows. Indeed, in our hearts there is no friendliness to the polytheists, these are your guides, your imams, and your leaders.\n So the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did what Abu Bakr said, and he did not like what I said, so he took a ransom from them.\n The next day, Omar said: I went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was sitting, and Abu Bakr was there. They were crying. He said: I said: O Messenger of God: Tell me what makes you and your friend cry? If I find you crying, I cry, and if I do not find crying, I cry because of your crying. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The one whose ransom your companions offered to me, your torment has already been offered to me closer than this tree, to a nearby tree.And God revealed: {It is not for a prophet to have captives until he has made a fortune in the land, and you desire the wealth of the world} to His saying: {Had it not been for a Book from God which had preceded to touch you concerning what you took} of ransom {a great punishment} Then He made lawful to them the spoils.\n When it was the day of Uhud of the following year, they were punished for what they had done on the day of Badr in that they had to pay ransom, and seventy of them were killed and fled. The Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his robes were broken, the white stones on his head were shattered, and blood flowed on him. His face, and God revealed: {Or when a calamity befell you, you befell the like of it. You said, “This is it.” Say, “Who is this?” With yourselves, indeed, God has power over all things}, by taking your ransom."
"37840","(37840) Abdah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father; Ruqaya, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to Badr. Othman was the wife of Othman, and Othman left behind, and Asama bin Zayd was at that time. While they were burying us, Othman heard Takbir, so he said: O Asama, see what this takbir is? Then he looked, and behold, it was Zayd bin Harithha on the camel of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Al-Jada’i, giving good news of the killing of the people of Badr was one of the polytheists, and the hypocrites said: No, by God, this is nothing. This is nothing but falsehood, until they were brought in handcuffs. Covered\n(Hakim 217. Bayaqi 174)"
"37841","(37841) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ubaidah Al-Salmani, he said: He was captured On the day of Badr, seventy men of the polytheists were among them, and seventy of them were killed, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gathered the Ansar. So he gave them a choice, and said: Whatever you wish, if you wish, you can kill them, and some of your number will be killed, and if you wish, you can take Their ransom, so you strengthened yourself with it in the way of God. They said: O Messenger of God, we take the ransom to strengthen yourself with it in the way of God. And some of them will be killed. Their number will be killed. He said: So some of them will be killed on the Day of Uhud. (Abdul Razzaq 9402)"
"37842","(37842) Abu Dawud Al-Hafari narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Zayd, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, On the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; Similar to the hadith of Abdul Rahim. (Tirmidhi 1567, Hakim 140)"
"37843","(37843) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Zaid bin Yathai’, he said: It was Abu Bakr was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the Day of Badr on the Arish. He said: So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, made He supplicates, saying: O God, help this band of people, for if you do not do so, you will not be worshiped on earth. Abu Bakr said: Some Your appeal to your Lord, by God, He will certainly fulfill for you what He promised you."
"37844","(37844) Zayd bin Harun told us, saying: Muhammad bin Ishaq informed us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Yahya bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Saad bin Zurarah said: He was brought with the captives of Badr, and Sawda bint Zam’i was married. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was with the family of Afraa in his mourning for them, for Awf and Mu’awwidha, the sons of Afraa, and that was before The veil was drawn over her. She said: He was brought with the captives, so I came to my house and saw Suhail bin Amr near you. Al-Hujra, gathered from his hand to his neck, and when I saw him, I could not control myself if I said: Abu Yazid, you have given With your hands, do not die with dignity. She said: By God, nothing informed me except the saying of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from within. Al-Bayt: Is it soudah: May God and His Messenger be exalted? I said: O Messenger of God, by God, if I could control myself wherever I saw Abu Yazid, I would say what you said. (Hakim 22)"
"37845","(37845) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amr ibn Murr, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: On the day of Badr, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: What do you say about these captives? Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of God, your people and your origin, stay ahead of them and seek refuge from them, perhaps God will turn to them, and he said Omar: O Messenger of God, they lied to you and drove you out. Bring them forward and we will behead them. Abdullah bin Rawahih said: O Messenger of God. By God, you are in a valley abounding with firewood, so the valley kindled a fire for them, then threw them into it. Al-Abbas said: God has cut it off. Have mercy on you, he said, but the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, remained silent and did not respond to them, then he got up and entered.\n Some people said: He takes the opinion of Abu Bakr, and some people said: He takes the opinion of Omar, and some people said: He takes the opinion of Abdullah bin his souls, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out and said: God will soften the hearts of men in him, until they are Softer than milk, and God hardens the hearts of men in it, until they are harder than stones, and indeed someone like you, O father. A firstborn like Abraham. He said: (Whoever follows me is of me, and whoever disobeys me is indeed Forgiving and Merciful.) And indeed, someone like you, O Abu Bakr, like Jesus, said: {If you punish them, they are your servants, and if you forgive them, then you are the Mighty, the Wise} And your example, O Umar, is that of Moses. He said, “Our Lord, destroy their wealth and strengthen their hearts, so they will not believe until they see it.” The painful punishment. And indeed, your parable, O Umar, is that of Noah. He said: {My Lord, do not leave on the earth an abode of the disbelievers.} You are exalted, so do not None of them will escape unless he has to ransom himself or be beheaded.\n Ibn Masoud said: O Messenger of God, except Suhayl bin Bayda, for I heard him mention Islam. He said: So I remained silent. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and you have never seen me more afraid that stones from the sky would fall on me than I did. Today, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Except Suhayl bin Bayda’, so God revealed: “It is not for a prophet to He will have captives until he grows thick in the land} until the end of the verse."
"37846","(37846) Abdullah told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was not killed on that day. Badr was patient, except for Uqba bin Abi Muait. (Abu Dawud 2679. Bayhaqi 64)"
"37847","(37847) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was not killed on the Day of Badr patiently except three: Uqba bin Abi Mu’it, and Al-Nadr bin Al-Harith, and Tuaimah bin Adi, and Al-Nadr was captured by Al-Miqdad."
"37848","(37848) Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father; A man captured Umayyah ibn Khalaf, and Bilal saw him and killed him."
"37849","(37849) Ahmad bin Abdullah narrated to us, saying: Zuhair narrated to us, saying: Sulayman al-Taymimi narrated to us, that Anas narrated to them. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Who will see what Abu Jahal did? He said: So Ibn Masoud went and found that Ibn Afra had beaten him until he was cold. He said: You are Abu Jahl, so he took hold of his beard. He said: And above a man whom you killed, or: A man whose people killed him. (Bukhari 3962, Muslim 118)"
"37850","(37850) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Abu Jal ibn Afra’ cut his hair, and shuffled it. Ali Ibn Masoud."
"37851","(37851) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Al-Mughiriya, on the authority of Thabit, who said: Abu Jal’s companions said to Abu Jal And he was walking to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace on the day of Badr: Did you see your march to Muhammad? Do you know that he is a prophet? He said: Yes, but when did we follow Abd Manaf?"
"37852","(37852) Waki’ told us, he said: My father told us, and Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, he said: He said: Abdullah: I went to Abu Jalal on the day of Badr, and his leg had been struck and he was epileptic, and he was defending the people from him. With his sword, I said: Praise be to God who has disgraced you, O enemy of God. He said: Is he anything but a man whose people killed him? He said: So I made I approached him with my sword, but it was useless, so I hit his hand, and his sword dangled, so I took it and hit him with it until he became cold, then I went out until I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, as if it were smaller than the earth, meaning speed, so I informed him, and he said: Is there any god but Him? He repeated it to me three times, then he went out and walked with me until he stood up to him and said: Praise be to God who has disgraced you, O enemy of God. This was the Pharaoh of this nation.\n Waki` said: My father added to it, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, he said: Abdullah said: So the Messenger of God sent me away. May God bless him and grant him peace."
"37853","(37853) Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaydah, on the authority of his father, He said: They were diminished in our eyes on the day of Badr, until I said to a friend of mine next to me: How many do you see? See them as seventy. He said: He showed them a hundred, until we took a man from them and asked him, and he said: We were a thousand."
"37854","(37854) Shazan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: He was killed On the day of Badr, five men from among the immigrants, from Quraysh; A refuge, the servant of Omar. He said: I am a refuge, and I seek refuge in my Lord. Dhu al-Shamalayn and Ibn Bayda were killed. And Ubaidah bin Al-Harith, and Amer bin Abi Waqqas."
"37855","(37855) Abu Asama narrated to us, he said: Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah narrated to me, he said: Thabit narrated to us, he said: With Omar bin Al-Khattab fought the war on the day of Badr, and no prisoner is brought without being rewarded for it. He said: When Al-Abbas was taken, he said to his captor: Do you know who I am? He said: No. He said: I am the uncle of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so do not take him to Omar. He said: So he seized him, and Aqeel was taken away. And he said to his captor: Do you know who I am? He said: No. He said: I am the cousin of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: So the people caught him."
"37856","(37856) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his father, meaning his grandfather, on the authority of the one with the misty face, He said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, after he had finished with the people of Badr with Ibn Faras, who is called Al-Qurha’i. So I said: O Muhammad, I have brought you Ibn al-Qurha’i so that you may take him. He said: I have no need for him, but if you want me to settle with you I did so with the chosen one from the armor of Badr, saying: I would not give you anything today for which I have no need. Then he said: Here Al-Jawshan, will you not surrender and be among the first of this matter? I said: No. He said: Why? I said: I saw that your people were in love with you. He said: How was what you heard about their struggles? I said: He has informed me. He said: How can I guide you? I said: If you conquer the Kaaba and capture it, he said: Perhaps if you live you will see that.\n Then he said: O Bilal, take the man’s bag and provide him with a piece of dough. When I turned away, he said: He is the best of the horsemen of my children. Amer, he said: By God, I am seeking refuge with my family when a rider came, so I said: Where are you from? He said: From Mecca. He said: I said: What did the people do? He said: By God, Muhammad defeated her and forced her to marry. So I said: My mother has confounded me. If I were to convert to Islam that day, then I would ask him. Al-Hira would have cut it off, saying: By God, I will never drink from a cup, nor will my life fart under a bud. (Musnad 559)"
"37857","(37857) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: It was said to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, when he finished Badr: You have to go through the camel, and you will have nothing to do with it. So Al-Abbas called out to him. And he is captive in his bonds: he is not fit, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Why? He said: God promised you one of the two groups, and He has given you what He promised you. (Tirmidhi 3080 and Ahmad 229)"
"37858","(37858) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of a man from the descendants of al-Zubayr, who said: He was with al-Zubayr on the day Badr was a yellow turban, shrouded in it, and the angels descended upon them, and yellow turbans were upon them."
"37859","(37859) Abdou told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Abbad bin Hamza, on the authority of Al-Zubair; In a similar way"
"37860","(37860) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood at the heart of Badr and said: Have you found what your Lord promised to be true? Then he said: They will now hear what I say. (Bukhari 3980, Muslim 643)"
"37861","(37861) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, who said: He was not with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Badr except Two knights, one of whom was Al-Zubayr."
"37862","(37862) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: I and Ibn Umar were presented to The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Badr, so we looked down, and we witnessed someone."
"37863","(37863) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, consulted when he was informed of the arrival of Abu Sufyan. He said: Then Abu Bakr spoke, and he declined. Then Omar spoke, but he turned away, and Saad bin Ubadah said: What do you want, O Messenger of God? By the One in whose hand is my soul, if you had commanded us to plunge it into the sea, we would have submerged it, and if you had commanded us to plunge its livers into Barak Al-Ghimad for our action. He said: So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mourned for the people.\n He said: So they set out until they stopped at Badr, and stories of Quraysh came to them, and among them was a black boy of the sons of al-Hajjaj, so they took him. Then the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to ask him about Abu Sufyan and his companions, and he would say: He has no knowledge. By Abu Sufyan, but this is Abu Jalal, Utbah, Shaybab, and Umayya bin Khalaf, so when he said that They beat him, and when they beat him, he said: Yes, I am telling you, this is Abu Sufyan. When they left him, he said: What is the matter with him? He knew about Abu Sufyan, but this is Abu Jalal, Utbah, Shaybab, and Umayyah ibn Khalaf among the people, so when he said This man they also beat.\n The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was standing and praying. When he saw that, he left and said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, you You will strike him when he tells the truth, and leave him when he tells you a lie. He said: And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: This The death of so-and-so, he lays his hand on the ground here and there, and not one of them strayed from the place of the hand of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. (Muslim 1403. Abu Dawud 2674)"
"37864","(37864) Shababah bin Siwar narrated to us, saying: Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit, he said: Anas narrated to us, he said: We were with Omar between Mecca and Medina, looking out for the crescent moon, and I saw it and was keen-sighted, so I started saying to Omar: What? Do you see it? Then Omar looked but did not see him, so Omar said: I will see him while I am lying on my bed, then he began to tell us about the people of Badr. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to see what the people of Badr fought yesterday, and he said: This is the death of so-and-so tomorrow, if he wishes. By God, this is the death of so-and-so tomorrow, God willing. He said: By those whom He sent with the truth, they had not missed those borders and would be struck down. Aliyah\n Then they were placed in a well, one on top of another, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, set off until he came to them and said: O so-and-so, son of so-and-so, and O so-and-so, son of so-and-so: Did you find what God and His Messenger promised you to be true? Omar said: O Messenger of God, how can you speak to bodies that have no souls? He said: You do not listen better to what I say than they do, except that they cannot respond to me anything. (Ahmad 26. Abu Ali 135)"
"37865","(37865) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Sulayman al-Taymi informed us, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Qais bin Abbad. He said: Ali, Hamza, Ubaidah bin Al-Harith, Utbah bin Rabi’ah, and Shaybah bin Rabi’ah competed. And Al-Walid bin Utba, so the following verse was revealed about them: {These are two adversaries who disputed concerning their Lord}"
"37866","(37866) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Yunus informed us, on the authority of Abu Al-Sifar, he said: The herald of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called out. May God bless him and grant him peace on the day of Badr: Whoever takes Umm Hakim bint Hizam prisoner, let him free her, for the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, He gave her peace and secured her, so a man from the Ansar took her prisoner and wrapped her clothes around her. When he heard the call of the Messenger of God, leave her on her way."
"37867","(37867) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Abu Nazrha: {And whoever is in charge of them will turn back from that day except one retreating to battle. Or siding with a faction} It was revealed on the day of Badr, and it was not for them to side with a group, and if they sided, they would only side with The polytheists\n(Abu Dawud 2641. An-Nasa’i 8654)"
"37868","(37868) Shababah bin Siwar told us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, who said: He was your cousin. Harithah set out with the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on the day of Badr. He set out as a young overseer. He did not set out to fight, but he was struck by an arrow. So he killed him, and his maternal aunt came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, son of Harith. In Paradise, I was patient and sought reward. Otherwise, you will see what I will do. He said: O Umm Harithah, this is a large Paradise, and indeed Haritha in the highest paradise. (Ahmad 215. Tabarani 3234)"
"37869","(37869) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Juma’, he said: Abu Al-Tufayl narrated to us, he said: Hudhayfah bin narrated to us. Al-Yaman, he said: Nothing prevented me from witnessing Badr except that I and Abu Husayl went out. He said: Then the infidels of Quraysh captured us. They said: Do you want Muhammad? So we said: We do not want it. We only want Medina. So they took from us God’s covenant and covenant that we would go to Medina, and not We fight with him, so we came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and told him the news, and he said: Go away, we will deny them, and we will seek help. May Allah be upon them."
"37870","(37870) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Ibn Al-Ghaseel narrated to us, on the authority of Hamza bin Abi Asid, on the authority of his father, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on the day of Badr when we lined up for the Quraysh and they lined up for us: If they defeat you, So shoot them with arrows.\n(Bukhari 2900 and Abu Dawud 2456)"
"37871","(37871) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Talhah was the one who had his own opinion. The polytheists on the day of Badr, and Ali bin Abi Talib killed him in a duel."
"37872","(37872) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Ikrimah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on the Day of Badr: Whoever among you meets anyone from Banu Hashim, let him not kill him. They were expelled by force."
"37873","(37873) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Al-Haytham, Ibrahim Al-Taymiy said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, killed a man from the polytheists of Quraysh on the day of Badr, and crucified him to a tree."
"37874","(37874) Aidh bin Habib told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Muqasim, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The people of Badr were three hundred and thirteen, the emigrants of whom were seventy-five, and the defeat of Badr was For the seventeenth of Ramadan, the night of Friday."
"37875","(37875) Aidh bin Habib told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: The people of Badr were three One hundred and twelve, of whom are seventy-six immigrants. (Ahmad 248 Bazzar 1783)"
"37876","(37876) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of al-Bara’ bin Aazib, who said: It was The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Badr were twelve hundred and thirteen, and we used to say that they were numbered. The companions of Taloot who crossed the river with him, and no one crossed with him except a believer. (Bukhar 3957)"
"37877","(37877) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ubaidah, he said: He counted those who testified with The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, at Badr, the number of those who crossed the river with Talut, I counted them as three hundred and thirteen."
"37878","(37878) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit bin Amara, on the authority of Ghanim bin Qays, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: He was a number The companions of Taloot on the Day of Goliath are three hundred and twelve hundred."
"37879","(37879) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan and Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’ ibn Azib, who said: The number of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was three hundred and twelve, and they believed that they were numbered. The companions of Talut on the Day of Goliath, those who crossed the river with him, and no one crossed the river with him except a believer."
"37880","(37880) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muadh bin Rifa’i bin Rafi’ al-Ansari. ; An angel came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: How are the people of Badr among you? He said: The best of people. Then the king said: And so are the angels who witnessed a full moon."
"37881","(37881) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Muhammad, that Ubaid Allah bin Abi Rafi’ was a scribe. Ali told him that he heard Ali say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He witnessed Badr, meaning Hatib bin Abi Balta’a, and who knows, perhaps God has looked at the people of Badr and said: Do whatever you want, for I have forgiven. punch"
"37882","(37882) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, he said: I heard Ali: He says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Is he not one of the people of Badr? And what makes you know? Perhaps God looked at the people of Badr and said: Do whatever you want, for Paradise has been guaranteed for you. (Bukhari 3081, Muslim 1942)"
"37883","(37883) Abu Asama told us, he said: Omar bin Hamza told us, he said: Salem told me, he said: Ibn Omar told me; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Omar: What makes you know? Perhaps God has looked at the people of Badr, and he said: Do whatever you want. (Ahmad 1097, Abu Ali 5497)"
"37884","(37884) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Asim bin Abi Al-Najjoud, on the authority of Abu Salih On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Indeed, God, Blessed and Most High, looked at the people of Badr. He said: Do whatever you want, for I have forgiven you."
"37885","(37885) Shababi bin Siwar narrated to us, saying: Laith informed us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir; Abd Lahatib bin Abi Balta’a came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to complain to Hatib, and he said: O Messenger of God, The arsonist will enter the Fire, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: You lied, he will not enter it, for he witnessed a full moon. And Al-Hudaybiyya."
"37886","(37886) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Abaya bin Rifa’i, on the authority of His grandfather, Rafi’ bin Khadij, said: Gabriel, or an angel, came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: What do you think of? Did a full moon witness among you? He said: Our choice. He said: Likewise, with us they are the choice of the angels. (Ibn Majah 1600 and Ahmad 465)"
"37887","(37887) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Al-Dahhak; {And whoever will be in charge of them that day will turn away} He said: This is the day of Badr in particular."
"37888","(37888) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan; {And whoever is in charge of them on that day will turn away from him except one retreating to fight, or joining a group} He said: This is the day of a special full moon. Fleeing on foot is not a major sin."
"37889","(37889) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a ransom The Arab on the day of Badr was forty uqiyahs, and he made the ransom of the servant twenty uqiyahs, the uqiyah being forty dirhams."
"37890","(37890) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Al-Zinad, who said: Al-Safi was on the day of Badr under the sword of Asim bin Munabbih bin Al-Hajjaj"
"37891","(37891) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Amr, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Jubayr Bin Mutim said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to ransom the people of Badr. (Bukhari 3050, Ahmed 84)"
"37892","(37892) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, who said: We were talking about his saying: {On the Day of We will strike with the greatest assault} on the day of Badr, and the smoke has passed."
"37893","(37893) Waki’ told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: On the day of Badr, I, Ammar, and Saad participated in what we struck on the day of Badr. As for Ammar and I, we did not bring anything, and he came. Saad with two captives."
"37894","(37894) Abdul Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Ata’, he said: Suhail bin Amr is a man more knowledgeable than his lower lip. Omar bin Al-Khattab said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day he was captured at Badr: Messenger of God, remove his two lower folds and his tongue will stick out, and he will never speak to you in a foreign place. He said: No. I act, and God acts as an example through me."
"37895","(37895) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: The spoils were not permissible for a black-headed people before you. Fire used to come down from the sky and consume it, so when On the day of Badr, people hurried to the spoils, so God revealed: {If it had not been a book from God, a great punishment would have touched you while you took. So eat of what you have gained, lawful and good."
"37896","(37896) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Masoudi told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, he said: The first to be martyred among On the day of Badr, Muslims will be a haven of refuge."
"37897","(37897) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, plotted. He, peace be upon him, greeted the polytheists on the day of Uhud, and it was the first day on which he plotted against them."
"37898","(37898) Abu Asama told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwah told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: When it was On the day of Uhud, the polytheists were defeated, and Iblis shouted: O servants of God, I am the last of you. He said: Then their relatives returned and fought against him. And the last of them, he said: Then Hudhafi looked and saw his father, Al-Eman, and he said: Servants of God, my father, my father. She said: By God, they did not detain him until they had killed him. Then Hudhayfa said: May God forgive you. Urwah said: By God, she is still in Hudhayfa. What remains is better until he joins God."
"37899","(37899) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: When it was the day of Uhud and he left The polytheists, and the Muslims saw their brothers as a bad example. They began to cut off their ears and noses, and cut them open. Their bellies, so the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If God grants us some of them, we will certainly do it and we will do it, so God revealed: {And if you punish, then punish with the same as what you were punished with, and if you are patient, indeed, it is better for those who are patient.} Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Rather, we are patient. (Ibn Jarir 1951, Ahmad 135)"
"37900","(37900) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Hashim, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: I heard him. He says: Saad was the most powerful of the Muslims on the Day of Uhud."
"37901","(37901) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Umair bin Ishaq; The people turned away from the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on the day of Uhud, and Sa’d bin Malik was shooting, and a young man was being noble for him. Whenever his arrows ran out, he handed over his arrows to him, then said: Throw him away, Abu Ishaq. When he was after that, they asked for the young man, but he did not. They have power over it."
"37902","(37902) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, on the authority of Ali bin Abi A student, he said: I did not hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ransom anyone with his parents except Saad, for I heard him say On the day of Uhud: Accuse Saad, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you."
"37903","(37903) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, he said: I heard Sa’d, He says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gathered his parents for me on the day of Uhud."
"37904","(37904) Muhammad bin Bishr and Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Saad, He said: I saw to the right of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and to his left, on the Day of Uhud, two men wearing clothes. White, I have not seen them before or after."
"37905","(37905) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Umair ibn Ishaq, who said: Hamza used to fight hand-to-hand. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the Day of Uhud with two swords, and saying: I am the lion of God. He said: So he began to face and turn away. So he stumbled and fell on his back, lying down, and was scraped, and the armor on his stomach was exposed, so the Ethiopian slave saw him and bit him. With a spear, or a spear, so he executed him with it."
"37906","(37906) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr; {And do not think that those who were killed in the cause of God are dead, but rather alive with their Lord and being provided for.} He said: When Hamza bin Abdul Muttalib and Musaab bin Umair on the day of Uhud, they said: I wish our brothers knew what good we have befallen. Their desire increased, so God said: I will convey the news about you. Then it was revealed: {And do not think that those who are killed in the way of God are dead}) To his saying: {The believers}"
"37907","(37907) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Usama ibn Zayd, he said: Al-Zuhri narrated to us, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by Hamzah on the day of Uhud while he was being mutilated, so he stood over him and said: Had it not been that I fear that she will find my purity within herself; I would have left it until good health had consumed it, and it would have been gathered from its bellies. Then he called for a tiger, and when it was spread over his head His legs appeared, and when his legs were extended, his head appeared, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Stretched out on him. His head, and put the sheep on his feet, and the clothes were few, and the killings were many, so there was one man, two men, and three They would be shrouded in a garment, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, would ask which of them had the most recited Qur’an, and he would present it to him. \n(Abu Dawud 3128 and Ahmad 128)"
"37908","(37908) Shababah narrated to us, saying: Laith bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ka’b bin Malik. Jabir bin Abdullah told him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to combine the two men who killed someone in the same garment, and then he would say: Which of them recites the Qur’an the most? So when one of them was pointed out to him, he brought it into the grave and said: I am a witness over these on the Day of Resurrection, and ordered He buried them in their blood, and did not pray over them, nor did they wash them."
"37909","(37909) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Usama ibn Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of May God’s prayers and peace be upon him on the day of Uhud, while the wives of Banu Abd al-Ashhal were crying over their daughters, and he said: But Hamza was not crying for him, so the women of the Ansar came crying for Hamza, and he fell asleep and woke up, and he said: Oh And are they here even now? They were marooned, so let them return, and do not weep over someone who has perished after today."
"37910","(37910) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Khabab, who said: We emigrated with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God’s peace and blessings be upon him. We seek the face of God, so our reward has become obligatory for God. Among us are those who passed away who did not eat any of His reward. Musaab bin Umair was killed on the day of Uhud, and there was nothing to shroud him with except a tiger. When they placed it on His head came out and his legs came out, and when they put it on his feet his head came out, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Make it of what turns its head, and make it of Idhkhir upon its feet, and among us is he whose fruit is abundant, so he is He guides her."
"37911","(37911) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to me, saying: Muhammad ibn Salih narrated to me, saying: Yazid ibn Zayd, my father’s client, narrated to me. Usaid Al-Badri, on the authority of Abu Usaid, said: We are with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at the grave of Hamza, so the tiger stretched out On his head and his legs were uncovered, so he was pulled over his feet and his head was uncovered, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Stretch it over his head, and put the trees of the Haramal tree on his feet.”"
"37912","(37912) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of his father, on the authority of elders from the Ansar, who said: He came The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, killed two people on the day of Uhud, Abdullah bin Amr bin Haram and Amr bin Jamuh, and he said: Bury them both in one grave, for they were pure in this world."
"37913","(37913) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, he said: My father told me, on the authority of men from Banu Salama, They said: When Muawiyah turned away from the eye that passes over the graves of martyrs, it ran over them, and their graves emerged, and he cried out. upon them, so We brought them out two by two, as if they had died yesterday, upon them were two cloaks with which they had been covered. Their faces, and on their feet, are made of the Izker plant."
"37914","(37914) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Qays, on the authority of Nabih, on the authority of Jabir, who said: Abu Abd said to me God: O my son, if it were not for women whom I will succeed after me as sisters and daughters, I would love to present you before me, but be in The overseers of the city, he said: I did not wait long before she brought two of her paternal uncles, meaning his father and paternal uncle, to them. On a camel."
"37915","(37915) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He was killed A man from the polytheists on the day of Uhud. The polytheists wanted to pay him off, but he refused. So they gave him money until he reached the level of blood money, but he refused."
"37916","(37916) Khaled bin Mukhlid told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Ismail told us, he said: Abdul Rahman bin Thabit told me, And Dawud bin Al-Husayn, on the authority of Al-Farisi, the client of Banu Muawiyah; He struck a man on the day of Uhud and killed him, and he said: Take her, and I will be the Persian boy. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: : What prevented you from saying: The Ansari and you are one of them? Indeed, the master of the people is among them."
"37917","(37917) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Humaid told us, on the authority of Anas bin Malik; That his uncle was absent from the battle of Badr, so he said: I was absent from the first battle in which the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fought the polytheists. By God, if God wanted me to fight the polytheists, God would show me what I would do. When it was the day of Uhud, the Muslims were revealed, so he said : Oh God, I apologize to you for what these people have done, meaning the Muslims, and I disavow before you what these people have brought. Meaning the polytheists, and he came forward and Saad met him at the end of it, without anyone, so Saad said: I am with you. Saad said: I was not able to I did what he did, and eighty-one people were found on him, striking him with a sword, stabbing him with a spear, and shooting him with an arrow, so we used to say: About him and his companions the following verse was revealed: {And among them are those whose love has died, and among them are those who wait}"
"37918","(37918) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Hammam told us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab; Indeed, the slain of Uhud were washed."
"37919","(37919) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, who said: I saw Talha’s hand. Ibn Ubaidullah Shala, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, met her on the day of Uhud."
"37920","(37920) Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, who said: Hamza ibn Abd al-Muttalib was killed. On the day of Uhud, Hanzalah bin Al-Rahib, who was purified by the angels, was killed on the day of Uhud."
"37921","(37921) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: I was presented to the Messenger of May God bless him and grant him peace on the day of Uhud when I was fourteen years old, so they looked down upon me, and I appeared to him on the day of the ditch when I was Ibn Abd al-Aziz, so he granted me permission. Nafi’ said: I narrated it to Omar bin Abdul Aziz, and he said: This is a punishment between the two minors. And the eldest, so he wrote to his workers: To make an allotment for the son of fifteen years in the fight, and for the son of fourteen years in Offspring"
"37922","(37922) Ali bin Ubaid narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Amr narrated to us, on the authority of Saad bin Al-Mundhir, he said: The Messenger of God came out May God bless him and grant him peace to Uhud. When he left his farewell prayer, he looked behind him and saw a rough booklet. He said: Who? These? They said: Abdullah bin Ubayy bin Salul and his followers were Jews. He said: Have they converted to Islam? They said: No, but on their religion. He said: Tell them, let them return, for we do not seek help from the polytheists against the polytheists."
"37923","(37923) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Omar bin Qatada; Qatadah ibn al-Numan’s eye fell on his cheek on the day of Uhud, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, restored it. It was the most beautiful and one of the eyes."
"37924","(37924) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Mu’ammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Jabir; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered that the people be killed on the day of Uhud and covered with their blood, and that most of them be presented by taking. According to the Qur’an, and that two should be buried in a grave. He said: So I buried my father and my uncle in a grave. (Ibn Majah 1514 and Abd al-Razzaq 6633)"
"37925","(37925) Zaid bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, who said: Muhammad bin Thabit narrated to me; On the day of Uhud, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Mus’ab has arrived, and Abdul Rahman said to him: O Messenger of God, did not Is Mus'ab killed? He said: Yes, but an angel took his place, and he was called by his name."
"37926","(37926) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdullah, He said: On the day of Uhud, the women used to treat the wounded, give them water to drink, and treat the wounded."
"37927","(37927) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Thabit told us, on the authority of Anas; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took a sword on the day of Uhud and said: Who will take this from me? So they spread out their hands, and each one of them began to say: I, I, then he said: Who will hold him accountable? He said: So the people refrained, and Samak Abu Dujanan said: I will take it as he deserves it. He said: So he took it, and he broke up with him. The polytheists (Muslim 1917. Ahmad 123)"
"37928","(37928) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He saw someone and said: This is a mountain that loves us and we love it. (Muslim 993)"
"37929","(37929) Hashim bin Al-Qasim narrated to us, saying: Shu’ba narrated to us, on the authority of the ruling, he said: The prayer was not performed on them and they were not washed. It means killing someone."
"37930","(37930) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Amer, who said: On the day of Uhud, the nose of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was injured. May God bless him and grant him peace and his quartets, and he claimed that Talhah protected the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with his hand, but he was struck and failed. His finger (Ibn Saad 217)"
"37931","(37931) Abdullah bin Bakr Al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Abu Talha, he said: I was among those who Drowsiness descended upon him on the day of Uhud, to the point that my sword fell from my hand repeatedly."
"37932","(37932) Aswad bin Amir told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ali bin Zaid and Thabit told us, on the authority of Anas; When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, massacred them on the Day of Uhud, he said: Who will ward them off from Us while they are in Paradise? Then a man from the Ansar stood up and fought until he was killed, then another man stood up and repulsed them until he was killed, until seven people were killed. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: We have not done justice to our companions. (Muslim 1415, Abu Ali 3306)"
"37933","(37933) Zaid bin Hubab narrated to us, saying: Musa bin Ubaidah narrated to us, saying: Abdullah bin Ubaid informed me, on the authority of Abu Salih, the client of Umm Hani’; Al-Harith bin Suwayd pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and believed in him. Then he followed the people of Mecca and saw Uhud. So he fought the Muslims, then he was captured. He returned to Mecca and wrote to his brother Jalas bin Suwayd: O my brother, I regret what I did, so I repent to God and return to Islam, so mention that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him. If you desire his repentance, write to him. He mentioned it to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and God revealed: {How can God guide a people who disbelieved after their belief?} He said: Then some of his companions who were upon him said: He will refrain, then He returned to Islam, so God revealed: {Indeed, those who disbelieved after their belief, and then increased in disbelief, their repentance will not be accepted. And those are the ones who are astray. (Nasa’i 3531, Ahmad 247)"
"37934","(37934) Zaid bin Hubab told us, he said: Musa bin Ubaidah told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ka’b Al-Qurazi told me; That Ali met Fatimah on the day of Uhud, and he said: Take the sword, it is not reprehensible. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Oh. Ali, if you fought well today, then Abu Dujanan, Mus’ab bin Umair, and Al-Harith bin Al-Sammi have done well. And Sahil bin Hanif; Three Ansar, and a man from Quraysh."
"37935","(37935) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: Ali came with his sword, and he said: Take it. Praiseworthy, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If you fought well today, then Saul bin Hanif has done well. And Asim bin Thabit, and Al-Harith bin Al-Samma, and Abu Dujaniya, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Who took this? The sword is true? So Abu Dujani said: I am, and he took the sword and struck with it until he brought it with it bent over, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He said: Did you give him what he deserved? He said: Yes."
"37936","(37936) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al Harith bin Nawfal. ; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was met by a man from the polytheists on the day of Uhud, walking in prayer, so the Messenger of God met him. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he walked and said:\nI am the Prophet who is not lying. I am the son of Abdul Muttalib.\n He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, struck him and killed him."
"37937","(37937) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ata bin Al-Sa’ib told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; On the day of Uhud, a woman handed a sword to her son, but he could not bear it, so she pulled it tightly around his forearm, then she came. With him the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: O Messenger of God, this is my son fighting on your behalf, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: O son, carry this here, O son, carry this here. He was wounded, so he was struck down, and he was brought to him. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: My son, perhaps you are alarmed? He said: No, O Messenger of God."
"37938","(37938) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ata bin Al-Sa’ib told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ibn Masoud. ; On the day of Uhud, women were behind the Muslims, punishing the wounds of the polytheists. If I had sworn on that day, I would have hoped to be vindicated. Indeed, none of us desires this world until God has revealed: {Among you are those who desire this world, and among you are those who desire the next, Then He turned you away from them in order to test you.\n When the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, violated the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and disobeyed what they were commanded to do, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent away. May God bless him and grant him peace among nine people, seven of the Ansar and two men of Quraysh, and he was the tenth of them. When they recovered from him, he said: May God have mercy on a man who turned them away from us. He said: Then a man from the Ansar stood up and fought him until he was killed. When they recovered from him also, he said: Have mercy. God sent a man back from us, and he did not stop talking until the seven were killed. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to his companion: What? We were fair to our companions.\n Then Abu Sufyan came and said: Is it better? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Say: God is Most High and Most Majestic, so he said Abu Sufyan: We have Uzza, but you do not have Uzza. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Say: God is our Master, and the disbelievers do not. A servant of them,\n Abu Sufyan said: One day after the day of Badr.\n A day for us, a day against us, a day for women, and a day for victory.\n Hanzalah for Hanzalah, and so-and-so for so-and-so, and so-and-so for so-and-so, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No, it is the same. As for the two of us killed Then those alive will be provided with sustenance, and those who kill you will be tortured in the Fire. Then Abu Sufyan said: There has been among the people someone like that, even if It was without my control. I neither commanded nor forbade, nor did I like nor dislike, nor did I compel nor did I please. He said: So they looked. Then, behold, Hamza had his stomach ripped open, and Hind took his liver and ate it, but was unable to eat it. Then the Messenger of God said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Did you eat any of it? They said: No. He said: God would not cause any of Hamza to enter the Fire.\n Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, placed Hamza and prayed over him, and a man from the Ansar was brought and he was placed next to him. So he prayed over him, and the Ansari rose and left Hamza, then another one was brought and he placed him next to Hamza and he prayed over him, then He was raised and left Hamza, then someone else was brought and placed next to Hamza and he prayed over him, then he was raised and Hamza was left, until... He prayed seventy prayers for him that day. (Ahmad 463. Ibn Saad 13)"
"37939","(37939) Muhammad bin Marwan told us, on the authority of Amara bin Abi Hafsah, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace May the peace and blessings of God be upon him in his face on the day of Uhud, and his quads were broken, and he became thirsty, until he fell on his knees. And his companions left him, so Ubayy bin Khalaf came and asked him for the blood of his brother Umayyah bin Khalaf, and he said: Where is this? He claims to be a prophet, so let him stand out to me, for if he was a prophet he would have killed me. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: They gave you the war, and they said: O Messenger of God, are you on the move? He said: Indeed, I have asked God for his blood to drink. So he took the spear, then walked to him and stabbed him, so he threw him off his animal and carried him. His companions asked him to rescue him, and they said to him: We do not see any harm in you. He said: Indeed, God has asked for my blood to drink. Indeed, I will find something wrong with you. It was on Rabi'a and Mudhar, it would be ample for them."
"37940","(37940) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Zubayr, Like him"
"37941","(37941) Ahmad bin Abdullah told us, he said: Abu Bakr told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: When Hamzah was killed on the day of Uhud, Safiyyah came looking for him, not knowing what he had done. He said: She met Ali and Al-Zubair. He said: Ali to Al-Zubair: Mention it to your mother, and Al-Zubair said: No, rather mention it to your paternal aunt. She said: What did Hamza do? He said: He showed her that they did not know. He said: Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and said: I fear for her mind. He said: So he placed his hand on her chest and prayed for her. He said: Then she recovered and wept. He said: Then he came and rose over her, and he acted With him, he said: Were it not for the women’s alarm, they would have left him until he was gathered from the crops of birds and the bellies of wild beasts. He said: Then he ordered him to be killed and he made He would pray upon them, he said: Then he would place nine times and Hamzah, and he would say “Allahu Akbar” to them seven times, then they would raise it and leave. Hamza, then he would come with nine times, and he would say “Allahu Akbar” to them seven times until he had finished with them. (Ibn Majah 1513. Tabarani 2936)"
"37942","(37942) Khaled bin Mukhlid narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman bin Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, saying: Al-Zuhri narrated to us, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Kaab bin Malik, on the authority of his father; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on the day of Uhud: Who saw the killing of Hamza? Then an unarmed man said: I saw him killed. He said: So go and show us him. So he went out until he stopped upon Hamzah and saw that he had been maimed. His stomach, and he mutilated it, so he said: O Messenger of God, mutilate it, by God. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, thought that He looked at her, and stood between the backs of the dead, and said: I am a witness against these people. They were killed. Their blood, for no wounded person can be wounded, except his wound on the Day of Resurrection will be bloody, its color is the color of blood, and its smell is the smell Musk, present the Qur’an to the people who recite the Qur’an, and put it in the grave."
"37943","(37943) Suleiman bin Harb told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Humaid bin Hilal, on the authority of Saad Ibn Hisham Ibn Amer, on the authority of his father, said: He complained to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about his severe wounds on the day of Uhud. So he said: Dig, make spacious, do good, and bury the two and three in the grave, and present most of them with the Qur’an. So they presented My father is between the hands of two men. (Abu Dawud 3207, Ahmed 19)"
"37944","(37944) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Adiy ibn Thabit, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Zayd, on the authority of Zayd ibn Thabit. He said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to Uhud, some people went out with him, and they returned. He said: They were the companions of the Messenger of God. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, divided among them two groups; One group said: We will kill them, and another group said: No, we will kill them. So it was revealed: “What have you to do with the hypocrites? Two groups, by God. Punish them for what they have earned. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Indeed, it is pure, and it expels evil. Just as fire expels the impurities from silver."
"37945","(37945) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: Hisham al-Dastawwi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: He shouted Until We killed them on the day of Uhud, when Mu'awiyah was wounded by the eye, so We extracted them after forty years to soften their bodies. Their limbs are bent."
"37946","(37946) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Abu Talha, he said: I raised my head. On the day of Uhud, I started to look, and I did not see any of the people lying under his armpit from drowsiness."
"37947","(37947) Malik narrated to us, he said: Ya’qub bin Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Abi Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Ibn Abza, He said: Ali came out on the day of Uhud from the Banu Shayba, Talha and Musaffa. He said: And he named another man. He said: So he killed them just as he had killed From the people, and he said to Fatima where he descended: It is not reprehensible to take the sword. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If you You have done well, so-and-so the Ansari, and so-and-so the Ansari, and so-and-so the Ansari did so until he stopped breathing, or almost He stops breathing."
"37948","(37948) Yahya bin Abdul-Malik bin Abi Ghaniyya told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: When it was broken On the day of Uhud, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The wrath of God intensified upon me. Three; On the one who claimed that he was the owner of the kingdoms, and the wrath of God was intensified on the one who broke the quadrilateral of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He affected his countenance, and God’s wrath intensified against whoever claimed that God had a son."
"37949","(37949) Khalid bin Mukhlid narrated to us, saying: Malik bin Anas narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of a man, who said: The eggs were smashed on the head of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Uhud, and his four-blade bracelet was broken, and he was wounded in the chest. His face was covered with a burning mat, and Ali bin Abi Talib was carrying water to him in the hujf. (Bukhari 243)"
"37950","(37950) Abu Asama told us, he said: Hammad bin Zayd told us, on the authority of Ayyub, he said: Abdul Rahman bin Abi Bakr said: To Abu Bakr: I saw you on the day of Uhud and spoke about you. He said: Abu Bakr said: But if I had seen you, I would not have spoken about you."
"37951","(37951) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Amr informed us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Aisha, She said: I went out on the day of the trench, tracing the tracks of the people, and I heard the roar of the earth behind me. I turned around and saw that I was with Saad bin Muadh. And with him was his nephew, Al-Harith bin Aws, carrying a shield, so I sat on the ground. She said: Then Sa’d passed by, wearing a shield. His limbs left her, so I fear for Sa’d’s limbs. She said: He was one of the greatest and tallest of people. She said: So he passed. He shudders and says:\nWait a little while and the excitement will overtake you. Bear what a good death when the time has come.\n She said: So I got up and stormed into a garden, and there was a group of Muslims there. Among them was Omar bin Al-Khattab, and among them was a man. May God bless him, meaning the Forgiver. He said: Then Omar said: Woe to you, what brought you here? Woe to you, what brought you here? By God, you are indeed bold. What is your guarantee that there will be hardship and affliction? She said: They continued to blame me until I wished that the earth would split open and I could enter it. She said: Then the man removed the tan from his face. Then, when Talha bin Ubaidullah spoke, he said: O Umar, woe to you, you have increased since today, and where is the bias? Flee except to Allah.She said: A man from the polytheists of Quraysh, called Hibban ibn al-Irqi, was shooting Sa`d with an arrow, and he said: Take her and me. Ibn al-Irqā, so he injured his eyelid and cut it, so he called upon God and said: Oh God, do not let me die until you make my eyes happy with my Quran. And they were his allies and loyalists in the pre-Islamic period. She said: His speech was clear, and God sent the wind upon the polytheists: (And God is sufficient for the believers in fighting, and God is Powerful, Mighty.) So Abu Sufyan joined Tihamah, and Aynah bin Badr joined him. Bin Hisn and those with him in Najd, and Banu Qurayza returned and barricaded themselves in their camps, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned. He was delivered to Medina, and he ordered that it be covered, so Saad was attacked in the mosque, and the weapon was placed.\n She said: Then Gabriel came to him and said: Have you laid down the weapon? By God, the angels have not laid down their weapons, so go out to the Banu Quraysh and fight them. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded: He greeted his departure and put on his clothes, so he went out and passed by the people of Bani Ghanam, who were neighbors of the mosque, and he said: Who passed by you? They said: Al-Kalbi passed by us, and his beard, teeth, and face resembled Gabriel. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to them and besieged them for twenty-five days.When their besiegement became severe and the calamities became more severe, they were told: Admit to the ruling of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So they consulted Abu Lubabah, and he indicated to them with his hand that it was to be slaughtered. They said: We will reveal the ruling of Ibn Muadh, so the Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: They descended upon the ruling of Sa’d bin Muadh, so they descended, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was sent to Sa’d. Then he was carried on a donkey with saddlebags of fiber, and his people surrounded him, and they started saying: O Abu Amr, your allies and your loyalists. And the people of spite and those whom you have known. She said: He does not return a word to them, even when he approaches their homes he turns to his people. Then he said: How is it that Saad does not care about God when he is blamed by a blameworthy person? When he appeared to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said Abu Saeed: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Go to your master and take him down. Omar said: Our master God, he said: They took it down, so they took it down.\n The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Judge them. He said: For I judge them that the woman who fights them should be killed. Their descendants will be taken captive, and their wealth will be divided. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: You have judged them according to the judgment of God. And His Messenger ruled. He said: Then God called Saad.He said: Oh God, if you have spared your Prophet from the war of Quraysh at all, then spare me for it, and if you have cut off the war between him and them, so take me to you, and he said: Then his words gushed out, and he had been healed until all that was left of him except an example NS\n She said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned, and Saad returned to his dome over which the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had beaten him. May God bless him and grant him peace. She said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr and Omar attended him. She said: So who My soul is in His hand. Indeed, I know Abu Bakr’s crying from Omar’s crying while I was in my room, and they were as God Almighty said: {Merciful among them} Alqamah said: So I said: Oh, his mother, so what did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, do? She said: His eyes did not shed tears for anyone, but whenever he was around, he was just holding his beard."
"37952","(37952) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr told us, he said: Asim bin Omar bin Qatada told me, he said When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, slept in the evening, Gabriel came to him, or he said: an angel, and said: Who is a man from your nation? He died at night, were the people of heaven rejoiced about his death? He said: No, unless it is Saad, for he was in a bad evening. What did Saad do? They said: O Messenger of God, he has been arrested, and his people came and carried him to their home. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed. He said the dawn greetings, then he went out, and the people left, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spent the night and greeted the people while walking, so much so that the covers of their sandals They will be cut off from their feet, and if you cloak them, they will fall off their shoulders. Then a man said: O Messenger of God, the people have spent the night, and he said: Indeed. I fear that the angels will precede us to Him, just as they preceded us to Hanzala.\n Muhammad said: Then Ash’ath bin Ishaq informed me, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, attended him while he was washing. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, knelt down and said: An angel entered and there was no place for him, so I made room for him. And his mother was crying and saying:\nWoe to the mother of Saad, Saad."
"37953","(37953) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: It was given to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He handed over a silk garment, and they began to marvel at its softness. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: For Saad’s handkerchiefs in Paradise. Softer than what you see."
"37954","(37954) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, he said: Zuhair narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Al-Muhallab bin Abi Safari. He says, and he mentioned the Haruriyya and their overnight stay, and he said: The companions of Muhammad said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on the day He dug the trench, and he was afraid that Abu Sufyan would make them spend the night. “If you spend the night, then your claim is forbidden, they will not be helped.”"
"37955","(37955) Muhammad bin Fudail told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The throne shook. For the love of meeting God, Sa`d. He said: He only means the bed. He said: {And his parents were raised on the throne.} He said: His sticks rotted. He said: He entered. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, buried him in his grave and was detained. When he came out, they said: O Messenger of God, what imprisoned you? He said: Saad was held in the grave, so I prayed to God to uncover him."
"37956","(37956) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May the peace and blessings of God be upon him: The throne was shaken by the death of Saad bin Muadh."
"37957","(37957) Zayd bin Harun told us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Rashid, on the authority of A woman from the Ansar, called: Asma’ bint Zayd bin Sakan. She said: When he came out with the funeral of Saad bin Muadh, his mother cried out. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Umm Saad: Will your tears not stop and your sadness go away? Your son is the first at whom God laughed and for whom the throne shook."
"37958","(37958) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Amr informed us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Aisha, She said: We came on Hajj, or Umrah, and we met Dhul-Halif, and the servants of the Ansar used to meet their families, so they met Usaid bin Hudair, and they mourned for him with his wife, so he disguised himself and began to cry. I said: May God forgive you, you are the companion of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and you have something to do with the past and the past, and you are crying over a woman. She said: So he uncovered his head. He said: You have told the truth for my life, so that it is certain that I will not cry over anyone after Saad bin Muadh, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: What did he say? I said: What did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say to him? He said: The throne shook with the death of Saad bin Muadh. She said: He is walking between me and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he greeted you."
"37959","(37959) Dhudha bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him. He said: The throne was shaken by the death of Saad bin Muadh."
"37960","(37960) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of a man who narrated to him, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said When Saad bin Muadh died, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The throne shook for the spirit of Saad bin Muadh."
"37961","(37961) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: Sa'd's best man was injured on the day of the trench. He was shot by a man called Ibn al-Irqi. She said: So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saved him. And he made the salutation to the mosque, and he set up a tent for him so that he could return soon. (Bukhari 4631, Muslim 66)"
"37962","(37962) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha; In his saying: {When it came to you from above you and from below you, and when the eyes became deviated, and the hearts reached the throats} She said: That was the day of the ditch.\n(Bukhari 4103 and Muslim 2316)"
"37963","(37963) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, surrounded the polytheists on the Day of the Trench. He said, “It was a difficult day and he did not meet anyone.” Muslims have never been like him. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sitting, and Abu Bakr was sitting with him, and that was a long time ago. The palm trees came out, he said: And they were very happy with it when they saw it, because their life was in it, he said, so Abu Bakr raised He raised his head and saw his appearance, and it was the first appearance he had seen. He said: Then he said thus with his hand: Your appearance, O Messenger of God, from Joy, he said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, looked at him and smiled, and said: Oh God, do not take away from us the good things You have given us. Or a righteous thing You have given us."
"37964","(37964) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Shurahbil, he said: When Saad was injured Ibn Muadh with the shooting on the day of the ditch, and his blood flowed on the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so Abu Bakr came. Then he began to say: By the end of his appearance, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O Abu Bakr, then Omar came and said: I To God we belong, and to Him we shall return."
"37965","(37965) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, he said: It was in The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a man called Masoud, and he was a gossip. When it was the day of the ditch, he sent The people of Qurayzah to Abu Sufyan: To send to us men who will be in our lands, so that we may fight Muhammad from among those who will come to him. Medina, and you fight from those who are near the trench. This was difficult for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to fight those who Two faces, and he said to Masoud: O Masoud, we have sent a message to the Banu Qurayz: that they send to Abu Sufyan. So he sent men to them, and when they came to them, they killed them. He said: Not unless he heard that from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: He did not hesitate until he came to Abu Sufyan and told him, and he said: Muhammad has told the truth, by God, he never lied, so he was not sent. To them is anyone."
"37966","(37966) Waki’ bin Al-Jarrah narrated to us, saying: Abdul-Wahid bin Ayman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, stayed while his companions were digging the trench for three days. They did not taste any food, so they said: O Messenger. God, here is a piece of the mountain, meaning a piece of the mountain, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: They bribed They poured water on her, and they sprinkled water on her, then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and took the pickaxe, or the mop, and then said: In the name of God, then he struck three times and it became a hill. Jabir said: Then I turned around and saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said hello, and he had drawn a stone over his stomach. (Bukhari 4101. Darmi 42)"
"37967","(37967) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. On the day of the ditch, he moved the dirt until the hair of his chest was covered with dirt, and he shook with the sting of Abdullah bin Rawah, saying:\nOh God, if it were not for you, we would not have been guided.\nThen they sent down peace upon us.\nIndeed, the Initiates have transgressed against us\nWe did not give alms or pray\nAnd keep your feet firm when we meet\nAnd if they want to tempt us, we refuse."
"37968","(37968) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out in the morning. Cold, while the Muhajireen and Ansar were digging the trench, so when he looked at them, he said:\nThe life of the hereafter is the life of the hereafter\nSo forgive the Ansar and the Muhajirs.\nThey answered him:\nWe are the ones who pledged allegiance to Muhammad\nOn jihad as long as we remain"
"37969","(37969) Zayd ibn Harun told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, on the authority of Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Saeed Al-Khudri, on the authority of his father, said: We were imprisoned on the day of the ditch for noon, afternoon, sunset, and evening prayers. Until that was sufficient for us, and that is the saying of God: {And God is sufficient for the believers from fighting, and God is Strong, Mighty} So the Messenger of God stood up God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered Bilal to stand, then he prayed the noon prayer as he had prayed before, then he stood. He prayed the afternoon prayer as he had prayed before, then he stood and prayed the sunset prayer as he had prayed before. That, then he stood up and prayed the evening prayer as he had prayed it before that, and that was before he descended: {Then if you fear On foot, or riding.}"
"37970","(37970) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Sa’id, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace On the Day of the Trench, he did not pray the noon and afternoon prayers until the sun had set."
"37971","(37971) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, he said: Al-Harith bin Awf came and appointed him bin Hisn. So they said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace in the year of the ditch: We will spare you two ghats, on the condition that you give us the fruits of Medina. He said: So they negotiated with him until the matter was settled over half the fruits of the city, so they said: Write a letter between us and you, so he called for a document. He said: And the two monkeys. Saad bin Muadh and Saad bin Ubadah were sitting, so they approached the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Is there something that has come to you about By God, is it not for us to turn away from Him? He said: No, but I wanted to turn their faces away from Him, and let His face be empty. To them, he said: They said to him: The Arabs did not get anything from us in our era except a human being, or a village. \n(Bukhari 2931, Muslim 436)"
"37972","(37972) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Hisham bin Hassan told us, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ali; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on the Day of the Trench: They detained us from the middle prayer, the afternoon prayer. May God make their homes and graves a fire."
"37973","(37973) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman and Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, presented me with the day of the ditch when I was fifteen years old, so he granted me permission. However, Ibn Idris said: I was offered."
"37974","(37974) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on the Day of the Trench: Who is a man who will go and bring us news of the children of Qurayz? So Al-Zubayr rode and came to him with their news, then he returned and said three times: Who will bring me their news? Al-Zubair said: Yes, he said: And the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, gathered his parents to Al-Zubair, and said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you. He said to Zubair: Every prophet has a disciple, and my disciple is Zubair and the son of my cousin."
"37975","(37975) Dhudha bin Khalifa told us, he said: Awf told us, on the authority of Maimun, he said: Al-Bara’ bin Aazib told us, he said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered us to dig a trench, a rock was shown to us in a part of the mountain. It was very large, and shovels could not be inserted into it. So we complained about that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he came. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he saw her, he took the pickaxe, threw down his garment, and said: In the name of God, then he struck. He broke a third of it, and said: God is Great, I have been given the keys to Syria, and by God, I can see its red palaces at the hour. Then he struck. The second: He cut another third and said: God is Great. I have been given the keys of Persia. By God, I can see the White Palace of Medina. Then The third struck and said: In the name of God, so he cut the rest of the stone and said: God is great, I have been given the keys to Yemen, and by God I am To see the gates of Sanaa. (Ahmad 303. Abu Ali 1681)"
"37976","(37976) Hushaym told us, he said: Abu Al-Zubayr informed us, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah; The polytheists occupied the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of the ditch with four prayers, until some of the night had passed. God willing, so he commanded Bilal, so he called the call to prayer and performed the noon prayer, then he stood and prayed the afternoon prayer, then he stood up and prayed the sunset prayer, then he stood and prayed the sunset prayer. Dinner"
"37977","(37977) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ikrimah; Safiyya was with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of the ditch."
"37978","(37978) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Karim, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: When it was the day of the ditch A man from the polytheists got up and said: Who will duel? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Get up, Zubayr. Safiyyah said: O Messenger of God, one of you. So he said: Get up. O Zubair, so Zubair stood up, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Which one of them exalted his companion killed him, so Zubair exalted him. So he killed him, then brought his loot, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, let him go."
"37979","(37979) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Ali bin Hakim, Al-Zubayr bin Al-Kharit, and Ayyub Al-Sakhtiyaani, all of them, on the authority of Ikrimah; Nawfal, or Ibn Nawfal, lost his horse on the day of the ditch and was killed, so Abu Sufyan was sent to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, may God bless him and grant him peace, sacrificed a hundred camels, but the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, refused and said: Take him, for he is evil. Bloodworm, evil carrion."
"37980","(37980) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ikrimah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent Khwat bin Jubair to Banu Qurayz on a horse called Jinnah. (Bukhari 4117, Muslim 1389)"
"37981","(37981) Abdullah bin Numir and Abdou told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned on the day of the trench, put down his weapon and washed himself, Gabriel came to him, and he was tied. His head was filled with dust, and he said: Did you put down the weapon? By God, I did not put it down. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Where? He said: Here, and he gestured to Banu Qurayz. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out to them."
"37982","(37982) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: On the day Qurayz: War is a deception."
"37983","(37983) Zayd bin Harun told us, Hisham told us, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: Ayed Huyy bin Akhtab addressed the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that he should not be attacked by anyone, and God made him a guarantor. He said: When it was the Day of the Quran, He and his son were brought safely. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: I will pay the guarantor’s debt. So he ordered that it be done, and she was struck. His neck, and the neck of his son."
"37984","(37984) Abdullah bin Suleiman told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Abdullah bin Urwa, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubair, on the authority of Al-Zubair, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gathered his parents for me on the day of Qurayz, and said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you."
"37985","(37985) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Umamah bin Sahl, he heard him say: I heard Abu Sa`id al-Khudri saying: The people of Qurayz descended upon the rule of Sa`d bin Muadh. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Then he came to him on a donkey. He said: When he approached the mosque, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Go to your master, or the best of you. Then he said: These people came down to judge you. He said: You shall be killed. Fighting them, and taking their descendants captive. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: You have decided according to the king’s ruling, and perhaps He said: You have decided by the judgment of God. (Bukhari 4121, Muslim 1388)"
"37986","(37986) Abdou bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, he said: My father told me; They came down to the ruling of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they returned the ruling to Saad bin Muadh, so Saad bin Muadh ruled over them. Muadh: That the woman who fights them is killed, and the women and children are taken captive, and their property is divided. Hisham said: My father said: So I was informed, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: You have judged them according to the judgment of God."
"37987","(37987) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Aamir, who said: The people of Qurayzad threw stones. Saad bin Muadh, so they injured his ankle, and he said: Oh God, do not let me die until you cure me of them. He said: So they came down to Saad’s ruling. Ibn Muadh, so it was decided that those who fight them should be killed and their descendants taken captive. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: With the ruling God is your wisdom"
"37988","(37988) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Ibn Abi Awfay, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed On the factions, he said: O God, who sent down the Book, who is quick to judge, who defeated the factions, defeat them and shake them."
"37989","(37989) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, he said: Zaid ibn al-Asam narrated to us, he said: When God revealed the parties, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned to his house and began washing his head. Gabriel came to him and said: May God forgive him. About you, did you lay down the weapon but your angels in the heavens did not lay down it? Come to the fortress of Banu Qurayz. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called out to the people: Come to the fortress of Banu Qurayz. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, washed himself and came to them at the fort. (Ibn Saad 75)"
"37990","(37990) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I wrote to Nafi’ asking him about the supplications of the polytheists. So he wrote to me: Abdullah bin Omar informed me; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, attacked the Banu al-Mustaliq, and they were jealous, and their blessings were watered with water, so it was Juwayriyah bint Al-Harith was among those who struck them, and I was among the horses."
"37991","(37991) Yahya bin Ishaq told us, he said: Yahya bin Ayyub told us, he said: Rabi’ah bin Abi told me. Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hibban, on the authority of Ibn Muhayriz, who said: I and Abu Sarmah al-Mazini entered upon me. Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, so we asked him about isolation? He said: We captured the noble Arabs, we captured the women of Banu Abd al-Mustaliq, so we wanted to be isolated, and we wanted to be ransomed, so some of us said: Do you isolate yourself while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is behind you? So we came to him and said: O Messenger of God, we captured the noblemen of the Arabs, we captured the women of the Banu Mutaliq, so we wanted to be isolated. We wanted to make a ransom, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: You do not have to do it, for it is not written from His name. May God protect her from remaining until the Day of Resurrection except as He exists. (Nasa’i 5045. Malik 95)"
"37992","(37992) Abu Asama told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of his father; The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, were on a campaign against Banu al-Muttaliq when they came to the house, and its people had evacuated. They made them angry, and there were chickens left in the metal, so there was a fight between two young men from the Muhajireen and two young men from the Ansar, so he said Two young men from the Muhajireen said: Oh, the Muhajireen, and two young men from the Ansar said: Oh, the Ansar. This was reported to Abdullah bin Abi Ibn Salul, and he said: By God, if they had not spent on them, they would disperse from around them. By God: (If we return to Al-Madina - They will certainly drive out of it the more honorable and the meaner.) That reached the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he ordered them to leave. It was as if he was keeping them busy, so he met a group of Banu Abd al-Ashhal on the way, and he said to them: Did you not know what he said? The hypocrite Abdullah bin Ubayy? They said: What did he say, O Messenger of God? He said: He said: By God, if you had not spent on them, they would have dispersed from around it. By God, if we returned to Medina they would have expelled them. The more honorable are the more humble. They said: He has spoken the truth, O Messenger of God. You, by God, are the Mighty, and he is the humble."
"37993","(37993) Ghandar told us, on the authority of his people, he said: I heard his leaders speaking, on the authority of Anas; He said in these verses: {Indeed, We have opened for you a clear conquest}, he said: Al-Hudaybiyya. (Bukhari 4834, Muslim 1413)"
"37994","(37994) Abu Asama told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out To Al-Hudaybiyah, and Al-Hudaibiyah was in Shawwal. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out until when He was in Usfan, and a man from Banu Ka’b met him and said: O Messenger of God, we have left Quraysh, and I have gathered for you. Her loved ones were feeding her to the pigs. They wanted to keep you away from the House. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left. Even when he emerged from Usfan, Khalid bin Al-Walid met them as a vanguard of Quraysh, and he met them on the road, and the Messenger said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Come here, so he took between two trees, meaning two trees, and turned away from the path. Until the cloud descended.\n When the clouds descended, he addressed the people, praising God and praising Him as He deserves, then he said:\n As for what follows, the Quraysh have gathered for you their beloved ones to feed them to the sheep, and they want to prevent us from the House. So advise me of what you see? Do you baptize against the head, meaning the people of Mecca, or do you think that you baptize against those who have helped them, so we differ from them in Their women and children, if they sit, they sit in a state of agony, defeated, and if they seek Us, they seek Us in a weak, distracted manner.So God disgraced them?\n Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of God, we think that you should aim at the head, for God is your helper, God is your helper, and God is Your appearance, Al-Miqdad bin Al-Aswad said while he was on his journey: By God, O Messenger of God, we do not say to you as the sons of Israel to its Prophet: {Go, you and your Lord, and fight. Indeed, here we will sit.} But go, you and your Lord, and fight. We are fighters with you.\n Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went out and when he had covered the sanctuary and entered its monuments, his young she-camel blessed him, and they said: She was alone, and he said: By God, she was not alone, and it was not her custom to be alone, but the elephant was keeping her away from Mecca. Do not invite the Quraysh to it. Glorifying the forbidden things, and they will precede me to it. Come here to his companions. So he took the right hand in a second called Dhaat. Al-Hanthal, until he landed on Al-Hudaybiyah, and when he came down, the people vomited from the well, and it bled and did not help them, so they complained. That was his god, so he gave them one of his arrows, and said: Stick it into the well. So they stuck it into the well, and it boiled. And its water was stagnant\n He even hit people with curses.\n When the Quraysh heard about him, they sent to him a brother of Banu Halis, who is from a people who venerate the sacrifice, and he said: Send Hadi, and when he saw Hadi, he did not speak a word to them.Then he left his place and went to the Quraysh and said: O people of the necklaces, the body, and the gift. So he warned them and venerated them. They cursed him and frowned at him, and said: You are a rude Bedouin and we do not admire you, but we admire ourselves when we sent you. Sit down\n Then they said to Urwa bin Masoud: Go to Muhammad, and let us not come from behind you. So Urwah left and came to him, and he said: Oh. Muhammad, I have never seen an Arab man go the way you did. You went with the rabble of people to your family and your family which It separated from you to annihilate its greenery. You know that I have come to you from Ka’b bin Luay and Aamir bin Luay. The skins of tigers are at the shelter of the camps. They swear by God: Do not expose them to any sin unless they expose to you something other than that.\n Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: We did not come to fight, but we wanted to complete our Umrah and sacrifice our sacrifice. So, may you go to your people, for they are the people of Qatab, and the war has frightened them, and there is no good for them if The war will consume all of them except what it has consumed, so they will be alone between me and the House, so we will complete our Umrah and sacrifice our sacrifice. And they will place a stretch of land between me and them, in which we will lodge their wives, and in which their concubines will be safe.And they will be alone between me and the people. By God, I will fight over this matter, the red and the black, until God supports me, or My previous statement is unique. If the people afflict me with me, that is what they want, and if God makes me appear over them, they will choose. Either they fought prepared, or they entered peace fleeing.\n He said: Then Urwah returned to Quraysh and said: You know, by God, there is no people on earth more beloved to me than you. Indeed, you are my brothers. He is the most beloved of the people to me, and I pleaded with the people for you in the gatherings, but when they did not help you, I came to you with my family until I came down. With you, I wanted to console you. By God, I do not like life after you. You know that a man has offered half, so accept it. You know that I have been before kings and seen great men, so I swear by God that I have seen a king, and there is no great man greater than me. His Companions, if a man among them speaks until he asks permission, then if he gives permission, he speaks, and if he does not give permission, he speaks. He was silent, then he was about to perform his ablution, and they hastened to perform his ablution and poured it on their heads, treating it as tenderness.\n When they heard his words, they sent Suhail bin Amr and Mikraz bin Hafs to him, and said: Go to Muhammad, and if he gives you 'Urwah did not mention it, so he judged him to return this year from us.He does not return to the House until he hears from the Arabs who hears about his journey. We have repelled him, so Suhail and Mikraz went out and came to him and mentioned that to him, so he gave them what they asked for, and he said: Write: In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. They said: By God, we will never write this. He said: So how? They said: We write in your name, O God. He said: And this, so write it. So they wrote it, then he said:\n Write: This is what Muhammad, the Messenger of God, has decreed. They said: By God, we only disagree about this. He said: What should I write? They said: He was affiliated, so write Muhammad bin Abdullah. He said: This is good, write it down, so they wrote it down.\n And it was in their condition, that between us is the blind defect, and that there is no shackles, nor slander.\n Abu Asama said: Shackles are shields, and shackles are swords, and what he means by blind cloak is that its companions suffice for them. About them\n And whoever of us comes to you, you will return him to us, and whoever of you comes to us, we will not return him to you. So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: And whoever enters with me will have a police like ours. The Quraysh said: Whoever enters with us is one of us. He will have a police like ours. So they said Banu Kaab: We are with you, O Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Banu Bakr said: We are with Quraysh.While they were in the book, Abu Jandal came, paving the chains, and the Muslims said: This is Abu Jandal, so he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It is for me, and Suhail said: It is for me, and Suhail said: Read the book, and behold, it is To Suhayl, Abu Jandal said: O Messenger of God, O community of Muslims, shall I be returned to the polytheists? So Omar said: O Abu Jandal, this sword, it is only a man and a man, so Suhail said: You have been helpful to me, O Omar, so the Messenger of God said God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to Sahil: He gave it to me. He said: No. He said: So reward him for me. He said: No. Mukarz said: It may. I granted it to you, O Muhammad, but he did not perform the Hajj. (Bukhari 2731 and Abu Dawud 2759)"
"37995","(37995) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Marwan; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, set out in the year of his battle, and when he reached Al-Hudaybiyah, he was confused about the solution, and he was He prayed in the Sacred Mosque, and when they wrote down the matter and finished it, a great matter occurred to the people. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: O people, sacrifice, shave, and proclaim law. Not a single man among the people rose up. Then he repeated it, and not a single one of the people rose up. The people, so he entered upon Umm Salamah and said: Did you not see that he entered upon the people? She said: O Messenger of God, go and slaughter your animal, shave, and permissible, for the people will permissible. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, slaughtered it. May God bless him and grant him peace, and make it permissible. (Ahmed 323)"
"37996","(37996) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Zakariya, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was besieged May God’s peace and blessings be upon him from the House. He made an agreement with the people of Mecca that he would enter it, so he would stay there three times, and he would not enter it except Bringing weapons: the sword and its holsters, and he does not take any of its people out with it, and he does not prevent any of its people from staying there. He was with him, so he said to Ali: Write down the condition between us: In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. This is what Muhammad, the Messenger of God, has decided upon. Then the polytheists said: If we knew that you are the Messenger of God, we would follow you, but write: Muhammad bin Abdullah. He said: So he ordered Ali to He erased it, and Ali said: No, by God, I will not erase it, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Show me its place. So he showed him where it was, erased it, and wrote: Ibn Abdullah. So he stayed there for three days, and when it was the third day, They said to Ali: This is the last day of your companion’s condition, so he ordered him to go out, so he told him about that, and he said: Yes, so he went out. (Bukhari 2698, Muslim 1410)"
"37997","(37997) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Zakariya, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: We descended on the day of Al-Hudaybiyah. We found its water that the first people had drunk, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sat at the well, then called for a bucket of it. So he took some of it with his mouth, then poured into it and prayed to God, and its water increased until the people drank from it."
"37998","(37998) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out He performed Umrah in Dhul-Qa’dah, with the Muhajirs and Ansar, until he came to Al-Hudaybiyah, and a group of Quraysh came out to him and returned him. About the House, until there was talk and dispute between them, until there was almost a fight between them, he said: So he pledged allegiance to the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, his companions and their number were one thousand and five hundred under the tree, and that was the day of the sale of Al-Ridwan. So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sued them, and the Quraysh said: We will sue you on the condition that you slaughter the sacrificial animal in its place, and that you shave and return. Until next year, we will vacate Mecca for you for three days. So he did so.\n He said: So they went out to Ukaz, where they stayed there for three days, and they stipulated that he should not enter it with any weapon except the sword, nor You go out with one of the people of Mecca, if he goes out with you, and he slaughters the sacrificial animal in its place, and flies and returns, until when he is in Qabil, he In those days, he entered Mecca, and brought the body with him, and the people came with him, so he entered the Sacred Mosque, and God revealed to him: {Indeed, Allah, His Messenger, has confirmed the vision with the truth, so that you will enter the Sacred Mosque, if Allah wills, secure.} He said: And Allah revealed to him: {The sacred month for the sacred month, and sacred things are retaliation. So whoever commits aggression against you, commit aggression against him in the same manner as he committed aggression against you.} If they fight you in the Sacred Mosque, then fight them. God has made it lawful for them, if they fight him in the Sacred Mosque, to fight them. In it, Abu Jandal bin Suhail bin Amr came to him, and he was bound. His father bound him, so he returned him to his father."
"37999","(37999) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He presented The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his companions in the truce that existed before the peace that was made between them And among them, he said: And the polytheists were at the gate of prayer next to the stone, and they said that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He and his companions greeted him in earnest and in jest, and when they greeted, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to them: They had spoken that How hard and how weak are you? So they completed three laps until they saw that you had strength. He said: When they received the stone, they raised it. They braked their feet, until some of them said to one another: Did you not claim that they were weak and tired, and that they were not content to walk? Until they strive hard? (Ahmad 356. Tabarani 12077)"
"38000","(38000) Yunus bin Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Mujma’ bin Yaqoub narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, on the authority of his uncle Abd al-Rahman bin Zaid, on the authority of Mujma’ bin Jariyah, said: I witnessed Al-Hudaybiyah with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when we departed When people were drying camels, some of the people said to others: What is the matter with the people? They said: It was revealed to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: So we went out and wandered with the people until we found the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, was standing at the hands of the clouds, and when some of the people gathered to him, he recited to them: (Indeed, We have conquered for you A clear opening) Then one of his companions said: O Messenger of God, did he open it? He said: Yes, by the One in whose hand is my soul, it is an opening. He said: So I divided it among the people of Al-Hudaybiyyah, into eighteen arrows, and the army was one thousand and five hundred, and three hundred knights, so the knight had two arrows."
"38001","(38001) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Musa ibn Ubaidah, on the authority of Iyas ibn Salamah, on the authority of his father, he said: We left With the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the Battle of Al-Hudaybiyah. We slaughtered a hundred people, and we were seventeen hundred. They had with them a number of weapons, men and horses, and there was a camel in his body, so Al-Hudaybiyyah came down and the Quraysh made peace with him on the condition that This guidance is its place where We have confined it. (Ibn Saad 102)"
"38002","(38002) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz bin Siyah narrated to us, saying: Habib bin Abi Thabit narrated to us. On the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Sahil ibn Hanif, he said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, if we saw fighting. He would have fought us, and that was in the reconciliation that was between the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the polytheists, so Omar bin Al-Khattab Then he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, are we not on the right and they are on the wrong? He said: Yes, he said: Weren't those who killed us in Paradise and those who killed them in Hell? He said: Yes, he said: Why should we give up this worldly life and return when God has judged between us and them? He said: O Ibn Al-Khattab, I am the Messenger of God, and God will never let me go. He said: So Omar went off, and was not patient, angry to the point of He came to Abu Bakr and said: O Abu Bakr, are we not on the right and they are on the wrong? He said: Yes, he said: Weren't those who killed us in Paradise and those who killed them in Hell? He said: Yes, he said: Why should we give this worldly life for the sake of our religion, and return when God has judged between us and them? He said: O Ibn Al-Khattab, he is the Messenger of God, and God will never forsake him. He said: Then the Qur’an was revealed to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said with the fatha, so he sent for Omar and he read it to him, and he said: O Messenger of God, did he give the fatha? He said: Yes, and his soul was at ease and he returned. (Bukhari 3182, Muslim 1411)"
"38003","(38003) Affan told us, Hammad bin Salamah said, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas; The Quraysh made peace with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, over Suhail bin Amr, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Perhaps it is written: In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. So Suhail said: As for In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, we do not know what In the Name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. The Most Merciful, but write with what we know: In Your Name, O God. He said: Write from Muhammad, the Messenger of God. They said: If only we knew that you are the Messenger of God. By God, we have followed you, but write your name and the name of your father. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Write: from Muhammad ibn Abd. God, so they made a condition of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that whoever of you comes, we will not return him to you, and whoever of us comes to you You returned it to us, and they said: O Messenger of God, will you write this? He said: Yes, for whoever among us goes to them, God will keep him away, and whoever of them comes to us, God will provide him with relief and a way out. (Bukhari 4154, Muslim 1484)"
"38004","(38004) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, he heard Jabir say: On the day of Al-Hudaybiyyah, we were one thousand and four hundred. Then he said to us: Today you are the best people on earth."
"38005","(38005) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Al-Miswar, and Marwan; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out in the year of Hudaybiyyah with some fifteen hundred of his companions. With Dhul-Halif, he tied the Hadi, put his hair on his hair, and entered the Ihram."
"38006","(38006) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Musa ibn Ubaidah, on the authority of Iyas ibn Salamah, on the authority of his father, he said: I was sent Quraysh: Suhail bin Amr, Huwaytib bin Abd al-Uzza, and Mikraz bin Hafs to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. To reconcile with him, when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw Suhail among them, he said: Suhail has asked of your command, the people. They will come to you with their compassion, and ask you for peace, so send guidance and show the Talbiyah, perhaps that will soften Their hearts, so they responded from the side of the army, until their voices shook with the Talbiyah. He said: So they came to him and asked for peace.\n He said: While the people were bidding farewell, and among the Muslims were some of the polytheists, and among the polytheists were some of the Muslims, so it was said: Abu Sufyan, when the valley was flowing with men and weapons, he said: Iyas said: Salamah said: I brought six of The polytheists, armed with their own weapons, cannot do for themselves any benefit or harm. So We brought them to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He gave peace, did not rob him, did not kill him, and pardoned him. He said: We strengthened what was in the hands of the polytheists among us, so we did not leave them behind. If We saved a man from among us, he said: And We defeated those of them in our power.\n Then the Quraysh went to Suhail bin Amr and Huwaytib bin Abd al-Uzza, and they concluded their peace treaty, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent to May God bless him and grant him peace, and they greeted him, and Ali wrote between them: In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. This is what Muhammad has made peace with. The Messenger of God with the Quraysh, and he made peace with them on the condition that there would be no shackles or shackles, and that whoever of Muhammad’s companions would come to Mecca as a pilgrim, or He is performing Umrah, or he is seeking the bounty of God, so he is safe for his blood and his wealth, and whoever of the Quraysh came to Medina, passing through Egypt. And to the Levant, seeking the bounty of God, and he is safe for his blood and his wealth, and for whoever comes to Muhammad from the Quraysh, he will be rejected. And whoever of Muhammad’s companions comes to them, he is theirs.\n This became difficult for the Muslims, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever of us comes to them, God will keep him away, and whoever We came from them and we returned it to them. God knows Islam from itself and God will make a way out for it.\n They agreed with him that he would perform Umrah a year coming in a month like this, and he would not enter upon us with horses or weapons, except what The traveler carries his sack and stays in it for three nights, and this is the gift where We kept him. It is permissible, he should not present it to us, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: We will drive him away, and you will turn away from him. (Tabari 96)"
"38007","(38007) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Musa ibn Ubaidah, he said: Iyas ibn Salamah narrated to me, on the authority of his father, He said: Quraysh sent Kharij bin Kurz to go out to them, and he returned, praising and doing well. They said to him: Indeed, you are Bedouins, they rattled their weapons for you, and your heart flew, but you did not know what was said to you or what you said. Then they sent Urwa bin Masoud to surprise you. He said: O Muhammad, what is this hadith? You call to the essence of God, then you bring to your people the bastards of people, those you know and those you do not know, to cut off their relatives and make it permissible You deprived them, their blood, and their property, and he said: I did not come to my people except to extend their ties of kinship. May God replace them with a better religion. Of their religion, and a better livelihood than theirs, so he came back praising the two.\n He said: Iyas said, on the authority of his father: Then the calamity became severe for those who were in the hands of the polytheists among the Muslims. He said: So the Messenger of God called May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, Omar, and he said: O Omar, are you reporting on the behalf of your Muslim brothers? He said: No, O Prophet of God, by God, I do not have any clan in Mecca other than me who is more clan than me. So he called Othman. So he sent him to them, and Othman set out on his mount, until the polytheist soldiers came, and they tampered with him and abused him. Then Aban bin Saeed bin Al-Aas, his cousin, helped him and carried him on the saddle and his buttocks. When he came, he said: Cousin, Why do I see you so shy? Asbil, he said: And his lower garment extended to half of his shins, so Othman said to him: This is the lower garment of our friend, so he did not leave anyone alone. Some of the Muslim captives in Makkah will inform them of what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said.\n Salamah said: While we were talking, the herald of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called out: O people, the sale. The Holy Spirit descended and said: We went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was under a Samra tree. So we pledged allegiance to him, and that is the saying of God: {God was indeed pleased with the believers when they pledged allegiance to you under the tree} He said: So he pledged allegiance to you under the tree. Othman had one hand over the other, so the people said: Congratulations to Abu Abdullah, he is circumambulating the Kaaba while we are here. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If he had stayed for such and such a year, he would not have circumambulated until I had circumambulated."
"38008","(38008) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Yahya, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abi Saeed, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on the day of Al-Hudaybiyyah: Do not light a fire at night. Then he said: Light it and create it. For no people after you will overtake your tide or your hardship."
"38009","(38009) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Jabir, who said: People became thirsty on the day of Hudaybiyyah. He said: Then the people rushed to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: He put his hand in the rukoo, and I saw water like The eyes. He said: I said: How old were you? He said: If we were a hundred thousand, it would be enough for us. We were fifteen hundred. (Bukhari 35761 Muslim 1284)"
"38010","(38010) Khaled ibn Mukhlid narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Ansari narrated to us, saying: Ibn Shihab, he said: Urwa bin Al-Zubair told me; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out in the year of Al-Hudaybiyyah in one thousand and eight hundred and was sent with him. A servant of his from Khuza'a, called Najiya, brought news of the people until the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came down. He greeted Ghadeer B'Usfan, who is called Ghadeer Al-Ashtat, and he met him at Ghadeer Al-Ashtat, and said: O Muhammad, I have left Your people; Ka'b ibn Luayyah and Aamir ibn Luyyah have summoned the Ahabish for you, and whoever obeyed them, they have heard of your journey, and you have left Their servants feed the barley in their homes, and this is Khalid bin Al-Walid in the horses of his expedition.\n Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and said: What do you say? What do you command? Advise me, news of Quraysh has come to you twice, and what you have done, and here is Khaled bin Al-Walid with grief, he said to them The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Do you think we should go on our way? Whoever turns us away from the House, we will kill him? Or do you think that we should differ from those who left behind them? If a group of them follows us, God will cut it off. They say: O Messenger of God. The matter is your command, and the opinion is your opinion,So they entrusted themselves with this mount, but neither Khalid nor the horses with him noticed it until he passed the army's flank.\n And his she-camel was brought in full, sitting on the people’s faeces, and it was called Baldah, and she was blessed. He said: Halal, Halal. But he did not. It came out, and they said: The cages were alone. He said: By God, they were not alone, nor did they have any manners, but the one holding the elephant kept them in prison. But, by God, they will not call me today to commit a sin, nor will they venerate a sanctuary therein, nor will they call you therein to a prayer except I responded to them, then he rebuked her and she remained steadfast, so he returned from where he had come, returning to his beginning, until he descended upon the people. Some of the Thumad Al-Hadbiyya was of unknown quantity, with little water, and the people spit out its water, so they complained to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him. The water was scarce, so he pulled out an arrow from his quiver, so he ordered a man to stick it into the heart, and it overflowed with water until People criticized him for insulting him.\n While he was doing that, Budail ibn Warqa’ al-Khuza’i passed by him in a group of his people, from Khuza’i, and he said: Muhammad, these people of yours have gone out seeking refuge with the Mutafils, swearing by God that they will come between you and Mecca so that no One of them remained. He said: O Badeel, I did not come to fight anyone, but rather I came to perform my rituals and go around this land. The house,Otherwise, do the Quraysh have anything other than that? Will they have anything other than that? Until I provide them with a stretch in which they will be safe and take shelter. And they will be alone between me and the people. If a matter becomes apparent to the people, they have the option of entering there. As the people entered it, and they were going to fight, and they had gathered and prepared, Badil said: I will present this to your people.\n So Badil rode until he passed by Quraysh, and they said: From where? He said: I came to you from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and if you wish, I will tell you what I heard from him. I did so, so some people said: Of their fools: Do not tell us anything about it, and some of their teeth and wisdom said: Rather, tell us what you saw? And what did you hear? So he took retaliation against them in an alternative to the story of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and what was presented to them of the range. He said: And among the infidels. Quraysh. At that time, Urwah bin Masoud Al-Thaqafi came and jumped up and said: O people of Quraysh, do you accuse me of anything? Am I not a boy? Aren't you the father? Did I not mobilize for you the people of Ukaz? When they reached out to me, I fled to you with myself, my children, and those who obeyed me. They said: Yes. You have done so. He said: So accept as an alternative whatever he has brought to you and what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, has offered you.And send me until I bring to you what is authenticated from him. They said: Then go.\n 'Urwa went out until he came down to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at Al-Hudaybiyah, and said: O Muhammad, these are your people. ; Ka'b ibn Luayyah and Aamir ibn Luyyah went out with the help of the mutafils, swearing that they would not be alone between you and Mecca. Until you destroy their green lands, but by fighting them you are only between one of two things: to invade your people, and you have never heard of a man Its roots spread before you, and the one I see with you is between you and I see with you nothing but scoundrels from among the people, I do not know. Their names, not their faces.\n Then Abu Bakr said, and became angry: Suck Al-Lat’s clitoris. Shall we abandon him or deliver him? Urwah said: By God, if you had not been able to reward you with it, I would have responded to what you said. And Urwah had tolerated it. He was in need, so Abu Bakr helped him with good help.\n Al-Mughirah bin Shu’ba was standing over the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he had a forgiving face, but he did not recognize him. Urwa, and Urwa used to speak to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and whenever he extended his hand, he touched the beard of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he used the changing gourd with a cup that was in his hand, until when he embarrassed him, he said: Who is this? He said: This is Al-Mughirah bin Shu’ba.Urwah said: You are in that, O treacherous one. Did I wash your treachery except yesterday with Ukaz? The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Urwah bin Masoud the same as he said to Badil.\n Then Urwah got up and went out until he came to his people and said: O people of Quraysh, I have come to the kings, to Caesar. In his kingdom in the Levant, over the Negus in the land of Abyssinia, and over Kisra in Iraq, and by God I have never seen a king like him. He is greater among those who appeared before him than Muhammad among his companions. By God, they do not draw attention to Him, nor do they raise He has the voice, and whenever he performs ablution, they crowd in on him. Whoever of them can achieve any of it, so accept the one. He brought you an alternative; For it is a guided mistake.\n They said: Sit, and they called a man from Banu al-Harith ibn Abd Manaf, called: Al-Halis, so they said: Go, and see what comes before. This man, and what he met you with, so Al-Halis left, and when the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw him coming, he recognized him, and he said: This is Al-Halis, and he is from a people who venerate guidance, so send guidance before him. So they sent guidance in his face. His face, Ibn Shihab said: Then the hadith differed regarding Al-Halis. Some of them said: He came to him and said to him the same as what he said. For an alternative and a loophole,And among them is he who said, when he saw the sacrifice, he returned to Quraysh and said: I have seen a man. If you stop him, I am afraid. You must be afflicted with hardship, so maintain your sight.\n They said: Sit down, and they called a man from Quraysh called: Mikraz bin Hafs bin Al-Ahnaf, from Banu Amir bin Luay. So they sent him, and when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw him, he said: This is an immoral man who looks with an eye, and he told him something like that. He said to Badil and his companions in the meantime, so he came to them and informed them, so they sent Suhail bin Amr from Banu Amir bin Luayy wrote to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the one who called for him. Then Suhail bin Amr came to him and said: He has The Quraysh sent me to write to you about a matter. You and I will be satisfied. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Yes. Write: In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. He said: He said: I do not know God, nor do I know the Most Gracious, but write as we used to write: In your name, O God, and the people found out about that and said:\n We will not write to you about a mistake until you acknowledge the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. Suhail said: Then I will not write about a mistake until I return. He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Write: In your name, O God. This is what Muhammad, the Messenger of God, has decreed. He said: I do not acknowledge.If I had known that you are the Messenger of God, I would not have disobeyed you, nor would I have disobeyed you. Rather, it was written: Muhammad bin Abdullah, and the people found out about it. Also, he said: Write: Muhammad bin Abdullah. Suhail bin Amr.\n Then Omar bin Al-Khattab stood up and said: O Messenger of God, are we not following the truth, and is our enemy not following falsehood? He said: Yes, he said: Why should we give this worldly life in exchange for our religion? He said: I am the Messenger of God, and I will not disobey him, and he will not forsake me. And Abu Bakr was walking away, so Omar came to him and said: O Abu Bakr, and he said: Yes, he said: Are we on the truth, and is not our enemy on falsehood? He said: Yes, he said: Why should we give this worldly life in exchange for our religion? He said: Leave what you see, O Omar, for he is the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and God will not forsake him, nor will He disobeys her.\n And it was a condition of the book that: Whoever is among us comes to you, and if he follows your religion, you will return him to us, and whoever comes to us from Before you, We returned it to you. He said: As for whoever came before me, he has no need for me to return it. As for what you have stipulated for yourself, that is yours. Between you and me.\n While the people were in that state, Abu Jandal bin Suhail bin Amr appeared before them, kicking iron. He was at the bottom of Mecca, unsheathing his sword, and Suhail raised his head, and behold, there he was with his son, Abu Jandal.He said: This is the first person I sued you for his response. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O Suhail. We have not yet annulled the letter. He said: Nor will I write to you about a mistake until you turn it back. He said: What is your business with it? He said: Abu Bashash He went to the people and said: O Muslims, shall I be returned to the polytheists? Are they tempting me in my religion? Omar clung to him while his father was holding his cud in his hand, and Omar said: He is just a man, and you have a sword, so he set off with him. His father\n The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to respond to them who had come before them to enter into their religion. When they gathered, a group Among them was Abu Basir, who returned them to them. They settled on the sea coast, and they cut off the Quraysh’s passage to the Levant. So they sent to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: We see that you are a pity, that you should return them to you and gather them together, so he sent them back. God\n And what the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wanted them to do in the book: to invite him to enter Mecca, and perform his rituals. And his guide would be slaughtered between their backs, and they said: Do not tell the Arabs that you took us by force, but come back. This year of yours, then, if he accepts your permission, then you perform Umrah and perform the night prayers three times.\n And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up.So he said to the people: Arise and sacrifice your sacrifices, and shave and be free. Not a single man rose or moved, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded Peace be upon him and greeted the people three times, but no man moved or rose from his seat. When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw When he greeted him, he entered upon Umm Salama, and he had gone out with her on that campaign, and he said: O Umm Salama, what is the matter with the people? I commanded them. There are three conditions: to sacrifice, to shave, and to make lawful. No man has done what I commanded him to do? She said: O Messenger of God, come out and do that, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and guided him. So he slaughtered him, called a barber and shaved him, and when the people saw what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had done, they jumped to his guidance. So they pushed him, and some of them jumped on each other's throats, to the point that some of them almost fainted due to the crowding.\n Ibn Shihab said: The gift that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his companions brought was seventy bodies.\n Ibn Shihab said: Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, divided the news among the people of Al-Hudaybiyah into eighteen parts. An arrow, for every hundred men an arrow."
"38011","(38011) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Ata’, who said: It was the home of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Day of Hudaybiyyah in the Sanctuary."
"38012","(38012) Al-Fadl narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: We were a thousand on the day of Al-Hudaybiyyah. And four hundred"
"38013","(38013) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, he said: Musa ibn Ubaidah informed us, he said: Abu Muriya, the servant of a mother, informed me. Hani’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: When the Hadith was below the mountains overlooking Wadi Al-Thaniyah, the polytheists presented to it. They turned the faces of his body away, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, slaughtered himself where they imprisoned him, and he was shaved. Some people followed him and shaved, and others waited. They said: Perhaps we will circumambulate the Kaaba. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Have mercy. May God have mercy on those who shave, it was said: And those who fall short, he said: May God have mercy on those who shave, three."
"38014","(38014) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Al-Dastawai informed us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Ibrahim Al-Ansari, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went on the Day of Hudaybiyyah, he and his companions, except for Uthman and Abu Qatada, and he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: May God have mercy on those who shave their heads. They said: And those who fall short, O Messenger of God? He said: May God have mercy on those who shave. They said: And those who cut their hair, O Messenger of God? He said: May God have mercy on those who shave. They said: And those who cut their hair, O Messenger of God? He said: And those who fall short."
"38015","(38015) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, saying: Musa ibn Ubaidah informed us, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Aslam, on the authority of Najiya bin Jundub bin Najiya said: When we were in the clouds, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, received news of the Quraysh. She sent Khaled ibn al-Walid to a horse camp to meet the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Messenger of God thought God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wanted to meet him, and he was merciful to them, and he said: Is there a man who will turn us away from the path? So I said: I, by my father and my mother, O Messenger of God. He said: I took them on a path that was sad; With it, Fadafid and Uqab, and the earth leveled me until I sent it down on the humpback, and he fled, he said: so he was thrown into it. An arrow, or two arrows of his own, then he spat on it, then he called and said: Then her eyes returned to such an extent that I could say, or We say: If we had wished, we could have drowned our cups. (Tabarani 1727)"
"38016","(38016) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, On the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said on the Day of Hudaybiyah: May God have mercy on those who shave. They said: O Messenger of God, And the negligent? He said: May God have mercy on those who cut their hair three times. They said: And those who cut their hair short, O Messenger of God? He said: And those who were negligent. They said: O Messenger of God, what is the matter with those who shave their heads when compassion has become apparent to them? He said: They did not complain."
"38017","(38017) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Jami’ ibn Shaddad, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Alqamiya, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Masoud said: We came with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from Al-Hudaybiyah, and they mentioned that they had descended Trampling on the ground, meaning by trampling on sand, he said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Who are we to eat? He said: Bilal said: I. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Then we sleep. He said: So they slept until the sun rose. Then some people woke up, among whom was so-and-so and so-and-so, and among them was Omar. He said: So we said: Be prepared, meaning, speak. He said: Then the Prophet woke up. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: Do as you used to do. He said: So we did. He said: Likewise, do to him who falls asleep, or He forgot\n He said: The camel of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, had gone astray, so I looked for her. He said: I found her rope clung to a tree, so I came. To the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he took our breath away. He said: Whenever the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, descended upon him, The revelation made this difficult for him, and we knew that about him. He said: So he stepped aside, standing behind us. He said: So he covered his head. With his garment, and this became difficult for him until we knew that it had been revealed to him, so they came to us and informed us that it had been revealed. Ali: {Indeed, We have opened for you a clear victory}"
"38018","(38018) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Sa’id. Mawla Al-Mahri, that Abu Saeed told him; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to them in a campaign that the Banu Lahyan had invaded: To emerge from all Two men, one man, and the reward is between them. (Muslim 1507. Ahmad 137)"
"38019","(38019) Ja’far bin Aoun told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Ismail Al-Ansari told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Amr, or Omar bin Asid, told me on the authority of Abu Hurairah; The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent ten secret troops, and appointed Asim bin Thabit over them, so they went out Until, when they were offering guidance, they mentioned Lihiyyah from Dhayl, and they were called Banu Layyan, so he sent to them a hundred men. archers, and they found their place of food where they had eaten dates, and they said: This one intended for Yathrib, then they followed in their footsteps, until when... Asim and his companions felt that they had taken refuge in a mountain, and others surrounded them, so they took them down and gave them the covenant, so Asim said: By God, I will not make a covenant with an infidel. Oh God, tell your Prophet about us. And Ibn Duthna Al-Bayadhi revealed to him. (Bukhari 3045, Abu Dawud 2653)"
"38020","(38020) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: We sent the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on his journey to Najd. He said: We received many blessings. He said: Then our companion who was We had a camel before us, then we came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, because of what happened to us, and our arrows were after the fifth. Twelve camels, twelve camels, so each man among us had thirteen camels, including the camel that our companion granted us as a ransom. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not fault our companion for what we held accountable for in our arrows.\n(Abu Dawud 2737. Al-Bayhaqi 312)"
"38021","(38021) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: We sent the Messenger of Allah May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he traveled to Najd, where our stock reached twelve camels, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent us off. May God bless him and grant him peace. (Abu Dawud 2737. Al-Bayhaqi 312)"
"38022","(38022) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hajjaj bin Arta, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Ziyad bin Jariyah, on the authority of Habib bin Muslimah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to give away some of the spoils at the beginning of the quarter, and in I returned it for a third. (Tabarani 3527)"
"38023","(38023) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Harith bin Ayyash bin Abi Rabi’ al-Zarqiy. , on the authority of Suleiman bin Musa, on the authority of Makhoul al-Shami, on the authority of Abu Salam al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Umamah al-Bailili, on the authority of Ubadah ibn The silent one; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed a voluntary prayer at the beginning a quarter, and at the return a third.\n(Tirmidhi 1561 and Ibn Majah 2852)"
"38024","(38024) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sa’id bin Abdul Aziz al-Tanukhi narrated to us, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Ziyad bin Jariyah, On the authority of Habib bin Muslimama, he said: I witnessed the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, performing the voluntary third act. (Ahmad 1594 Hakim 432)"
"38025","(38025) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Yazid bin Jabir, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Ziyad Bin Jariyah, on the authority of Habib Bin Muslimama; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made a third voluntary prayer after the fifth. (Abu Dawud 2742. Ahmed 159)"
"38026","(38026) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Amr, who said: Abu Salamah remembered, and Yahya ibn Abd Al-Rahman, Abd al-Malik ibn al-Mughirah, and the Anfals and I were with them, so they sent to Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab to ask him about Then the Messenger came and said: He refused to tell me something. He said: Then Sa’id sent his servant, and he said: Sa’id is telling you: You have been sent to ask me about the voluntary acts, and there is no voluntary act after the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Tabari 1777, Ibn Hibban 4835)"
"38027","(38027) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: Al-Hajjaj bin told me Abdullah Al-Nasri said: The supererogatory act is a right. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed the supererogatory prayer. (Tabarani 3198, Abu Naim 1953)"
"38028","(38028) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Anas; {Indeed, We have given you a clear victory} He said: Khaybar. (Hakim 459)"
"38029","(38029) Hashim bin Al-Qasim told us, he said: Ikrimah bin Ammar told us, he said: Iyas bin Salamah told me, he said: My father told me, he said: My uncle came out on the day of Khaybar to welcome the Jew, and Marhab said:\nKhaybar has learned that I am welcomed. He who wields weapons is a proven hero.\nWhen wars come, they will break out\n My uncle Amer said:\nKhaybar has learned that I am Amer, wielding weapons, a heroic adventurer.\n So they struck with two different blows, and Marhab’s sword fell on Amir’s shield, so the sword returned to his leg and cut off his ankle, and it was in it. Himself, Salamah said: So I met some of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they said: Amir’s deed was in vain, he killed himself. Salamah said: So I came to the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, crying. I said: O Messenger of God, has Amer’s work been in vain? He said: Who said that? I said: Some of your companions. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever said that lied, but he will have his reward twice:\n When he went out to Khaybar, he started to meet the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and among them was the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He drives passengers and says:\nBy God, had it not been for God, we would not have followed God, nor given alms, nor prayed.\nIndeed, those who have transgressed against us when they wish to tempt our father\nAnd we are of Your grace as long as we do not need it, so stand firm when we meet us.\nAnd they sent down a knife upon us.\n Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Who is this? He said: Amer, O Messenger of God. He said: Your Lord has forgiven you. He said: I have never asked forgiveness of any human being except that he was martyred. So when he heard That is Omar bin Al-Khattab. He said: O Messenger of God, had you not given us the pleasure of Amer, then he rose and was martyred.\n Salamah said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me to Ali, and he said: I will give you the opinion today to a man. He loves God and His Messenger, or God and His Messenger love him. He said: So I brought him, leading him, white-haired. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spat. May God bless him and grant him peace, then he gave him the banner, and he came out welcomingly, brandishing his sword, and said:\nKhaybar has learned that I am welcomed. He who wields weapons is a proven hero.\nWhen wars come, they will break out\n Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, said:\nI am the one whom my mother called me Heidara, like a forest dweller with an unpleasant appearance.\nI will repay them with a Saa’, like the kayl of a sindarah.\n So he cut open the head of Marhab with the sword, and the conquest was at his hand, may God be pleased with him."
"38030","(38030) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, on the authority of Jubayr bin Mutim said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, divided the shares of relatives from Khaybar among the Banu Hashim. And Banu al-Muttalib said: Then I and Uthman ibn Affan walked until we entered upon him, and we said: O Messenger of God, these are Your brothers from Banu Hashim, their grace cannot be denied due to your place in which God has placed you among them. Have you seen our brothers from Banu al-Muttalib: You gave them to us rather than us, but we and they are of the same status in lineage. So he said: They have not separated from us. In pre-Islamic times and Islam."
"38031","(38031) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did not change his prayers until the morning, and he would listen. If he heard an adhan, he would refrain from it, and if not, he would listen. He heard a call to prayer and was jealous. He said, “So he came to Khaybar, and they had left their fortresses and dispersed throughout their land, taking with them their camps.” And their axes and their swords. When they saw it, they said: Muhammad and Al-Khamis. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God is great. Khaybar was destroyed: When we camped in the battlefield of a people, he dispersed in the morning of those who had been warned, and he fought them until God granted victory over him, then he divided the spoils. Then Safiyah fell into the arrow of Dihiyah al-Kalbi.\n Then it was said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: A beautiful slave girl has fallen victim to the arrow of the dog. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, bought it for seven heads, and he sent it to Umm Sulaym to repair it. He said: No. I know, except that he said: And she will observe the waiting period with her. Then when he wanted to specify the specifics, the people said: We do not know whether he took her as a concubine, or married her? Then when he mounted her cover and put it behind him, they moved forward until, when they approached the city, they were humbled, and so they were. What they would do when they returned and approached Medina, and the camel of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stumbled and fell, and she fell, and women The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw them looking around and said: God has removed the Jew and crushed her, so she will see her. And they carried her.\n(Bukhari 947. Abu Dawud 2990)"
"38032","(38032) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Amr bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Talha, he said: I was the buttocks of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Khaybar. When we finished and they had come out with wiped cloths, when they saw us, they said: Muhammad and God, Muhammad and Thursday, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God is the Greatest. When we descend upon the battlefield of a people Good morning to those who are warned. (Ahmad 29. Tabarani 4703)"
"38033","(38033) Zaid bin Harun told us, saying: Dawud bin Abi Hind told us, on the authority of Amer; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, told Akri about the two parts, then he sent Ibn Rawahih to Al-Qasmi, so he gave them a choice."
"38034","(38034) Dhudha bin Khalifa narrated to us, saying: Awf narrated to us, on the authority of Maymun Abi Abdullah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraida Al-Aslami, on the authority of his father, said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, descended in the presence of Khaybar, the people of Khaybar, and they said: Muhammad came to visit the people of Yathrib. He said: So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent Omar bin Al-Khattab with the people. So he met the people of Khaybar, and they brought him back and uncovered him and his companions, so they returned to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he responded. His companions, and his companions make him obligatory. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I will give you the banner tomorrow a man who loves God and His Messenger, and God and His Messenger love him.\n He said: The next day, Abu Bakr and Omar confiscated it for her. He said: So he called Ali, and he was turning gray that day, so he spit on his eyes. And he gave him the banners, he said: So he set off with the people, he said: He met the people of Khaybar and met the Khaybari welcoming him, and lo and behold, he was shaking And he says:\nKhaybar has learned that I am welcome\nWhen the lions approached, blazing\nHe who wields weapons is a proven hero\nSometimes I stab and sometimes I hit\n He said: Then he and Ali met, and he struck him on the forehead with the sword. The sword bit the molars on it, and he heard a sound I struck the people of the army. He said: The last of the people had not finished until an victory was opened for the first of them. (Nasa’i 8403. Ahmad 358)"
"38035","(38035) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Sa’id ibn Abi Aroub narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abi Nadrah, on the authority of my father Saeed, he said: We went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from Mecca to Khaybar in the twelve remaining days of Ramadan. A group of the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fasted and others broke their fast. This did not matter."
"38036","(38036) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Al-Hikam; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, swore an oath to Ja’far and his companions on the Day of Khabar, but they did not witness the event."
"38037","(38037) Shazan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Omar said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Tomorrow I will hand over the banners to a man who loves God and His Messenger, and God will win the victory through them. Omar said: I did not wish for the woman except that day, but when the next day came, I argued for her, he said: So he said: O Ali, get up, go and fight. And do not turn around until God grants victory to you. When he stood up, he hated to turn around, so he said: O Messenger of God, why should I fight them? He said: Until they say: There is no god but Allah, then when they say it, their blood and their property are sanctified except in accordance with their rights. (Muslim 1871, Ahmad 384)"
"38038","(38038) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Manhal, Al-Hakam, and Isa, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of his father, said: Ali said: Were you not with us, O Aba Layla, in Khaybar? I said: Yes, by God, I was with you. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent Abu Bakr and he went with the people. So he was defeated until he returned to him, and he sent Omar, and he was defeated by the people until he returned to him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: And peace be upon him: I will give you the opinion of a man who loves God and His Messenger, and God and His Messenger love him. May God grant victory to him. By fleeing, he said: So he sent for me and summoned me, so I came to him while I was blind and could not see anything, so he handed the vision to me, and I said: O Messenger God, how is it that I am blind and cannot see anything? He said: He spit in my eyes, then he said: Oh God, protect him from heat and cold. He said: Neither heat nor cold has harmed me yet."
"38039","(38039) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abu Marzouq, the client of Tajib, said: We invaded with Ruwaifi bin Thabit Al-Ansari towards the West, so we conquered Qurayyat. It is said He did not try it, he said: Then he stood up to give us a preacher and said: I do not say anything about you except what I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said about us on the Day of Khaybar: Whoever believes in God and the Last Day should not irrigate anyone else’s crops with his water, nor He sells spoils until they are divided, and he does not ride an animal from among the Muslims. If he gives it back, he will return it, and he does not He wears a garment of some kind, and even when he takes it off, he puts it back in it."
"38040","(38040) Hashim bin Al-Qasim narrated to us, saying: Ikrimah bin Ammar narrated to us, saying: Samak Al-Hanafi Abu Zumail narrated to me, He said: Abdullah bin Abbas told me, he said: Omar bin Al-Khattab told me, he said: On the Day of Khaybar, a group of the companions of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, they said: So-and-so is a martyr, so-and-so is a martyr, until they passed by a man, and they said: So-and-so is a witness. Shahid, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No, I saw him in Hell, in a garment that he had covered, or in He covered his cloak, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Ibn Al-Khattab, go and call out to the people: He will not enter. Paradise except the believers. He said: So I went out and called: No one will enter Paradise except the believers. (Muslim 1071, Ahmad 47)"
"38041","(38041) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Rafi’ ibn Salma al-Ashja’i narrated to us, saying: Hashraj ibn Ziyad narrated to me. Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of his grandmother, his father’s mother; She went on a campaign with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the year of Khaybar, the sixth of Peace be upon him, so he sent to us and said: On whose orders did you leave us? We saw anger in him, so we said: O Messenger of God, we went out with a medicine to treat him with, and to hand arrows to him, and to give him water to the stalks. And we spin hair, with which we help in the cause of God. Then he said to us: “Stand up.” When God granted victory to Khaybar, he swore to us just as he swore For men"
"38042","(38042) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Zayd, he said: Umair, the servant of Abi al-Lahm, narrated to me. He said: I witnessed Khaybar and I were a slave slave. When they conquered it, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave me a sword and said: “Grip this.” And he gave me some of Khurthi’s possessions, but he did not strike any arrow for me."
"38043","(38043) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Burayd bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: We came to The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, after the conquest of Khaybar with three, so he swore an oath for us, and he did not swear to anyone who had not witnessed the conquest other than us."
"38044","(38044) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: When It was on the Day of Khaybar that people slaughtered reds and boiled pots with them. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered Abu Talhah, So he called out: Indeed, Allah and His Messenger have forbidden you from the meat of domestic donkeys, for it is an abomination, so the pots are sufficient."
"38045","(38045) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, on the authority of Abdullah bin Mughaffal, he said: I heard it. He said: A sack of fat was given to me on the Day of Khaybar. He said: So I stuck to it and said: I will not give any of it to anyone. He said: So I turned around and saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, smiling, so I felt ashamed."
"38046","(38046) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Damra Al-Fazari, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Salit, on the authority of his father, Abi Salit, who was Badr, said: The prohibition of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came He, peace and blessings be upon him, refrained from eating donkeys, and pots boiled with them. He said: So He sufficed them on their faces."
"38047","(38047) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, he said: Al-Qasim and Makhul narrated to us, on the authority of Abu In front of him; The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the news of eating a domestic donkey and any wild animal with a fang. And ropes should be stepped on until they are broken, and arrows should be sold until they are divided, and fruits should be sold until their goodness appears, At that time, he cursed the one who was connected and the one who was connected, the one who tattooed and the one who was tattooed, the one who made a mark on her face, and the one who made a mark on her pocket."
"38048","(38048) Hashim bin Al-Qasim narrated to us, saying: Ikrimah bin Ammar narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abi Salamah, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, said: On the Day of Khaybar, people were struck by famine, and they took human donkeys. So they slaughtered it and filled pots with it, and that was reported to the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Jabir said: So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us. May God bless him and grant him peace, so He sufficed us with the pots, and He said: Indeed, God will bring you a provision that is more lawful and delicious than that, so He is sufficient for us. The pots would boil at that time, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the meat of human donkeys and the meat of... Mules, and every fanged wild animal, and every bird with a claw, and forbidden the perching, and the stealthy, and the predatory."
"38049","(38049) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, he said: Nu’aym bin Hakim narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Maryam, on the authority of Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah walked To Khaybar, and when he came to it, he sent Omar and the people with him, to their city or to their palace, and they fought them, but they did not stay. Omar and his companions were defeated, and they became cowardly and they made you cowardly. The Messenger of God was displeased with that, and said: I will send a god to them. A man who loves God and His Messenger, and God and His Messenger love him. He will fight them until God grants victory to him, but he is not fleeing. So the people approached her and stretched out their necks to see themselves, hoping for what he said. He stayed for an hour, then said: How is Ali? They said: It is Armad, and he said: Call him for me. When I came to him, he opened my eyes, then spit in them, then he gave me the banners. So I set out with him in pursuit, fearing that the Messenger of God would narrate something about them, or about me, until I came to them and fought them. So Marhab appeared, trembling, and I appeared to him, trembling just as he trembles, until we met, then God killed him with my own hand, and he was defeated. His friends, so they fortified themselves and closed the door, so we came to the door, and I continued treating him until God opened it. (Hakim 37)"
"38050","(38050) Ali bin Ubaid narrated to us, he said: Abu Munin narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said: The Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Today I will give my opinion to a man whom God and His Messenger love. Then the people became arrogant and said: Where is Ali? They said: His eye complained, so he called him, spit on his palms, and wiped Ali’s eyes with them, then delivered the opinion to him. So God granted him victory that day."
"38051","(38051) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Malik ibn Anas, on the authority of Zayd ibn Aslam, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Omar, He says: Were it not that the last of the people were left with nothing, the Muslims would not have conquered any of the infidels’ villages without dividing it. He brought among them an arrow, as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, swore. He informed of an arrow, but I wanted you to be a slave. You oppress the Muslims, and I hate that the last of the people should be left without anything."
"38052","(38052) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of al-Hakam, on the authority of Muqasim, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Captivity. A man met a woman on the day of the news, so he carried her behind him, and she disputed with him, the one who was standing with his sword, and he killed her, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw her. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Who killed this man? So they informed him, and he forbade killing women."
"38053","(38053) Abdul Rahim told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ka’b bin Malik; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the group who were sent to Ibn Abi al-Haqqiq in Khaybar to kill him. He forbade them from killing women and children."
"38054","(38054) Abu Asama narrated to us, he said: Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Thabit Al-Bunani narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Rabah, he said: Delegations came to Muawiyah and Abu Hurairah was among us, and that was in Ramadan, so some of us did things to one another. Food. He said: Abu Hurairah was one of those who made it for us in abundance, and they invited us to his trip. He said: I said: Should I not make it for our companions? So I invite them to my journey. He said: So I ordered food and it was prepared, and I met Abu Hurairah in the evening, so I said: The invitation is with me. Night, he said: Did you outrun me? He said: I said: Yes, he said: So I called them and they are with me. He said: Abu Hurairah said: Shall I not explain to you a hadith from your hadith? O people of Ansar? He said: Then he mentioned the conquest of Mecca.\n He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, approached and entered Mecca, and he sent Al-Zubair ibn Al-Awwam to visit one of the pilgrimage places. He sent Khaled bin Al-Walid to the other side of the desert, and he sent Abu Ubaidah to Al-Hussar, so they took the middle of the valley. He said: And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in\n A booklet. He said: He called me. He said: O Abu Hurairah. I said: To your father, O Messenger of God. He said: Call me. By the Ansar, and no one will come to me except my Ansar. He said: So I led a circle around them. He said: They came until they surrounded him.He said: The Quraysh attacked their thugs and followers. They said: Let us advance these people. If they have anything to do with us, we will be with them. And if they are afflicted, We will give what we asked.\n Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to the Ansar when they surrounded him: Do you see the thugs of Quraysh and their followers? Then he said with his hands, one over the other: Reap them, then he struck Suleiman with the edge of his right palm on the stomach. Al-Yusra said: “Reap them with a harvest until you come to me at Al-Safa.” He said: “So we went, and none of us wanted to be killed.” None of them killed him, but as for one of them directed something at us, Abu Sufyan said: O Messenger of God, it is permitted. The Khadra’ of Quraysh, no Quraysh after this day. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever closes his door So he is safe, and whoever enters Abu Sufyan’s house is safe. He said: So the people closed their doors.\n He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, approached until he received the stone and circumambulated the Kaaba, and came to an idol next to it. The House they worship, and in His hand is a bow, and He took hold of the bow, and began to strike it in the eye, and He said: {Truth has come and falsehood has vanished. Indeed, falsehood has vanished}\n Even when he finished his tawaf, he came to Al-Safa and ascended to it where he looked at the House.So he raised his hands and started praising God and remembering Him, and supplicating as he wished to supplicate. He said: And the Ansar were under him. He said: You say The Ansar, one to another: As for the man, his desire for his people and his compassion for his clan overtook him.\n He said: Abu Hurairah said: The revelation came, and when the revelation came, it was not hidden from us, for none of the people would raise it. He passed it on to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, until he had finished. When he had decided, the revelation said, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: And he greeted: O community of Ansar, they said: At your command, O Messenger of God. He said: You said: As for the man, his desire overtook him. He was kind and compassionate to his family. They said: We said that, O Messenger of God. He said: What is his name then? No, I am the servant of God and His Messenger. I emigrated to God and to you. My life is your life and my death is your death. He said: So they came to him weeping, saying: By God, O Messenger of God, we did not say what we said except out of anguish toward God and His Messenger. He said: Indeed, Allah and His Messenger will excuse you and give you the truth.\n(Muslim 1405. Abu Dawud 1867)"
"38055","(38055) Zayd bin Harun told us, saying: Muhammad bin Amr told us, on the authority of Abu Salama, and Yahya bin Abd Al-Rahman bin Hatib, they said: There was truce between the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the polytheists. Banu Ka'b and Banu Bakr were fighting in Mecca, so a shout from Banu Ka'b came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said:\nOh God, I call upon Muhammad to swear by our father and his father, the Apostles.\nSo support, may God guide you to a victorious victory, and call upon the servants of God to come to aid.\n Then clouds passed by and thundered, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: This will thunder with the victory of Banu Kaab, then he said To Aisha: Prepare me, and do not tell anyone about that. Then Abu Bakr entered upon her and disapproved of some of her affair, so he said: What is the matter? This, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered me to reward him. He said: To where. She said: To Mecca. He said: By God, the truce between us and them had not yet ended. Abu Bakr came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he mentioned it to him, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: They were the first to betray me. Then he ordered the way to go and I was imprisoned, then he left and left. The Muslims are with him, so the people of Mecca are saddened that no news comes to them.Abu Sufyan said to Hakim bin Hazzam: O Hakim, by God, we have been distressed and distressed, so may you ride what is between us? And between Marwa, perhaps we will receive news, so Budail bin Warqa’ al-Kaabi from Khuza’a said to him: And I am with you. They said: And you, if you wish. He said: So they rode until, when they approached the two groups of Marwa, they turned dark and approached the two groups. Then, behold, the fire broke out. It occupied the entire valley. Abu Sufyan said to Hakim: What are these fires? Badil bin Warqaq said: This is fires. Banu Amr, starved by war. Abu Sufyan said: Your father’s Banu Amr was more humiliated and inferior than them, so he was exposed. The Arrak left them, so the guards of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took them and a group of the Ansar, and Omar bin Al-Khattab was that one. The night was upon the guards, so they brought them to him, and said: We have brought you a group whom we took from the people of Mecca, and Omar said, and he He laughs at them: By God, if you had brought me Abu Sufyan, I would not have added more. They said: By God, we have come to you with Abu Sufyan. He said: Lock him up, so they locked him up until the morning, then he brought it to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and it was said to him: He sold it. He said: I can find no one but that, or worse than him, so he pledged allegiance. Then it was said to Hakim ibn Hizam: I pledge allegiance, so he said: I pledge allegiance to you, but no. Last but standing,He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: As for those before us, you will not fall down unless standing.\n When they turned away, Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of God, Abu Sufyan is a man who loves to listen, meaning honor. So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever enters the house of Abu Sufyan is safe, except for Ibn Khatal, Miqis ibn Subabab al-Laythi, and Abdullah ibn Saad bin Abi Sarh, and the two Qaytans. If you find them clinging to the curtains of the Kaaba, then kill them. He said: When they turned away, Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of God, if you had ordered Abu Sufyan to be detained on the road and give the people permission to leave, then he would catch up with him. Al-Abbas, and he said: Do you have the right to sit down and look? He said: Yes, and that was only so that he could see your weakness and ask them. Then Jaina passed by, and he said: Yes, Abbas, from These? He said: This is a jinn. He said: What do I have to do with my jinn? By God, there was never a war between me and them. Then Muzainah passed by, and he said: Is it Abbas, who are these people? He said: This is decorated. He said: What do I have to do with Muzainah? By God, there has never been war between me and them. Then it passed. Sulaim, and he said: Oh Abbas, who are these people? He said: This is sound. He said: Then groups of Arabs began to pass by.So Aslam and Ghafar passed by him, so he asked about her and Al-Abbas told him.\n Until the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by the last days of the people, the first immigrants and the Ansar, and a mother shining Al-Basr, and he said: Oh Abbas, who are these people? He said: This is the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his companions, among the first immigrants and the Ansar. He said: It has become Your brother’s son is a great king. He said: No, by God, he is not a king, but we are prophets. They were ten thousand, or Twelve thousand.\n He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave the flag to Saad bin Ubadah, and Saad gave it to his son Qays bin Saad, and Abu Sufyan rode, and he preceded the people until he saw them from the other side. The people of Mecca said to him: What is behind you? He said: Behind me is the blood, behind me is what you have never seen before, and behind me is someone the like of whom I have never seen. Whoever enters my house is safe. So the people said: They were storming his house, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and stopped at the prisons at the highest level of Mecca, and he sent Al-Zubair bin The commoners were on horseback at the top of the valley, and he sent Khalid bin Al-Walid on horseback at the bottom of the valley, and the Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: You are the best of God’s land and the most beloved of God’s land to God.By God, if I had not left you, I would not have left. It was not permissible for anyone before me, and it is not permissible for anyone after me. Rather, it was permissible for anyone who was before me. For an hour of the day, and this hour of yours, it is forbidden: one does not support its trees, nor cut its branches, nor gather She went astray, except for one who seeks one. Then a man who was called a sheep said to him, and the people said: Al-Abbas said to him: O Messenger of God, except... Al-Idhkhar, for it is for our homes, our graves, and our graves, or for our graves and our graves.\n As for Ibn Khatal, he was found clinging to the curtains of the Ka’bah and was killed, and as for Muqays ibn Sababa, they found him between Al-Safa. As for Al-Marwah, a group of Banu Ka’b rushed to kill him, and his cousin Namila said: Leave him alone, for by God he will not come near. There was a man among him, but I struck him with this sword until he became cold, but they delayed from him, so he attacked him with his sword and separated him. He was humble, and he hated for anyone to be proud of him.\n Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, circumambulated the Kaaba, then Othman bin Talhah entered and said: O Othman, where is the key? He said: And with his mother, Salaf, son of Saad, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent to her, and she said: No, by Al-Lat. By Al-Uzza, I will never push him towards him. He said: Indeed, a matter has come other than the one we were upon.If you do not do that, my brother and I will be killed. He said: So I pushed him to him. He said: So he went with him until a messenger came to him. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, stumbled and the key fell from him, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, got up and bowed to him. He was wearing his garment, then Othman opened it for him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the Ka’bah and said the takbir in its corners. He put it back and thanked God, then he prayed two rak'ahs between the two pillars, then he went out and stood between the two doors, and Ali said: Then she became angry and asked that the key be given to us, so that the water-bearer and the veil-keeper would be with us. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Where is Othman? Here is what God has given you, so he gave the key to him.\n Then Bilal rose on the back of the Kaaba and called the call to prayer, and Khaled bin Asid said: What is this sound? They said: Bilal bin Rabah. He said: Abdul Abi Bakr al-Habashi? They said: Yes, he said: Where? They said: On the back of the Ka’bah. He said: On the roof of Banu Abi Talha? They said: Yes, he said: What does he say? They said: He says: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. He said: Allah has honored Abu Khaled by saying: He hears this voice, meaning his father, and he was among those who were killed on the Day of Badr among the polytheists.Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to Hunayn, and the scales of Hunayn were gathered for him. They fought, and the companions of Hunayn were defeated. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, God said: {And on the day of Hunayn, when your multitude astonished you, it was of no use to you. Something} Then God sent down His tranquility upon His Messenger and upon the believers, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, descended from His animal, and he said: O God, if You wish, You will not be worshiped after today. The faces looked up. Then he threw pebbles at them that were in His hand, so they turned away, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took the captives and the property, and said to them: If you wish. So ransom, and if you wish, then captivity. They said: Today we will not prefer anything over reckoning. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When I go out, ask me, for I will give you what is mine, and none of the Muslims will be unable to do so. When the Messenger of God went out, May God bless him and grant him peace. They shouted to him, and he said: As for what is mine, I have given it to you. And the Muslims said the same thing except It was appointed by Hisn bin Hudhayfy bin Badr, for he said: As for what is mine, I will not give it to you. He said: You are on your right from That is what he said: She became an old woman with one eye at that time.Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, besieged the people of Taif for a month or so, and Omar bin Al-Khattab said: Yes, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He called me and I entered upon them, so I called them to God. He said: If they fight you, then enter upon them. Urwa and called them to God, but a man from Banu Malik shot him with an arrow and killed him. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: An example of him among his people is that of the companion of Yasin, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Take their livestock and oppress them. May God bless you\n Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned and came back to a palm tree, and the people began to ask him. Anas said: Until they tore off his cloak from his back, and looked like the face of the moon, so he said: Return my cloak to me, I have no father. Are you miserly to me? By God, if what was between them had been camels and sheep, I would have given them to you. So he will give the one who returned them on that day. One hundred upon hundreds of camels, and he gave to the people.\n The Ansar said at that time, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called them and said: Did you say such-and-such? Did I not find you astray, and God guided you through me? They said: Yes, he said: Did I not find you high and God has enriched you through me? They said: Yes,He said: Did I not find you to be enemies, so God united your hearts with me? They said: Yes. He said: If you had wished, you could have said: You have come to us defeated and we have helped you. They said: God and His Messenger have believed. He said: If only. If you wish, you can say: You came to us as a fugitive, and we took you in. They said: Allah and His Messenger have believed. And if you wished, you could have said: You came to us as a family, and we took you in. They said: God and His Messenger have believed. He said: Would you not be content for the people to turn with a sheep and a camel, and for you to turn with the Messenger of God? Your homes? They said: Yes, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The people are a cover, and the Ansar are a symbol.\n He appointed Abbad bin Waqsh, the brother of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, in charge of al-Maqasim. Then a man from Aslam came, naked and with no clothing on, and said: Cover me with a cloak of this cloak. He said: “These are the places of worship of the Muslims, and it is not permissible for me to give you any of them.” Something, and his people said: Cover him with some of it, and if anyone speaks about it, then it is from our portion and our gifts. So he gave him a cloak, and this reached the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: I was not afraid of this for him. I was afraid of you, so he said: O Messenger of God, I did not give it to you, until his people said: If he spoke about it? Someone looked at us and said: May God reward you with good.May God reward you. (Tirmidhi 3925. Ibn Hibban 3708)"
"38056","(38056) Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Sawa’i, on the authority of Ibn Sabit; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave Othman bin Talha the key from behind the garment. (Abdul Razzaq 9073)"
"38057","(38057) Suleiman bin Harb told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: When he said goodbye The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the people of Mecca, and the Khuza’a were allies of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. The pre-Islamic era, and Banu Bakr were allies of Quraysh, so Khuza’a entered into peace with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Banu Bakr entered into a peace treaty with Quraysh, and there was a fight between Khuza’i and Banu Bakr, so Quraysh supplied them with weapons. And food, and they provided shade for them, so Banu Bakr attacked Khuza’a and killed them, so the Quraysh feared that they might They broke the oath and said to Abu Sufyan: Go to Muhammad, fulfill the oath, and make peace between the people.\n So Abu Sufyan set off until he came to Medina, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Abu Sufyan has come to you. He will return satisfied without his need, so he came to Abu Bakr and said: O Abu Bakr, honor the oath and make peace between the people. Or he said: Among your people. He said: The matter is not up to me. The matter is up to God and to His Messenger. He said: And he said to him regarding what he said: Not. From a people who misled a people and supplied them with weapons and food, or they committed transgression. Abu Bakr said: The matter is up to God and to Him. His Messenger\n Then Omar bin Al-Khattab came,So he said to him something similar to what he said to Abu Bakr. He said: Then Omar said to him: Have you decided? Whatever of it was new, God tested it, and whatever of it was tough or tough, God severed it. Abu Sufyan said: What I saw a group of people watching like today, then he came to Fatima and said: O Fatima, do you have a matter in which you can prevail? The women of your people, then he mentioned to her something similar to what he mentioned to Abu Bakr, and she said: The matter is not up to me, the matter is up to God and to Him. His Messenger, then he came to Ali and said to him something similar to what he said to Abu Bakr. Ali said to him: I have never seen a man like today. He went astray. You are the master of the people, so fulfill the oath and reconcile the people. He said: So he struck one of his hands over the other, and said: He has I rewarded people from one another.\n Then he went until he came to Mecca and told them what he had done, and they said: By God, he did not see us like the arrival of a people today. By God, you have not brought us war so that we should beware, nor have you brought us peace so that we should be safe. Return.\n He said: The delegation of Khuza’a came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and told him what the people had done, and called for victory. And he recited a poem about that:\nNo matter, I am seeking Muhammad\nYou were a parent and we were a child\nAnd they broke your confirmed covenant\nShe claimed that I did not invite anyoneAnd they brought to us the fasting of fasting.\nOur father and his father swore\nThe Quraysh broke their promise to you.\nAnd they made a burden for me as a guard\nThey are more humble and less numerous\nWe recite the Qur’an bowing and prostrating\nThen we submitted and did not withdraw our hand\nSo the Messenger of God was supported by a mighty victory.\nAnd send the soldiers of God that will come again\nAmong them, the Messenger of God, they were stripped\nIn a stream like the sea, coming foaming\nIf he looks down, his face will become dusty.\n Hammad said: Some of this poetry is on the authority of Ayyub, some of it is on the authority of Zayd ibn Hazim, and most of it is on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, then he returned. To the hadith of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah.\n He said: Hassan bin Thabit said:\nHe came to me but I did not bear witness to the waters of Mecca.\nMen of the Banu Ka'b whose necks are slit\nSafwan is an oud made of wood.\nThat was the time for war to tighten its bands.\nSo do not be alarmed, O son of a struggling mother.\nShe spoke clearly and had the best hair.\nI wish my poetry could meet with bitterness\nSuhail bin Amr Hubba and its punishment\n He said: So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered them to leave, so they set out, and walked until they camped in Mara. He said: Abu Sufyan came. Until he came down at night and saw the soldiers and the fires, so he said: Who are they? It was said: This is Tamim, she invaded her country and your country was prospered.He said: By God, these people are more than the people of Minna, or he said: like the people of Minna. When he knew that he was the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, And he greeted him. He said: Show me to Al-Abbas. Al-Abbas came and told him the news, and he took it to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was near him, and he said to him: O Abu Sufyan, submit to peace. He said: What should I do with Al-Lat and Al-Uzza?\n Ayoub said: Abu Al-Khalil told me, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, he said: Omar bin Al-Khattab told him, while he was leaving The dome around the neck of the sword: shut it down, but by God, if I had been outside the dome, I would never have said it.\n He said: Abu Sufyan said: Who is this? They said: Omar bin Al-Khattab.\n Then he returned to the hadith of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah.\n So Abu Sufyan converted to Islam, and Al-Abbas took him to his house, and when the morning came, the people revolted to perform his ritual rituals. He said: Then Abu Sufyan said: Sufyan: O Abul-Fadl, what do the people have? Were they ordered to do something? He said: No, but they stood up to pray. He said: So Al-Abbas ordered him to perform ablution, then he took him to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. peace and blessings of God be upon him. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the prayer, he said the takbir, and the people said the takbir, then he bowed, so they bowed, then he said the takbir. So they rose,Abu Sufyan said: I have never seen people obey you like today, gathered from here and here, nor by the noble Persians, nor by the Romans. The one with the horns, more obedient than them.\n Hammad said: Yazid bin Hazim claimed, on the authority of Ikrimah; That Abu Sufyan said: O Abu Al-Fadl, your brother’s son has risen in the morning, and God is a great king. He said: Then Al-Abbas said to him: It is He is not king, but we are prophecy. He said: Or that, or that.\n Then he returned to the hadith of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah.\n He said: Abu Sufyan said: In the morning, Quraysh said: Then Al-Abbas said: O Messenger of God, if you had permitted me to come to them, So you called them, and you secured them, and you made something for Abu Sufyan by which he would be remembered. So Al-Abbas set off and rode the mule of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, Al-Shiba’a and he set off, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Respond to me, my father.” The man’s paternal uncle is similar to his father. I fear that the Quraysh will do to him what Thaqif did to Urwa bin Masoud. He called them to By God, they killed him, but by God, if they had ridden from it, it would have ignited a fire upon them.\n So Al-Abbas set off until he came to Mecca, and said: O people of Mecca, submit to Islam and you will be safe. You have become accustomed to the likes of a disgraceful person.The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had sent Al-Zubair from the highest place in Mecca, and he sent Khalid bin Al-Walid from before him. At the bottom of Mecca, Abbas said to them: This Zubair is from the highest part of Mecca, and this Khalid is from the lowest part of Mecca. And Khaled, what is Khaled? And Khuza’a with wrinkled noses, then he said: Whoever lays down his weapon is safe. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came forward So they clashed over something of nobility.\n Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, appeared over them and made the people safe, except for Khuza’a from Banu Bakr, so he mentioned four : Miqis bin Sabab, Abdullah bin Abi Sarh, Ibn Khatal, and Sara, your servant Banu Hashim. Hammad said: Sara, in The hadith of Ayyub, and in another hadith: He said: So Khuza’a killed them until midday, and God revealed: “Will you not fight a people? They have broken their oaths and are planning to expel the Messenger, even though they did so the first time. Do you fear them, for God has more right to Fear them, if you are believers. Fight them. God will punish them at your own hands and disgrace them, and grant you victory over them. “And He will heal the breasts of a believing people,” he said: Khuzae’a, “and He will remove the anger of their hearts.” He said: Khuzae’ah, “and God will forgive those who He wills. He said: Khuza’a."
"38058","(38058) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria bin Abi Zaydah, who said: I was with Abi Ishaq while... Between Mecca and Medina, a man from Khuza'ah walked with us, and Abu Ishaq said to him: How is it? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Have these clouds thundered with the victory of Banu Ka’b? Al-Khuza’i said: I arrived at the victory of Banu Ka’b, and then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, brought out to us a message. Khuza’a, and I wrote it down at that time. It said: In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, from Muhammad, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, and peace be upon him, and the secrets of Banu Amr. Indeed, I praise God to you, there is no god but Him. After that: I have not sinned against you, nor have I committed a sin against you, and the people of Tayhama are more honorable than me. And the closest to him in compassion, and whoever follows you is of the righteous, and indeed I have taken for those of you who emigrated what I have taken for myself. And if he migrates to its land other than a resident of Mecca, except as a pilgrim or a pilgrim, and indeed, I have not put anything among you if you submit, and you are Do not be afraid of me, nor besieged.\n As for what comes next, Alqamah bin Ulathah and Ibn Dhudha converted to Islam and pledged allegiance and emigrated to those who followed them. Ikrimah, and he took for those who followed him the same as what he took for himself, and some of us are in charge of others in what is permissible and what is forbidden, and indeed, by God, we do not I lied to you, and may your Lord revive you.\n He said: And he informed me on the authority of Al-Zuhri. He said: These are Khuza'ah, and they are from his family. He said: So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote to them. Peace and blessings of God be upon him. On that day, they were camping between Arafat and Mecca, and they did not submit to Islam as God had written to them, and they were Allies of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"38059","(38059) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Husayn al-Mu’allim narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Find it; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on the day of the conquest of Mecca: Hold back weapons, except for Khuza’a on behalf of Banu Bakr, so he gave permission. He continued with them until they had prayed the afternoon prayer, then he said to them: Stop weapons. The next day, a man from Khuza’a met a man from Banu Bakr and killed him. In Muzdalifah, this reached the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he stood up to deliver a sermon and said: The most enemy of people before God is he who kills In the Sacred Mosque, and whoever kills someone other than his killer, and whoever kills in the pre-Islamic era. (Ahmed 207)"
"38060","(38060) Shababah bin Siwar narrated to us, saying: Al-Mughirah bin Muslim narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, who said: We entered Mecca with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and in and around the House were three hundred and sixty-three idols being worshiped. Instead of God, he said: So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered her to do so, and all of her faces were lowered, then he said: {The truth has come And falsehood has perished. Indeed, falsehood has perished. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the house and prayed therein. He prayed two rak'ahs, and he saw in it the statue of Abraham, Ishmael, and Isaac, and they had made sticks in Abraham's hand. He swore by it. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: May God kill them. Abraham did not swear by the arrows. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called for saffron and smeared it with those statues."
"38061","(38061) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Muammar, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered Mecca, and around the Kaaba were three hundred and sixty idols, and he began stabbing them with a stick. It was in His hand, and He says: {Truth has come and falsehood has annihilated. Indeed, falsehood was annihilating} {Truth has come, and what does falsehood begin and what He will celebrate. (Bukhari 2478, Muslim 1408)"
"38062","(38062) Shababi bin Siwar narrated to us, saying: Nu’aym bin Hakim narrated to us, saying: Abu Maryam narrated to me, on the authority of Ali, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, set off with me until he came to the Ka’bah and said: Sit. So I sat next to the Ka’bah. And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, climbed on my shoulders, then said to me: Get up with me, so I got up with him, and when he saw my weakness Under him, he said: Sit, so I sat down, and he came down to me, and sat down for me, and said: O Ali, climb on my shoulders, so I climbed on him. On my shoulders, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose up with me, and when he rose up with me, it seemed to me that if I wanted, I would attain success. Heaven, so I ascended to the Kaaba, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stepped aside and said to me: Throw down their greatest idol, an idol. Quraysh, and it was made of copper, and it was attached with iron stakes in the ground, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: He treated him, so I started treating him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Eh, so I continued treating him until I was able From him, and he said: Throw it away, so I threw it away and came down. (Hakim 3661, Ahmad 84)"
"38063","(38063) Suleiman bin Harb narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ikrimah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, arrived on the day of the conquest, and depicted Abraham and Ishmael in the House. He gave them the cup, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: What is Abraham’s and the cup? By God, he never swore by it. Then he ordered a garment to be wet and erased their faces with it."
"38064","(38064) Suleiman bin Harb told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Abu Al-Khalil, on the authority of Mujahid; On the Day of Conquest, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, presented the monuments between the pillar and the Maqam, and made it equal to its faces. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, stood up and delivered a sermon, and said: Indeed, Mecca is forever forbidden until the Day of Resurrection. It was permissible for anyone before me, and it will not be permissible for anyone after me, except that it was permissible for me for an hour of the day, in which its privates will not be missed, nor Its hunting will be hunted down, its trees will not be supported, and its shot will not be picked up unless it is identified. Then Al-Abbas stood up and said: O Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, except Al-Idhkhir, for our prayers, our homes, and our graves. He said: Except Al-Idhkhir, except Al-Idhkhir. (Bukhari 4313)"
"38065","(38065) Shababah bin Siwar narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Mihran, on the authority of Umair. Mawla Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Usama bin Zayd, who said: I entered the Kaaba with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he saw He made pictures of the house, so he commanded me, and I brought him a bucket of water, and he started striking those pictures and saying: God has fought a people who make pictures. What they do not create."
"38066","(38066) Ali bin Musir and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Zakariyya, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Malik bin Barsa’, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on the day of the conquest of Mecca: You will not fight after today until the Day of Resurrection. (Ahmad 412. Tabarani 3335)"
"38067","(38067) Ali bin Musir and Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Zakariyya, on the authority of Ash-Shu`abi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muti’, on the authority of His father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No Qurayshite will ever be killed out of patience after this day."
"38068","(38068) Ahmad bin Mufaddal narrated to us, saying: Asbat bin Nasr narrated to us, saying: Al-Suddi claimed, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Saad, on the authority of His father, he said: On the day of the conquest of Mecca, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made the people safe except four people. And two women, and he said: Kill them even if you find them clinging to the curtains of the Kaaba: Ikrimah bin Abi Jahl and Abd Allah bin Khatal, Muqays bin Sababa, and Abdullah bin Saad bin Abi Sarh.\n As for Abdullah bin Khatal, he caught up with you while he was clinging to the curtains of the Kaaba, so he overtook Sa`id bin Harith and Ammar. Sa`id outran Ammar, and he was the younger of the two men, and he killed him. As for Muqais bin Subababah, people overtook him in the market and killed him.\n As for Ikrimah, he sailed on the sea and a storm struck them, so the owners of the ship said to the people of the ship: Be safe, for Your family is of no use to you here. Then Ikrimah said: By God, if nothing saves me at sea except sincerity. No one else can save me in righteousness. O God, I have a promise to You, if You pardon me from what I am in, that I will come to Muhammad until I put my hand in his hand, and I found in him a generous pardon. He said: Then he came and converted to Islam.\n As for Abdullah bin Saad bin Abi Sarh, he hid with Uthman, when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called the people. To sell it, he brought it and presented it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: O Messenger of God, pledge allegiance to Abdullah. He said: He raised his head and looked at him three times. He refused all of that, so he pledged allegiance to him after the three, then he went to his companions. So he said: Was there not a sensible man among you who would stand up and kill him when he saw me withholding my pledge of allegiance? They said: We do not know, O Messenger of God, what is in your soul. Did you not gesture to us with your eyes? He said: It is not befitting for a prophet to have a traitor in his eyes. (Hakim 54, Abu Ali 753)"
"38069","(38069) Shababah told us, he said: Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered He greeted Mecca in the year of the conquest, with a man’s head on his head. When he entered, he removed it, and it was said to him: O Messenger of God, this is Ibn Khatal. Related to the curtains of the Kaaba, so he said: Kill him."
"38070","(38070) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Uthman; That Abu Barza killed Ibn Khatal while he was clinging to the curtains of the Kaaba."
"38071","(38071) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas; Eighty of the people of Mecca descended on the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from Mount Tan’im at the dawn prayer. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took them in peace, and pardoned them, and the Qur’an was revealed: {And it is He who restrained their hands. on your behalf, and I will give you victory over them in the interior of Mecca after I have given you victory over them. (Muslim 1442, Abu Dawud 2681)"
"38072","(38072) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Umm Hani’ said: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, came May God bless him and grant him peace, and he has four glands, which means braids."
"38073","(38073) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered Mecca wearing a black turban."
"38074","(38074) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, saying: Musa ibn Ubaidah informed us, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar. (H) On the authority of his brother Abdullah bin Ubaidah; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered Mecca when he entered it, and he was shrouded in two pieces of black cloth. Its riding mount is in its hand, and in its hand is a shrine with which it holds the pillars. He said: Ibn Umar said: We did not find it in any climate. The mosque, until he descended on the hands of the men, then he took it out until it collapsed in the valley, then he addressed the people on his feet. So he praised God and praised Him with what His family had, then he said: O people, God has removed from you a cloak. The ignorant and its veneration of its forefathers. There are two types of people: the righteous and pious, honorable to God, and the wretched disbeliever, easy on God. O people, God says: {O people, We created you from a male and a female, and made you into peoples and tribes. That you may come to know each other. Indeed, the most honorable of you in the sight of God is the most pious of you. Indeed, God is All-Knowing, All-Aware. I say this and I ask God’s forgiveness for me and for you.\n He said: Then he went to the side of the mosque, and a bucket of Zamzam water was brought to him, and he washed his face with it, not a drop of which fell except In the hand of a human being, if it is as much as they felt, he will wipe it, otherwise he wipes with it, and the polytheists look on, and they say: What We have never seen a king greater than today, nor a people more foolish than today.\n Then he ordered Bilal to kneel on the back of the Kaaba and call to prayer, and the Muslims stood up, stripped themselves of their robes, and took their buckets. And they went to Zamzam to wash the Ka’bah, its back and its belly, but they did not leave a trace of the polytheists except to erase it, or They washed him. (Tirmidhi 3270)"
"38075","(38075) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, saying: Musa ibn Ubaidah informed us, on the authority of Yaqub ibn Zayd ibn Talha. Al-Taymi and Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir said: At that time, there were sixty-three hundred idols on Al-Safa and on Al-Marwa. An idol, and what is between them is surrounded by idols, and the Ka’bah was surrounded by idols. He said: Then Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir said: So he stood up. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had a rod with which he pointed to idols. He was only pointing to something. Then it fell until it came to Isaf and Na'il, and they were in front of the Maqam, facing the Ka'bah Gate. He said: Remove them. So the Muslims met them. He said: Say. They said: What do we say, O Messenger of God? He said: Say: God has fulfilled His promise, and He has given victory to His servant, and He alone has defeated the parties."
"38076","(38076) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya, he said: Abu Salamah informed me that Aba He told him; The Khuza'ah killed a man from Banu Layth in the year of the conquest of Mecca, with one of their own men being killed by them. The Messenger of God was informed of that. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so he rode his camel and delivered a sermon, and said: God has withheld the elephant from being able to move, and His Messenger has given authority over it. And the believers, indeed, it was not permissible for anyone who was before me, and it is not permissible for anyone who was after me, except that it was permissible for me in an hour. Of the day, behold, this hour is forbidden. He does not pluck its thorns, nor support its trees, nor gather Its fallen ones are except one who seeks, and whoever is killed for his sake has the choice of two options: either he will be killed, or his ransom will be made. The family of the dead man.\n He said: Then a man called Abu Shah came and said: Write for me, O Messenger of God. He said: Write for Abu Shah, so a man said: Of the Quraysh: Except for the Idhkhir, O Messenger of God, for we place it in our homes and our graves. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And peace be upon him: Except for Idhikhar."
